{"raw": {"https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41375&lang=en": {"title": "Executive Assistant", "description": "Closing Date: 10/26/2026 Posted Date: Oct 12, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: ADM-CHAN Advancement Denver Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Executive Assistant Working Title: Executive Assistant FTE: Full-time 1.0 (100%) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range : $72,000 - $78,000 Position #00001288 \u2013 Requisition #41375 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . The University of Colorado Denver is a leading public urban research university located in the heart of downtown Denver, where academic excellence, innovation and community partnership come together to expand opportunity and strengthen communities. Within this dynamic institution, the School of Education & Human Development is a statewide and national leader in educational quality, access and equity across the lifespan, from birth through higher education. SEHD prepares equity-minded educators, counselors, researchers and leaders who create meaningful change in schools, families and communities across Colorado and beyond. Through innovative academic programs, impactful research and deep community partnerships, the school advances well-being, opportunity and lifelong learning in diverse urban, rural and global communities. The Director of Development will join SEHD at an important moment of opportunity, building philanthropic partnerships that expand student access, elevate faculty and research, and extend the school\u2019s impact for generations to come. Executive Assistant What you will do: Provide administrative and technical support to the Vice Chancellor for Advancement under the direction of the Strategic Advisor. Coordinate day-to-day activities of the Office of Advancement, handling a broad range of inquiries and assignments. The position possesses project management skills, effective analytical and problem-solving skills, works well under pressure, and can handle complex and concurrent tasks. The position exercises initiative to achieve goals and objectives, maintains confidentiality and establishes and maintains positive working relationships. Key Responsibilities: Provide executive support to the Vice Chancellor of Advancement and members of the Advancement leadership group. Manage Office of Advancement administrative activities/projects. Curates and prioritizes lists of key stakeholders for Chancellor engagement, guiding these lists through multiple layers of internal approval processes to ensure value adds for the Chancellor and campus, and collaborating weekly with the Chancellor\u2019s support staff to schedule and facilitate strategic donor interactions and initiatives. From start to finish, ensure seamless execution of tracking follow-through on action items, preparing detailed briefings and talking points for each interaction, and advising on the structure and content of events and meetings to maximize engagement and alignment with Advancement, Chancellor, and institutional goals. Conduct background & preparation research and compile information for upcoming meetings that include the Vice Chancellor and/or members of the Advancement leadership group. Track and follow up on action items from leadership meetings led by the Vice Chancellor for Advancement and/or by the Strategic Advisor Manage special projects of strategic importance to the Office of Advancement. Manage the Vice Chancellor\u2019s and members of the Advancement leadership group\u2019s calendars, ensuring that engagements are appropriately and sensitively prioritized and managed. Respond in a timely manner to all requests from various sources, both internal and external, for the Vice Chancellor\u2019s time. Coordinate meetings and events that include Vice Chancellor and/or members of the Advancement leadership group. Coordinate departmental agendas, support agenda planning, take notes, and track follow up for meetings that include Vice Chancellor for Advancement. Assist with managing expenses, preparing expense reports, reconciliation, and mileage/travel reports for Vice Chancellor for Advancement under the direction of the Executive Director of Finance & Administration. Provides back-up office presence when needed. Performs all other duties as assigned. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Bachelor\u2019s degree in business, public administration, communications, marketing, social science, or a related field from an accredited institution. 4+ years administrative support experience. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor\u2019s degree on a year-for-year basis. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) At least three (3) years of experience working in a complex university environment with progressive responsibility. Experience with program or project management with ability to effectively lead a team to accomplish critical strategic objectives. Experience with Concur, or similar procurement and travel software, CRM database, & Microsoft Suite. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of, or desire to learn, university policies and procedures, and ability to apply them Strong attention to detail and organizational skills Demonstrate commitment to providing a high level of responsive, thoughtful, and solutions-oriented service to university leadership, colleagues, donors, volunteers, and external partners. Strong communication skills and the ability to work well with a wide audience. Exceptional attention to detail and demonstrate ability to consistently produce accurate, complete work while managing multiple concurrent priorities. Proficiency with communication, word processing, spreadsheet, presentation, and scheduling software (such as Microsoft Outlook, Teams, Word, Excel, Access, PowerPoint, and Adobe Professional). Ability to take dictation. Ability to manage executive email inboxes. Ability to exercise sound judgment, independently prioritize competing and time-sensitive requests, and recognize when an issue requires escalation. Ability to communicate proactively, particularly when priorities change, deadlines may be affected, information is missing or additional clarification is needed. Ability to interact and partner positively with students, faculty, staff, administrators, donors, and visitors. Ability to establish work priorities and adapt to changing needs. Ability to follow through to ensure completion of activities by the deadline established. Ability to communicate effectively with all levels of faculty, administration, staff and students in both a written and verbal capacity. Ability to manage complex, sensitive, and confidential information. Ability to cooperate and support other department staff in order to contribute to a productive work environment. Ability to develop office processes as needed. Ability to work both individually and as a team with the support staff for the Chancellors and other Associate/Vice Chancellors. Other Variables This position will be expected to be in the office four days out of the week. This individual will be provided a remote work day of their choosing. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $72,000-$78,000. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Oct 26, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications. A current CV/resume. List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to nickolas.chabot-olson@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41348&lang=en": {"title": "Treasury Manager", "description": "Closing Date: 10/17/2026 Posted Date: Oct 12, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: Treasurer Schedule: Full-time Join Our Team and Make a Difference in Higher Education! At the System Administration office at the University of Colorado, we are dedicated to building a workplace where everyone feels valued, supported, and empowered to thrive. Our office is committed to fostering a culture where employees find community, a sense of belonging, and the opportunity to contribute meaningfully to our mission and purpose. By joining our team, you\u2019ll have a direct impact on shaping the future of higher education. In addition to the Office of the Board of Regents, the University of Colorado\u2019s system administration includes 19 units that provide essential services to CU\u2019s campuses in Aurora, Boulder, Colorado Springs, and Denver, as well as the Office of the President. While not a part of any one campus, we are proud to serve in the centralized office for the University system. Together, we ensure CU continues to deliver outstanding education, groundbreaking research, and valuable service to our communities. We believe in creating an environment where the unique experiences and perspectives of everyone are embraced, enriching the work we do and the strategic outcomes we pursue. If you\u2019re passionate about making a difference, contributing to a dynamic team, and supporting a mission that matters, we encourage you to apply and be part of our journey. Learn more about CU System Administration . Position Summary: The Office of the Treasurer is responsible for the University's cash management, debt management, investment oversight, and property management functions. The office provides strategic guidance and support to university campuses and departments regarding financing strategies, banking relationships, real estate matters, faculty housing assistance programs, and treasury-related initiatives. The Treasury Manager serves as a key member of the Office of the Treasurer and is responsible for managing and enhancing the University\u2019s treasury functions in support of the institution\u2019s long-term financial objectives. This position manages debt accounting and reporting activities, supports debt issuance transactions, and ensures compliance with applicable regulatory, contractual, and policy requirements. The person in this position leads and administers projects and programs in areas of debt management and faculty housing assistance program and serves as a resource for programs in other areas of Treasury. The Treasury Manager plays a critical role in providing accurate, timely, and meaningful financial information to internal and external stakeholders, including the Board of Regents, University leadership, rating agencies, and external service providers. The position also supports the effective stewardship of the University's financial resources through the oversight of key Treasury operations, process improvements, and strategic initiatives. The successful candidate will be a collaborative and results-oriented professional with strong analytical, project management, communication, and relationship management skills. The ability to balance strategic thinking with operational execution is essential. This position reports to the Associate Treasurer and is exempt from the State of Colorado Classified Staff System. Where You Will Work: Applicants must be Colorado residents or able to relocate to Colorado within a month of starting employment with University of Colorado System Administration. This role is eligible for a hybrid schedule, working 2-3 days a week in the office at 1800 Grant St, Denver, CO. Please note, leadership may adjust in-office work requirements with a minimum of three months' notice before any change can be implemented. Equal Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Duties and Responsibilities: Duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: General Stay informed of capital market developments, treasury management best practices, and emerging financial technologies. Develop a collaborative partnership with campuses, other departments within system administration to identify their needs, address challenges, and implement effective treasury solutions. Take a lead in reviewing and maintaining the University's Debt Management Policy and related procedures. Evaluate the impact of legislative initiatives and regulatory developments affecting Treasury operations and provide analysis regarding potential impacts to the treasury team. Maintain expertise regarding debt-related reporting requirements established by the Board of Regents, federal and state agencies, rating agencies, and other governing bodies. Assist in responding to information requests from the Board of Regents, President's Office, campus CFOs, CCHE, and other internal and external stakeholders. Debt Management Assist in managing and maintaining university\u2019s debt portfolio, including fixed-rate and variable-rate debt, commercial paper programs, bank loans, lines of credit and lease-financing obligations. Assist in analyzing financing alternatives, including public-private partnerships and other innovative financing structures, and prepare recommendations that are consistent with university\u2019s policies and procedures and regulatory requirements. Collaborate with campuses and/or financial advisor and develop financial models and debt affordability analyses to support capital planning and debt capacity assessments. Manage coordination of debt issuance and refinancing transactions, including preparation and organization of bond issuance documents, including Official Statements and other due diligence materials. Lead the collection, validation, and organization of information requested by underwriters, bond and disclosure counsels, financing advisors, rating agencies, auditors and other financing participants. Manage the investment and reinvestment of debt proceeds with the Treasurer and Assistant Treasurer Cash and Short-term Investments. Manage quarterly cash-flow forecasts in collaboration with campuses; analyze funding needs for campus capital projects and inform relevant stakeholders on debt issuance amount/timing, liquidity management and investment decisions. Manage and direct all debt service activities, including monitoring requirements and ensuring the timely fulfillment of principal, interest, and related payment obligations. Develop, maintain, and enhance debt management records and documentation systems. Project and Program Management Lead the implementation, administration, and ongoing optimization of debt management software supporting Treasury operations and reporting. Manage the development, implementation, and administration of the IRC Housing Assistance Program in collaboration with university stakeholders and external partners. Provide oversight and enhance reporting on university\u2019s Faculty Housing Assistance Program (FHAP). Evaluate potential benefit of internal bank structure for capital project financing across the university system and make recommendation if beneficial. Act as a treasury lead in procurement and RFP processes for debt-related service providers. Manage special projects and strategic initiatives assigned by the Treasurer and Associate Treasurer. Reporting and Compliance Prepare and coordinate debt-related reports required by federal regulations, state statutes, Board of Regents policies, rating agencies, debt covenants, contracts, and external service providers. Manage debt compliance calendars and including timely filing of continuing disclosure reports and other required compliance submissions. Manage partnership with campuses and affiliated entities to identify material financial obligations and ensure required notices are submitted through EMMA within regulatory deadlines. Ensure compliance with bond covenants, lease agreements, internal loan agreements, commercial paper programs, variable-rate debt obligations, and other financing arrangements. Manage relationship with the external arbitrage vendor to coordinate rebate calculations and reporting. Accounting and Audit Manage timely recording of debt-related transactions, including issuances, defeasances, amortizations, and other financing activities, in accordance with applicable GASB standards. Provide debt accounting guidance and support to campuses, including project fund allocations and debt-related financial reporting. Perform monthly, quarterly, and annual reconciliations of debt instruments, debt service payments, and project allocations. Manage internal loan activities, including resolution preparation, Board and management approvals, interest-rate determinations, and amortization schedule development. Initiate and/or coordinate debt service payments, wire transfers, and related treasury transactions; reconcile debt balances with trustee statements and general ledger accounts. Partner with the Office of the Controller and external auditors to prepare audit schedules, confirmations, supporting documentation, and follow-up responses. Lead all debt-related audit requests, confirmations, subsequent-event reporting, and supporting documentation requirements Other Duties Contribute in the enhancement of Treasury's cash forecasting, liquidity management, and asset allocation processes as needed. Document debt management and Treasury operational procedures to strengthen internal controls and continuity of operation. Participate in Treasury-related RFP processes and vendor evaluations as needed. Train Treasury staff on debt accounting, reporting, and compliance functions to ensure operational resiliency and adequate backup coverage. Provide backup support for critical Treasury operations as needed. What We Offer: Salary: The anticipated hiring range has been established at $118,000-$124,000. CU System Administration takes into consideration a combination of the selected candidate\u2019s education, training and experience as it relates to the position, as well as the position\u2019s scope and complexity, internal pay equity and external market value when determining a salary level for potential new employees. Benefits: With our unparalleled range of benefits, including top-notch healthcare, comprehensive wellness programs, enriching professional development, and a dynamic work-life balance, we ensure your holistic growth and happiness. For more information on benefits programs, please review our Comprehensive Benefits Guide . Access our Total Compensation Calculator to see what your total rewards could be at CU. (This position is a University Staff position) Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Please include all relevant experience in your resume to be accurately assessed against these qualifications. You must meet all minimum requirements at the time of application to be considered for this role. Bachelor's degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, Business Administration, or a related field from an accredited institution. Five (5) years of progressively responsible experience in treasury, finance, banking, investments, debt management, or a related financial discipline. Three (3) years of experience in debt accounting, debt management, capital financing, or debt compliance activities. One (1) year of experience in a team lead or supervisory role, which includes assigning and reviewing the work of others, providing guidance to internal and external team members, and assisting management with performance reviews (this requirement may be substituted by formal leadership training) Demonstrated experience with debt compliance requirements, including SEC Rule 15c2-12 continuing disclosure obligations. Experience conducting financial analysis and developing financial models. Experience with governmental accounting principles and capital budgeting processes. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in Finance, Accounting, Business Administration, Public Administration, or a related field. Seven (7) years of professional experience progressively responsible experience in treasury, finance, banking, investments, debt management, or a related financial discipline. Two (2) years of experience leading projects, serving as a team lead, or coordinating and guiding the work of others, including assigning or reviewing work, providing guidance to internal or external team members, and supporting team or organizational priorities. This requirement may be substituted by formal leadership training Experience working in higher education, public finance, municipal finance, or governmental treasury operations. Experience supporting bond issuances, commercial paper programs, variable-rate debt obligations, or other complex financing arrangements. Experience implementing or administering treasury or debt management software platforms. Certified Treasury Professional (CTP), Certified Public Accountant (CPA), Chartered Financial Analyst (CFA), or similar professional designation. Experience with PeopleSoft Financials and debt management systems. Project management experience involving cross-functional stakeholders and enterprise initiatives. How to Apply: For full consideration, please attach the following as separate documents to your application: A cover letter identifying the job specific minimum qualifications you possess and interest in the position. A resume including all relevant experience to be accurately assessed against the qualifications listed in the posting. Please ensure you check the \u201cJob Specific Attachments\u201d box next to each document on the \u201cRequired Documents\u201d page of the application for the appropriate documents to be attached. Per the Colorado Job Application Fairness Act, you are not required to provide your date of birth, dates of school attendance, or dates of graduation on your resume or cover letter. If an application requires additional materials, such as a transcript or certification, you may redact identifying information relating to your date or birth, dates of school attendance, or dates of graduation. When to Apply: For full consideration completed applications must be submitted by Friday, October 16th . Reference checking is a standard step in our hiring process. You may be asked to provide contact information, including email addresses and phone numbers, for up to five references as part of the search process for this position. *Please note: All application materials must be submitted through CU Careers; emailed materials will not be considered. * Sponsorship Statement: We are unable to sponsor applicants for work visas for this position. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The Immigration Reform and Control Act requires that a verification of employment eligibility be documented for all new employees by the end of the third day of work. The University of Colorado is committed to diversity and equality in education and employment. ADA Statement: We are committed to an inclusive and barrier-free search process. We provide accommodations for applicants requesting accommodation through the search process such as alternative formats of this posting. Individuals with disabilities in need of accommodations throughout the search process should contact the ADA Coordinator at: systemhr@cu.edu ."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=38857&lang=en": {"title": "Pipe Mechanical Trades - II Facilities Maintenance Technician Lead (Housing)", "description": "Closing Date: 10/24/2026 Posted Date: Oct 9, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: ADM AVCFM BMO Anschutz Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Denver Department: Facilities Management Job Title: Pipe Mechanical Trades - II Facilities Maintenance Technician Lead (Housing) Position #: 844879 \u2013 Requisition #: 38857 Job Summary: Join the Facilities Management Department on the University of Colorado Denver Campus as a Pipe Mechanical Trades II (PMTII), Facilities Maintenance Technician Lead (Housing). This is a full-time position. The PMT-II Facilities Maintenance Technician Lead (Housing) position: Maintain all facilities and operating systems in a safe and efficient working order. This includes regular maintenance on HVAC, electrical, mechanical, utility systems, interior finishes, and appliances and coordinate work with journey level technicians and contractors. You will record issues and make work reports via email, log your work in CMMS and monitor building systems in BAS and perform various other duties and tasks as required. This is an evening, second shift position. Hours are Monday through Friday, 9:30am to 6:00pm , and qualify for shift differential. Key Responsibilities: 30% - Zone Preventative Maintenance Receives preventive maintenance work orders, performs preventive maintenance on assigned equipment, which may include the following: faucets, pipes, hot water tanks, toilets, garbage disposals, dishwashers, refrigerators, ceiling lights, and logs reports as required The position must have the ability to perform data entry and be able to operate a computer to log reports. The position will record issues through the shift desk computer and maintain the logbook. The position must have the ability for written communication since the position will maintain the logbook. Set priorities based on urgency and make or arrange for the necessary repairs, including replacing or modifying components (e.g., plumbing, steam, electrical, HVAC, and workspace aesthetic-related items). Evaluate operations and implement recommendations to prevent failures and improve efficiency of HVAC and energy management systems. Maintain and monitor operating logs to determine irregular equipment performance 20% - Corrective Maintenance Respond to corrective maintenance calls and verbal assignments, ensuring that tenant/staff requests are attended to in a timely, courteous, and efficient manner. These work orders include requests for the repair of minor electrical items, including lighting, minor plumbing items, floods, freezer monitoring, HVAC items, including hot/cold calls, and too much/too little air supply. Respond to, and communicate with, tenants to ensure all complaints are resolved in a timely manner and in a craftsman-like fashion. The position will operate a university vehicle to transport necessary tools/equipment to work sites across campus 10% - Project Coordination and Support Assist in Capital Projects as appropriate to ensure quality construction and repairs. Coordinate Facilities Funded Projects within the Zone. Collaborate and advise project managers, general contractors, and vendors during construction, occupancy and warranty phases to ensure all mechanical and control problems are installed/repaired to meet UCD|AMC construction standards. Provide BO&M representation as required. Act as a Subject Matter Expert where appropriate and provide feedback to Project Manager via responses. 10% - Emergencies, Special Events and Other Duties Participates and assists in emergencies based on the magnitude and nature. Supports various special events both in preparation and during the event (i.e. Commencement). Examples of emergencies and special events could include commencement, snow removal, power outages, flood, etc. May be assigned other duties as required. The position must have the ability to communicate with security, fire department, and the police department in case of an emergency and be able to communicate the problem. 30% - Lead Responsibilities Coordinates the team\u2019s tasks, manages procurement, reviews WO entries, and assists team members as needed. Implements leadership priorities to support vision and objectives. Work Location: Onsite \u2013 this role is expected to work onsite and is located in Denver, Colorado. Why Join Us: Apply today to be part of a team where the focus is supporting the university\u2019s mission of education the next generation. We are looking for someone with a solid maintenance/service background to learn more and develop new skills. You will be set up for success. We will provide you with the training necessary to become proficient in the equipment we maintain. There are also paid external training opportunities for beneficial technical and professional development courses. All of the hand and specialty tools you need will be provided. We offer robust training program for anyone interested in growing their career options. From hands on work with journey level technicians and online self-paced technical training to paid external trades certifications and CU employee tuition assistance, CU Denver can be the place to boost your career trajectory. Come to a place where you can develop a career, not just another job. For more information about the university of Colorado Denver campus please visit www.ucdenver.edu Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 10/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Three years of progressively responsible residential maintenance experience, including minor repairs to HVAC, electrical, lighting, and plumbing systems and indoor finishes. Colorado law requires that candidates for state government jobs be residents of Colorado at the time of application. Substitution: Successful completion of a formalized plumbing, pipefitting, steam fitting, or heating, ventilation, and air conditioning apprenticeship program or higher level, non-correspondence course of work in the same field from an accredited vocational school or university may substitute for the experience on a year-to-year basis. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: 1 -3 years of lead experience Experience using computers to monitor buildings tied into Building Automation Systems (BAS) Experience fixing and maintaining equipment and machinery Experience keeping activity logs Experience in heating, ventilation, and air conditioning Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to manage multiple tasks and work independently with minimal supervision. Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to establish rapport with people of diverse backgrounds. Experience that demonstrates strong customer service skills. Excellent oral communication skills with the ability to handle stressful situations in a calm and professional manner. Ability to communicate effectively in written form, which includes the ability to check for typographical, grammatical, and spelling errors Mechanical Ability Physical Ability Planning and organization skills. Knowledge of heating, ventilation, and air conditioning How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position (only use if a cover letter is necessary) 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Megan Freije megan.freije@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by October 23, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range $4906 - $5690 per month for this position has been established. The second shift differential of 7.5% shall be paid for all hours worked when half or more of the scheduled work hours fall between 4 p.m. and 11 p.m. Monday through Thursday. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. This position may be eligible for a one-time non-base building sign-on bonus up to $2,000. Details of this recruitment incentive program will be provided during the interview process. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu \u200b. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41337&lang=en": {"title": "Assistant Budget Director", "description": "Closing Date: 11/01/2026 Posted Date: Oct 8, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: ADM-AVCBO Budget Office-Denver Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Business Services Assistant Director Working Title: Assistant Budget Director FTE: Full-time 1.0 (100%) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: $102,197 - $112,955 | Position #00804189 \u2013 Requisition #41337 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Assistant Budget Director provides budget and financial services for the University of Colorado Denver by coordinating the request and operating budget cycles in an efficient and timely manner. In this role, the Assistant Budget Director will work with many constituencies including campus administration, campus operating units, employee groups, and the President\u2019s Office. Assistant Budget Director What you will do: Supervises team of three Budget Analysts engaged in providing budget support for all administrative units and the Denver schools & colleges, including preparing annual budget requests, regular budget analysis, and revisions. Assist in reconciling and implementing the annual CU Denver operating budget in collaboration with the Anschutz team. Collaborate with Denver School and College fiscal managers with developing and maintaining budgets. Identify inefficient processes and make recommendations for improvement. Preparation of the annual University of Colorado Denver Budget Data document for state General Fund support by gathering data in accordance with state, CCHE, and University guidelines and specific formats. Develops related Budget Data schedules on data and information for student enrollment, tuition, and other programs. Monitor the budgetary data maintained in the University financial reporting system by reviewing departmental changes to initial operating budgets for reasonable budgeting decisions, compliance with applicable guidelines, and proper preparation. Assists in responding to requests for information from the President\u2019s Office, auditors, Administration and outside agencies. Manage processes in Anaplan through verifying system data, preparing drivers, determining Denver Campus security, creating reports, and managing documentation and training. Oversee the communications and change management for Anaplan including ensuring the distribution of information to end users on system design, updates, training, and deadlines. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. A bachelor\u2019s degree in business, business administration, finance, accounting, or directly related field from an accredited institution. Four years of progressively responsible finance or budget related experience, with at least one year in higher education or state government. The position requires extensive, diverse and progressively responsible experience, including direct responsibility for higher education budgets. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor\u2019s degree on a year for year basis. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Experience supervising a team of analysts. PeopleSoft or other Oracle-based financial system experience is highly desired. Anaplan based budgeting system experience is highly desired. Experience with the State of Colorado and/or University of Colorado budgetary processes is highly desired. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Leadership and team development skills. Advanced knowledge of fiscal management and HR practices. Ability to influence institutional financial strategy. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Demonstrate an exceptional understanding of access and engagement with a commitment to developing equitable practices. Knowledge of accounting and budgeting processes. Ability to evaluate existing processes and recommend improvements. Demonstrated competence in the use of MS Office applications, particularly MS Excel and MS Access, for spreadsheets, statistical analysis, graphics, and decision support. Analytical skills including the ability to apply math (algebra) skills, analyze implications of changes in methods, input data, policies, etc. Able to analyze and interpret financial data by using spreadsheets, databases, and modeling applications. Understanding of higher education policies and issues. Understanding of relational database concepts and queries. Strong organizational and time management skills; ability to meet multiple deadlines and manage interrelated and/or complex issues or transactions. Ability to evaluate policies and exercise good judgment in the interpretation and application of procedures and rules. Conditions of Employment This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $102,197 - $112,955. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Oct 22, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications A current CV/resume List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Tawnya Boulier, tawnya.boulier@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41323&lang=en": {"title": "Associate Vice Chancellor for Student Affairs", "description": "Closing Date: 12/01/2026 Posted Date: Oct 8, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCSSLS-AVCSCE UnivAdv&StdEngag Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Associate Vice Chancellor Working Title: Associate Vice Chancellor for Student Affairs FTE: Full-time Salary Range: $200,000-$220,000 Position #00350581 \u2013 Requisition #41323 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Associate Vice Chancellor (AVC) for Student Affairs provides strategic and visionary leadership for a comprehensive, student-centered approach to engagement, belonging, wellbeing, and success. The AVC establishes the vision, priorities, strategies, and organizational infrastructure necessary to create an exceptional student experience and ensure students have the support and resources they need to thrive. As a key leader within the Division of Strategic Enrollment and Student Success (SESS), the AVC reports to the Vice Chancellor for Strategic Enrollment and Student Success and serves as a strategic partner to senior leaders across the university. The AVC leads student services and resources that promote personal development, student engagement, wellbeing, and a safe, welcoming, and inclusive campus community. Through these efforts, Student Affairs plays a critical role in advancing student persistence, retention, completion, and overall success. The AVC will bring a deep understanding of the opportunities and challenges facing today\u2019s higher education institutions, particularly those affecting an increasingly diverse student population. The AVC will use data, research, assessment, and student feedback to identify emerging needs, inform decisions, evaluate effectiveness, and address structural barriers that may impede student success. The AVC will also build strong relationships across academic and administrative units and with external partners to strengthen the university\u2019s capacity to serve students effectively. The AVC will be a forward-thinking and entrepreneurial leader who anticipates the evolving needs of students and develops innovative approaches to the student experience. The AVC will strategically prioritize people, programs, technology, and financial resources to maximize student success and institutional impact. The position provides leadership for professional and student staff, has fiscal responsibility for the Student Affairs portfolio and its operating budgets, and leads organizational strategies that promote a high-performing, collaborative, and student-centered culture. As a member of the SESS leadership team, the AVC serves as a campus-wide leader and strategic partner at the intersection of academics, enrollment, student success, wellbeing, and external engagement. The AVC will work across organizational boundaries to align resources, strengthen partnerships, remove barriers, and advance institutional priorities that enable every student to succeed. Associate Vice Chancellor for Student Affairs What you will do: Develop and lead a comprehensive Student Affairs strategy aligned with the university\u2019s mission, strategic plan, enrollment goals, and student success priorities. Translate institutional priorities into measurable goals, strategies, initiatives, and outcomes. Serve as a strategic advisor to senior leadership, including the Senior Vice Chancellor for Strategic Enrollment and Student Success (SESS) and the SESS leadership team, on matters related to the student experience, engagement, campus climate, wellbeing, safety, and retention. Collaborate effectively with deans, Academic Affairs, and campus and external partners. Provide visionary leadership for the student experience, creating a welcoming, inclusive, engaging, and student-centered campus environment. Strengthen programs and services that advance belonging, community, leadership development, engagement, personal growth, wellbeing, and student success. Lead strategic planning, organizational development, and continuous improvement across the Student Affairs portfolio. Streamline functions, processes, practices, and technology to improve service delivery, operational effectiveness, student outcomes, and retention. Use data, research, assessment, and student feedback to identify emerging needs, evaluate programs and services, inform decision-making, and ensure student experiences meaningfully shape institutional policies and priorities. Promote a culture that recognizes students as partners in shaping the university experience. Lead a coordinated student success continuum that advances engagement, retention, wellbeing, and student success through collaboration across CU Denver, the tri-institutional community, AHEC, and external partners. Provide strategic leadership for student wellbeing, mental health, wellness, and conduct, working collaboratively across disciplines to strengthen a proactive campus wellness culture that supports student success. Lead and develop the Student Affairs leadership team, providing supervision, coaching, performance management, professional development, and support for six direct reports and the broader Student Affairs workforce. Foster a collaborative, supportive, high-performing workplace. Provide executive oversight of fiscal and administrative operations, including budget planning, resource allocation, business management, housing assets, contract services, negotiations, and procurement in accordance with university policies and procedures. Leverage internal and external resources and partnerships to strengthen the campus community, enhance the student experience, advance institutional priorities, and elevate the university\u2019s reputation. Travel as needed to support university, community, and professional responsibilities. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Earned Master\u2019s degree in higher education, educational leadership, business administration, public administration or a closely related field Eight (8) years of diverse and progressively responsible experience at the management level, including direct responsibility for student services and/or related services in higher education. Progressive responsibility and experience in supervising professional and administrative staff. Demonstrable experience in managing and working with complex budgets. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Earned doctorate Student Affairs and student success experience at a higher education institution that is a comprehensive urban campus. Documented experience in developing, implementing and evaluating unit budgets, goals and strategic planning. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong understanding of university student services and development programs, policies, and practices. Ability to work effectively with diverse teams and individuals and units on and off campus.\\ Demonstrated leadership, budget management and interpersonal skills. A leadership style that promotes collaboration and cooperation. Commitment to excellence, creativity and innovation. Strong oral and written communication skills. Demonstrated ability to communicate and maintain interpersonal relationships within an ethnically and culturally diverse urban learning environment with a commitment to inclusion, diversity and respect. Documented experience in developing, implementing and evaluating unit goals and strategic planning. Computer proficiency including MS Office, social media and CRM experience. Ability to prioritize and perform multiple projects simultaneously. Eagerness to acquire new skills. Dependable, team-oriented and a self-starter. Ability to manage and coach team members and develop staff. Skilled record of accomplishment leading, supervising, evaluating, hiring and resolving staff performance problems. Ability to think strategically and aptitude for managing multiple tasks and priorities. Experience collaborating with multiple stakeholders. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed in a hybrid environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $200,000 - $220,000. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by October 31st. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications A current CV/resume List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Tyler Keyworth, tyler.keyworth@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41344&lang=en": {"title": "Faculty Fellow for Lecturer Success", "description": "Closing Date: 10/28/2026 Posted Date: Oct 7, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: AVCASA-FAUE FacAffrs/UG Enrich Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Faculty Fellow for Lecturer Success Working Title: Faculty Fellow FTE: Part-time Salary Range: $5,000 stipend Position #00853662\u2013 Requisition #41344 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Center for Faculty Development & Advancement (CFDA) seeks a faculty fellow for the 26-27 academic year to support initiatives that enhance the success, engagement, and professional development of lecturers across CU Denver. Lecturers play a critical role in advancing the university's mission through high-quality teaching, student mentorship, and contributions to student success, retention, and belonging. This fellowship provides an opportunity for a faculty member to lead efforts that strengthen community, recognition, professional growth, and institutional connection among lecturers. A primary responsibility of this fellow will be the planning and implementation of the inaugural Lecturer Summit, a spring 2027 collaborative event sponsored by CFDA and UCDALI that celebrates and supports lecturers through professional learning, networking, and community-building opportunities. In partnership with CFDA and campus stakeholders, the fellow will have substantial autonomy to shape the vision, content, and experience of the summit while developing additional initiatives that support lecturer success throughout the academic year. This position is ideal for a faculty member who is passionate about teaching excellence, faculty development, community building, and advancing institutional support for lecturers. This position requires an estimated commitment of 5-7 hours per week during the academic year. Faculty Fellow for Lecturer Success What you will do: Lecturer Summit Leadership Serve as the primary faculty lead and organizer for the inaugural Lecturer Summit. Collaborate with CFDA and UCDALI, Bridge Liaisons, and other campus partners to develop the summit theme, goals, learning outcomes, and program structure. Compile data from lecturers around needs and desires for the Lecturer Summit learning outcomes. Design engaging programming focused on topics such as: Effective and innovative teaching practices Student success and engagement Faculty well-being and resilience Career development pathways for lecturers Inclusive and equitable teaching practices Cross-disciplinary collaboration and networking Identify and recruit speakers, facilitators, and panelists. Facilitate summit sessions and discussions as appropriate. Recruit collaborators to increase scope and impact of Summit. Assist with participant marketing, outreach, and promotion. Evaluate the effectiveness of the Lecturer Summit. Lecturer Community Building Develop opportunities for networking and community among lecturers across schools and colleges. Gather feedback from lecturers regarding professional development needs and institutional support. Foster cross-disciplinary connections and sharing of effective teaching practices. Program Development and Innovation Work collaboratively with CFDA staff to develop new programming and resources that support lecturer success. Recommend strategies for increasing lecturer engagement, recognition, and professional growth opportunities. Develop and pilot creative initiatives aligned with identified lecturer needs and interests. Assessment and Continuous Improvement Collect and analyze participant feedback from the Lecturer Summit and related programming. Prepare a brief annual report summarizing outcomes, recommendations, and future opportunities. Identify metrics and indicators of success related to lecturer engagement and satisfaction. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Full-time faculty member at CU Denver. Demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence and student success. Strong interpersonal, communication, and collaboration skills. Interest in faculty development, mentoring, and community building. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Experience designing or facilitating professional development programs. Experience organizing events, workshops, learning communities, or conferences. Experience supporting lecturer and/or IRC faculty development. Demonstrated commitment to inclusive excellence and belonging. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Passionate about supporting faculty success and professional growth. Bring creativity, initiative, and innovative thinking to program development. Enjoy designing and facilitating engaging learning experiences. Demonstrate strong organizational skills. Value collaboration, inclusion, and community building. Be committed to helping faculty thrive throughout their academic careers. Conditions of Employment This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. \u2022 Current faculty appointment at the University of Colorado Denver. \u2022 Position will last for one academic year Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at - $5,000 stipend. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is/is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Oct 28, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to Aubrey Thorburn, AUBREY.THORBURN@UCDENVER.EDU . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41335&lang=en": {"title": "Professor, Director of Construction", "description": "Closing Date: 12/31/2026 Posted Date: Oct 6, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CEDC-Civil Engineering Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Professor, Faculty and Director Working Title: Professor, Director of Construction FTE: Full-time Salary Range: $85,000.00 - $130,000.00, 9-month contract Position #: 00350978 - Req #41335 About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top ranked bachelors, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. About the College The College of Engineering, Design and Computing (CEDC) takes pride in having a faculty of excellent scholars and engineering practitioners. We attract hard-working students who are enthusiastic about engineering, and we are redesigning engineering education to create the agile versatile engineers of the future. Providing an education of enduring value to our students is at the heart of our College mission. We integrate design innovation and computing technology across disciplines, in conjunction with authentic experiences that develop human and social skills such as creativity, collaboration, entrepreneurship, and leadership. We embrace and leverage our setting across urban and medical campuses to broadly impact the social and economic growth of the Denver urban corridor through enterprise partnerships. Our goal is to emerge as Denver\u2019s technological innovation engine and significantly impact Colorado, the nation, and the world via informatics, infrastructure, sustainability, as a smart city. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Department of Civil Engineering and Construction in the College of Engineering, Design and Computing at the University of Colorado Denver invites applications for the position of Director of Construction. We seek an accomplished leader in construction education, research, and/or professional practice to lead CU Denver\u2019s growing Construction Management and Construction Engineering Management programs. The successful candidate will provide strategic leadership for the programs, support and mentor faculty and students, strengthen industry partnerships, and guide continued growth in education, research, and external engagement. We welcome candidates whose careers bridge academia and professional practice, including candidates with substantial leadership experience in the Architecture, Engineering, and Construction (AEC) industry. Candidates do not need to currently hold a tenured faculty appointment to be considered. The successful candidate will receive a faculty appointment in the Department of Civil Engineering and Construction and a separate four-year appointment as Director of Construction. Depending on the candidate\u2019s background and qualifications, the faculty appointment may be as a tenured Associate Professor or Professor or on the Teaching Professor track. Teaching duties will be in construction engineering management, with upcoming needs in Construction Management Fundamentals, Field Engineering and Management, Materials and Methods, Advanced Construction Technology, Construction Safety, and Construction Engineering. Faculty track and rank will be commensurate with the candidate\u2019s education, experience, qualifications, and career path. Why CU Denver and Denver CU Denver's downtown campus places faculty in the heart of a major metropolitan region, with close connections to construction firms, public agencies, professional organizations, and industry partners across Colorado. Denver offers the cultural and professional resources of a major city, with the Rocky Mountains and extensive outdoor recreation nearby. CU Denver combines the resources of the University of Colorado system with an urban campus closely connected to the community it serves. Eligible employees have access to health and retirement benefits, tuition assistance, professional development resources, and RTD EcoPass transit benefits. About the Department The Civil Engineering and Construction department has 10 full-time tenured and tenure-track faculty, 3 teaching-track faculty, and many part-time lecturers. The department offers undergraduate and graduate degrees, including master's and doctoral degrees, in civil engineering, construction engineering management, and construction management. The civil engineering program has been accredited continuously since its inception, and the newer construction programs were first accredited in 2023. In 2025, the department had 75 graduate students and 310 undergraduate students. Approximately 35% are in the construction programs. About the Program The Construction Engineering and Management (CEM) program at the University of Colorado Denver (CU Denver) launched in Fall 2014 as a graduate specialty of the Master of Engineering in Civil Engineering in response to local industry requests and support. Work on two bachelor's degrees began in 2017: the Bachelor of Science (BS) in Construction Management (CM) and the Bachelor of Science in Construction Engineering Management (CEM). CEDC moved forward with both degrees because of interdisciplinary support throughout the College and across CU Denver, especially from the College of Architecture and Planning and the Business School. The two BS degrees were approved by CU Denver, the University of Colorado Regents, and the Colorado Department of Higher Education in Fall 2019, launched in August 2020, and accredited by ABET in 2023. Professor, Director of Construction What you will do: The faculty responsibilities associated with this position depend on the appointment track and reflect the workload distribution while serving as Director of Construction. A Teaching Professor-track appointment will include 40% teaching and 60% service, while a tenure-line appointment will include 20% teaching, 20% research, and 60% service. The 60% service allocation includes the leadership and administrative responsibilities associated with the four-year Director appointment. The Director appointment includes an additional academic year administrative stipend equal to 7\u201310% of the faculty base salary. If the Director appointment ends, the faculty workload would be adjusted consistent with the individual\u2019s faculty track and other assigned responsibilities. Lead the Construction Programs Recruit, develop, and retain outstanding faculty and staff Oversee program ABET accreditation; manage operations and budget in partnership with department leadership; lead issue resolution Grow Enrollment and Program Reach Lead strategy to grow and retain undergraduate and graduate enrollment Increase the program\u2019s visibility and reputation regionally and nationally Advance Academic Quality and Student Experience Champion impactful curricular and extracurricular learning opportunities Integrate emerging construction technologies into teaching and learning Strengthen Industry Engagement and Fundraising Continue to build and activate a strong Industry Advisory Board (IAB) to support program relevance, student opportunities, and resource development Diversify program revenue streams Strengthen Research and External Funding Support growth in research activity and external funding across the program Support and mentor faculty in developing research and scholarly activities Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. All candidates: Demonstrated leadership experience in academia, the construction industry, or a closely related setting. For appointment on the tenure line: PhD in Construction Management, Construction Engineering, Civil Engineering, or a related field. A proven record of teaching, research, and service accomplishments commensurate with unit-level and college requirements for appointment with tenure at the Associate Professor or Professor level in the Department of Civil Engineering and Construction. For appointment on the Teaching Professor track: Terminal degree in Construction Management, Construction Engineering, Civil Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent qualifications and professional experience consistent with the applicable Teaching Professor-track appointment. A proven record of teaching and/or professional accomplishments commensurate with unit-level and college requirements for appointment at the applicable rank on the Teaching Professor track in the Department of Civil Engineering and Construction. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Competitive candidates may demonstrate strengths in several of the following areas. Candidates are not expected to possess every preferred qualification. Professional experience in or substantial engagement with the Architecture, Engineering, and Construction (AEC) industry. Experience developing industry partnerships, working with advisory boards, and/or supporting fundraising or external engagement. Experience teaching, training, advising, or mentoring students or professionals in construction-related fields. Experience with accreditation, program assessment, or continuous improvement; ABET experience is preferred. Interest in or experience with emerging construction technologies, including applications of AI in education, research, or professional practice. Professional Engineer licensure or other relevant professional license or certification. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Effective communication, interpersonal, and relationship-building skills. Ability to lead collaboratively and support the professional growth of faculty and staff. Strong commitment to undergraduate and graduate education and student success across a range of backgrounds, educational pathways, and career goals. Ability to guide curriculum and program development in response to changes in construction education and professional practice. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. Working from the office is encouraged particularly when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements The ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position may be eligible now and in the future for certain visa sponsorship limited to Change of Status (COS) within the United States or if the candidate meets the criteria for the portability provision. While the hiring unit is willing to pursue visa sponsorship, an offer of employment will be contingent on the candidate having a visa status that allows employment with the University as of the start date for the position or the University\u2019s petition being approved and on the candidate being able to obtain the appropriate visa status. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at: In addition to the faculty salary listed below, the four-year Director appointment includes an administrative stipend equal to 7\u201310% of the faculty base salary. Professor: $120,000 - $130,000 per 9-month academic year. Additional salary for summer months can be sourced from internal funds for additional duties or external funding. Associate Professor: $110,000 - $115,000 per 9-month academic year. Additional salary for summer months can be sourced from internal funds for additional duties or external funding. Teaching Professor-track appointment: $95,000 - $105,000 per 9-month academic year. Additional salary for summer months can be sourced from internal funds for additional duties or external funding. Teaching Associate Professor-track appointment: $85,000 - $95,000 per 9-month academic year. Additional salary for summer months can be sourced from internal funds for additional duties or external funding. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by January 1, 2027. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Interested applicants are welcome to continue to apply. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A one-page cover letter describing interest in the Director of Construction role and relevant qualifications. A current CV/resume. A two-page director philosophy. The names and contact information of three professional references. Candidates will be notified before references are contacted. Questions should be directed to David Mays, David.Mays@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41299&lang=en": {"title": "Director of Development SEHD", "description": "Closing Date: 11/15/2026 Posted Date: Oct 2, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: ADM-CHAN Advancement Denver Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Development Senior Professional Working Title: Director of Development (SEHD) FTE: Full-time 1.0 (100%) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: $90,000-$97,000 Position #00300024 \u2013 Requisition #41299 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . *This is a term limited position that is currently funded through June 30th 2029.* The position will be reviewed by January 2029 to assess financial sustainability. If your term of employment will be concluded based on a lack of funding, you will be provided 30 days\u2019 notice of the term of employment in writing by the University. Director of Development (SEHD) The University of Colorado Denver is a leading public urban research university located in the heart of downtown Denver, where academic excellence, innovation and community partnership come together to expand opportunity and strengthen communities. Within this dynamic institution, the School of Education & Human Development is a statewide and national leader in educational quality, access and equity across the lifespan, from birth through higher education. SEHD prepares equity-minded educators, counselors, researchers and leaders who create meaningful change in schools, families and communities across Colorado and beyond. Through innovative academic programs, impactful research and deep community partnerships, the school advances well-being, opportunity and lifelong learning in diverse urban, rural and global communities. The Director of Development will join SEHD at an important moment of opportunity, building philanthropic partnerships that expand student access, elevate faculty and research, and extend the school\u2019s impact for generations to come. What you will do: Job Purpose: The Director of Development is responsible for leading, developing and executing advancement efforts, which includes developing and managing relationships with gift prospects, and soliciting and stewarding major gifts to maximize philanthropic support for the School of Education & Human Development. Serves as a philanthropic advisor and builds relationships within the School of Education & Human Development to facilitate meaningful connections for donors. Impact & Influence: In a centralized Advancement structure with a team of 23 professionals, the Director of Development is a major gift officer who will grow the pipeline of major and principal gift prospects and donors by partnering with university administration, the Vice Chancellor for Advancement, Executive Director, Deans, faculty, and other campus partners and collaborate with Donor Engagement, Advancement Communications, Alumni Engagement, Gift Planning, fellow major gift officers, and colleagues in central Advancement, including Research, Strategy, and Prospect Management. Success in this role requires strong collaboration, strategic management of donor relationships, accountability for fundraising results, and a commitment to ethical, donor-centered fundraising practices. Key Responsibilities - 80% Maximize the philanthropic potential of a portfolio of major gift prospects by soliciting and closing gifts that advance the mission of the university with a portfolio heavily populated but not limited to Alumni, friends, corporations and foundations. The portfolio will vacillate based on the rating and research analysis of the best targets for major gift opportunities in service to the university. Qualify, cultivate, solicit, and steward a portfolio of 80-100 prospects, including individuals, corporations, and foundations (SEHD has a long history of heavy corporate, foundation, and gift planning engagement) for gifts of $25,000+. Align donor interests with the strategic priorities of the university. Analyze prospect research materials to target likely donors of $25,000+. Ensure that contact reports are written and entered in a timely manner and utilized to gain the maximum value from future donor engagements. Work with Executive Director of Development on developing an annual fundraising operating plan to establish fundraising goals built on portfolio projections and historical fundraising. Build fundraising strategies around existing research activities, specifically interdisciplinary societal grand challenges identified by the university. In addition to fundraising goals, the Director of Development will be responsible for meeting specific process targets designed to ensure a disciplined approach to building a successful major gift program, such as visits, proposals, and portfolio penetration. Serve as an Advancement liaison to campus units - 20% Creating and implementing fundraising strategies for programs and initiatives that focus on rated targets of $25,000+ Developing familiarity with campus and unit fundraising priorities Working collaboratively with campus partners and Advancement colleagues to formulate plans for prospect engagement and identifying potential top donors not yet aware of or engaged with the university Facilitating interaction between major gift prospects and campus and system leaders and faculty other duties as assigned. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Bachelor\u2019s Degree in nonprofit management, business, marketing or other related field Two (2) years of experience in fundraising, alumni/donor relations, or other nonprofit role or equivalent experience in for-profit marketing or project management or directly related field Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor\u2019s degree on a year for year basis. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Master\u2019s Degree in a directly related field. Five (5) or more years of professional related experience in fundraising in a college or university development program or other comparable charitable organization. Experience managing high-level volunteers. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of major gift fundraising within a higher education or similar environment. Superior relationship building skills. Proven success in securing and conducting face to face meetings for major solicitations. Excellent spoken and written communication skills. Ability to prioritize, negotiate, and influence effectively. Effective interpersonal, strategic planning, administrative and organizational skills. Solid judgement and sensitivity to others. Ability to work independently and as part of a larger team. Familiarity with financial planning, tax and charitable gift laws, and planned giving vehicles and methods. Ability to effectively manage multiple assignments simultaneously. Ability to cold call. Ability to qualify and disqualify. Ability to work with a generalized prospect pool. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and internet navigation tools with proven knowledge of word processing, spreadsheet software, email, internet access software, and CRM. Ability to meet metrics and establish goals. Maintain excellent records and stay up to date with contact reports, expense reports, and all required internal administrative processes. Proven track record of donor engagement to include identification, cultivation, solicitation at > $25,000. Ability to create individual donor strategies for solicitation. Demonstrates commitment to ethical fundraising practices and effective engagement with various constituencies. Other Variables: Position is highly visible and requires weekends and evenings for attendance at special events, travel, dinners, athletic events, and entertainment. This position requires great flexibility around weekend and evening activities. Shows enthusiasm for urban public higher education mission. Must have legal driver\u2019s license. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Position is highly visible and requires weekends and evenings for attendance at special events, travel, dinners, athletic events, and entertainment. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $90,000-$97,000. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Oct 16, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: \u2022 A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications \u2022 A current CV/resume \u2022 List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to nickolas.chabot-olson@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41297&lang=en": {"title": "Director of Development - CAM", "description": "Closing Date: 11/15/2026 Posted Date: Oct 2, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: ADM-CHAN Advancement Denver Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Development Senior Professional Working Title: Director of Development (CAM) FTE: Full-time 1.0 (100%) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: $90,000-$97,000 Position #000001242 \u2013 Requisition #41297 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . *This is a term limited position that is currently funded through June 30th 2029.* The position will be reviewed by January 2029 to assess financial sustainability. If your term of employment will be concluded based on a lack of funding, you will be provided 30 days\u2019 notice of the term of employment in writing by the University. Director of Development (CAM) The University of Colorado Denver is Colorado\u2019s public urban research university, located in the heart of a city known for creativity, innovation and cultural vitality. Within this dynamic environment, the College of Arts & Media (CAM) is home to an ambitious community of artists, makers, scholars and innovators preparing to shape the rapidly evolving creative industries. Through nationally recognized programs in film and television, music and entertainment, visual arts, recording arts and media forensics, CAM combines rigorous academic study with hands-on creative practice, state-of-the-art technology and meaningful connections to Denver\u2019s thriving arts and entertainment community. The Director of Development will join CAM at an exciting moment of possibility, building philanthropic partnerships that expand access for talented students, faculty and creative excellence, strengthen industry and community engagement, and bring bold artistic ideas to life. What you will do: Job Purpose: The Director of Development (CAM) is responsible for leading, developing and executing advancement efforts, which includes developing and managing relationships with gift prospects, and soliciting and stewarding major gifts to maximize philanthropic support for the College of Arts & Media. Serves as a philanthropic advisor and builds relationships within the College of Arts & Media to facilitate meaningful connections for donors. Impact & Influence: In a centralized Advancement structure with a team of 23 professionals, the Director of Development is a major gift officer who will grow the pipeline of major and principal gift prospects and donors by partnering with university administration, the Vice Chancellor for Advancement, Executive Director, Deans, faculty, and other campus partners and collaborate with Donor Engagement, Advancement Communications, Alumni Engagement, Gift Planning, fellow major gift officers, and colleagues in central Advancement, including Research, Strategy, and Prospect Management. Success in this role requires strong collaboration, strategic management of donor relationships, accountability for fundraising results, and a commitment to ethical, donor-centered fundraising practices. Key Responsibilities - 80% Maximize the philanthropic potential of a portfolio of major gift prospects by soliciting and closing gifts that advance the mission of the university with a portfolio heavily populated but not limited to Alumni, friends, corporations and foundations. The portfolio will vacillate based on the rating and research analysis of the best targets for major gift opportunities in service to the university. Qualify, cultivate, solicit, and steward a portfolio of 80-100 prospects, including individuals, corporations, and foundations, for gifts of $25,000+. Align donor interests with the strategic priorities of the university. Analyze prospect research materials to target likely donors of $25,000+. Ensure that contact reports are written and entered in a timely manner and utilized to gain the maximum value from future donor engagements. Work with Executive Director on developing an annual fundraising operating plan to establish fundraising goals built on portfolio projections and historical fundraising. Build fundraising strategies around existing research activities, specifically interdisciplinary societal grand challenges identified by the university. In addition to fundraising goals, the Director of Development will be responsible for meeting specific process targets designed to ensure a disciplined approach to building a successful major gift program, such as visits, proposals, and portfolio implementation. Position is highly visible and requires weekends and evenings for attendance at special events, travel, dinners, athletic events, and entertainment. This position requires great flexibility around weekend and evening activities. Serve as an Advancement liaison to campus units - 20% Creating and implementing fundraising strategies for programs and initiatives that focus on rated targets of $25,000+. Developing familiarity with campus and unit fundraising priorities. Working collaboratively with campus partners and Advancement colleagues to formulate plans for prospect engagement and identifying potential top donors not yet aware of or engaged with the university. Facilitating interaction between major gift prospects and campus and system leaders and faculty. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Bachelor\u2019s Degree in nonprofit management, business, marketing or other related field. Two (2) years of experience in fundraising, alumni/donor relations, or other nonprofit role or equivalent experience in for-profit marketing or project management or directly related field. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor\u2019s degree on a year for year basis. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Master\u2019s Degree in a directly related field. Five (5) or more years of professional related experience in fundraising in a college or university development program or other comparable charitable organization. Experience managing high-level volunteers. Familiarity with the arts community, including visual and multi-media. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of major gift fundraising within a higher education or similar environment. Superior relationship building skills. . Proven success in securing and conducting face to face meetings for major solicitations . Excellent spoken and written communication skills. Ability to prioritize, negotiate, and influence effectively. Effective interpersonal, strategic planning, administrative and organizational skills. Solid judgement and sensitivity to others. Ability to work independently and as part of a larger team. Familiarity with financial planning, tax and charitable gift laws, and planned giving vehicles and methods. Ability to effectively manage multiple assignments simultaneously. Ability to cold call. Ability to qualify and disqualify. Ability to work with a generalized prospect pool. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and internet navigation tools with proven knowledge of word processing, spreadsheet software, email, internet access software, and CRM. Ability to meet metrics and establish goals. Maintain excellent records and stay up to date with contact reports, expense reports, and all required internal administrative processes. Proven track record of donor engagement to include identification, cultivation, solicitation of more than $25,000. Ability to create individual donor strategies for solicitation. Demonstrates commitment to ethical fundraising practices and effective engagement with various constituencies. Other Variables: Position is highly visible and requires weekends and evenings for attendance at special events, travel, dinners, athletic events, and entertainment. This position requires great flexibility around weekend and evening activities. Shows enthusiasm for urban public higher education mission. Must have legal driver\u2019s license. Conditions of Employment This is a term limited position that is currently funded through June 30th 2029. Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Position is highly visible and requires weekends and evenings for attendance at special events, travel, dinners, athletic events, and entertainment. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $90,000-$97,000. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Oct 16, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications A current CV/resume List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to nickolas.chabot-olson@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41295&lang=en": {"title": "Lecturer - Illustration", "description": "Closing Date: 11/01/2026 Posted Date: Oct 1, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CAM-Visual Arts Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title : Lecturer - Illustration FTE: .225 per 3 credit course Salary Range : $5,371.19 per 3 credit course Position #00608146 \u2013 Requisition #41295 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * At the College of Arts & Media (CAM), we empower a diverse community of makers, scholars, and innovators to thrive in the rapidly evolving creative industries. Through a dynamic blend of critical inquiry, creative exploration, and real-world engagement, CAM prepares students for lives filled with opportunity, meaning, and purpose. Rooted in community and driven by a spirit of intellectual and artistic freedom, CAM embraces risk-takers, visionaries, and cultural disruptors by providing access to cutting-edge technology, global perspectives, and a nurturing environment where bold ideas flourish. CAM offers top-ranked degrees and programs in Film & Television, Media Forensics, Music & Entertainment, and Visual Arts. In Visual Arts at CU Denver, the city becomes our canvas, industry leaders become professors and a passion becomes a profession. We do our best work designing in a digital lab or putting paint to canvas in a studio. Our students have access to state-of-the art digital labs, sculpture studios, industrial equipment and darkrooms. They find opportunities at the Denver Art Museum, in galleries across the Front Range and at digital studios like Pixar. That\u2019s how the College of Arts & Media unites the ability to create with the means to succeed. Illustration at CU Denver has been recognized by Animation Career Review as a top national program. Traditional, conceptual, and technology-based education combine for dynamic course work that includes Image Making, Digital Illustration, Print Media, Investigative Methods, Digital Painting, Graphic Novel Workshop, Business of Art, and Typography. Illustration faculty prepare students for passionate successful careers in visual art, design, and illustration. Lecturer appointments are at-will and teaching assignments are determined on a semester by semester basis. Teaching assignments may fluctuate and are contingent upon the schedule of courses offered each term. Lecturer - Illustration What you will do: 100% Teaching Teaching Load: You will teach one or two classes per semester (3-6 credit hours) Instruction: Your focus will include one or more of the following areas- Illustration I: Image Making, Illustration II: Digital Media, Illustration III: Investigative Methods, Illustration IV: Thesis Development, Illustration V: BFA Thesis, Drawing 1, Life Drawing 1, Printed Image, Life Drawing 2: Portraiture & Anatomy, Life Painting and Drawing, Painting I, Media of Drawing, Drawing for Story, Digital Painting, Graphic Novel, Concept Art, Business of Art Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. BFA in Illustration, Animation, Games or a related field. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) MFA in Illustration. Three (3) years professional experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong drawing & painting skills including perspective & anatomy. Expertise in a specialization like Children\u2019s Books, Comics, Concept Art, Animation, Game Art, Tattooing or similar. Strong interpersonal and communication skills across multiple teaching modalities. Demonstrated history of building and maintaining effective working relationships with colleagues, students, and community partners representing a wide range of perspectives. Ability to work autonomously, taking initiative on tasks, and meeting deadlines. Outwardly contribute to a respectful, positive, and professional workspace. Interest in emerging trends and technologies in illustration education and practice. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,371.19 per 3 credit course. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training.The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. This position is not eligible for benefits. Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, and interviews begin. Preference will be given to complete applications received by October 14, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: 1. Letter of application specifically addressing the position requirements and outlining qualifications 2. Current CV or r\u00e9sum\u00e9 Questions should be directed to charles.valsechi@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41231&lang=en": {"title": "Midcareer Faculty Success Fellow", "description": "Closing Date: 10/19/2026 Posted Date: Sep 28, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: AVCASA-FAUE FacAffrs/UG Enrich Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Faculty Fellow Working Title: Midcareer Faculty Success Fellow FTE: Part-time Salary Range: $5,000 stipend Position #00853566\u2013 Requisition #41231 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Center for Faculty Development and Advancement (CFDA) invites applications from faculty of all ranks for a Midcareer Faculty Success Fellow position. This fellowship provides an opportunity for a faculty member to collaborate with CFDA in designing, launching, and facilitating a cohort-based Midcareer Faculty Success Program. Midcareer faculty often experience a unique set of opportunities and challenges as they navigate promotion pathways, leadership opportunities, increased service responsibilities, evolving scholarly agendas, and long-term career planning. The Faculty Success Fellow will help create a structured, cohort-based experience (for Spring 2027) that supports faculty in sustaining productivity, enhancing professional fulfillment, building community, and strategically planning the next phase of their academic careers. The Fellow will have substantial autonomy and flexibility to develop programming, pilot innovative initiatives, and design experiences that address the needs of midcareer faculty while partnering closely with CFDA leadership. This position requires an estimated commitment of 5-7 hours per week during the academic year. Midcareer Faculty Success Fellow What you will do: Program Design and Development Collaborate with CFDA to create and implement a cohort-based Midcareer Faculty Success Program. Identify priority topics, goals, and outcomes for participants. Design programming that addresses areas such as: Career planning and goal setting Promotion and advancement Scholarly productivity and impact Workload management and prioritization Work-life integration and well-being Leadership development Navigating institutional culture and influence Building networks and collaborations Mentorship and sponsorship Faculty vitality and long-term career engagement Develop program materials, resources, and learning activities. Cohort Facilitation and Community Building Recruit and support faculty participation in the program. Facilitate cohort meetings, workshops, discussions, and reflective activities. Foster meaningful peer connections and interdisciplinary networking. Create opportunities for faculty to share experiences, strategies, and challenges related to midcareer development. Innovation and Faculty-Led Programming Design and pilot new initiatives that support midcareer faculty success. Develop programming aligned with their own interests, expertise, and identified faculty needs. Explore emerging best practices and current research on faculty development and career advancement. Propose innovative approaches to supporting faculty engagement, productivity, and career satisfaction. Partner with CFDA to translate successful ideas into a sustainable program for midcareer faculty of all ranks. Assessment and Continuous Improvement Develop methods for evaluating program effectiveness and participant outcomes. Collect and analyze participant feedback. Recommend program enhancements and future directions. Assist in documenting program outcomes and institutional impact. Campus Engagement and Outreach Build relationships with faculty, departments, schools, and colleges across campus. Promote participation in the Midcareer Faculty Success Program. Serve as an advocate for faculty development and career advancement. Help identify emerging needs and opportunities for supporting faculty success. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Current faculty appointment at the University of Colorado Denver. Demonstrated commitment to faculty development, mentoring, or academic career advancement. Strong communication, facilitation, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty from a variety of disciplines and career stages. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Experience mentoring faculty or leading faculty development initiatives. Experience facilitating workshops, learning communities, or professional development programs. Experience in faculty leadership roles, such as program director, department chair, committee chair, or similar positions. Interest in faculty well-being, productivity, engagement, and career development. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Passionate about supporting faculty success and professional growth. Bring creativity, initiative, and innovative thinking to program development. Enjoy designing and facilitating engaging learning experiences. Demonstrate strong organizational skills. Value collaboration, inclusion, and community building. Be committed to helping faculty thrive throughout their academic careers. Conditions of Employment This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Current faculty appointment at the University of Colorado Denver. Position will last for one academic year Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at a $5,000 stipend. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is/is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Oct 19, 2026 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to Aubrey Thorburn, AUBREY.THORBURN@UCDENVER.EDU . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41228&lang=en": {"title": "Faculty Mentorship Fellow", "description": "Closing Date: 10/19/2026 Posted Date: Sep 28, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: AVCASA-FAUE FacAffrs/UG Enrich Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Faculty Fellow Working Title: Faculty Mentorship Fellow FTE : Part Time | Hybrid Salary Range: $5,000 stipend Position #00853564\u2013 Requisition #41228 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Center for Faculty Development and Advancement (CFDA) invites applications from faculty of all ranks for a Faculty Mentorship Fellow position. This appointment provides an opportunity for a faculty member to play a leadership role in expanding and strengthening mentoring initiatives across the University of Colorado Denver. The Faculty Mentorship Fellow will partner with CFDA to cultivate a robust culture of mentorship that supports faculty success, belonging, career advancement, and community building. While the Fellow will assist with existing mentorship initiatives, they will also have significant autonomy to develop and implement new mentoring programs, pilot innovative approaches, and help shape the future direction of faculty mentoring at CU Denver. The Fellow will work collaboratively with CFDA leadership while bringing their own expertise, ideas, and creativity to the role. Faculty who are passionate about mentoring and interested in designing meaningful programs that address emerging faculty needs are especially encouraged to apply. This position requires an estimated commitment of 5-7 hours per week during the academic year. Working Faculty Title What you will do : Mentorship Program Development and Innovation Collaborate with CFDA to expand and enhance faculty mentoring initiatives across the university. Assist with the recruitment, matching, and ongoing support of faculty mentors and mentees. Develop resources, tools, and programming that strengthen mentoring strategies, relationships, and outcomes. Identify opportunities for innovation and implement new mentoring strategies that address the evolving needs of faculty. Mentorship Circles Assist in the design, implementation, and assessment of faculty mentorship circles. Develop new mentorship circle models based on faculty interests and institutional priorities. Support and facilitate mentorship circles as needed while creating opportunities for interdisciplinary networking and peer support. Identity-Based Mentoring Initiatives Collaborate with campus partners to develop mentoring opportunities that support faculty from diverse backgrounds, identities, and career experiences. Design and implement identity-based mentoring programs that foster belonging, community, and professional growth. Explore emerging best practices and develop creative approaches to supporting faculty through mentoring networks and communities. Faculty-Led Program Development Propose and develop new mentoring programs aligned with their interests, expertise, and identified faculty needs. Pilot innovative mentoring models and evaluate their effectiveness. Collaborate with CFDA staff to translate ideas into sustainable programs and resources. Serve as a thought partner in shaping the strategic direction of mentoring efforts at CU Denver. Assessment and Continuous Improvement Collect and analyze feedback from mentoring participants. Contribute to program evaluation efforts and recommendations for future growth. Assist in documenting impacts and outcomes of mentoring initiatives. Campus Engagement and Outreach Serve as a champion for mentorship and faculty development. Promote mentoring opportunities across the institution. Build connections with faculty, departments, and campus partners to strengthen mentoring engagement. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Current faculty appointment at the University of Colorado Denver. Demonstrated commitment to faculty development, mentoring, or academic career advancement. Strong communication, facilitation, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty from a variety of disciplines and career stages. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Experience mentoring faculty or leading faculty development initiatives. Experience facilitating workshops, learning communities, or professional development programs. Experience in faculty leadership roles, such as program director, department chair, committee chair, or similar positions. Interest in faculty well-being, productivity, engagement, and career development. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrate a strong commitment to mentoring, faculty success, and community building. Bring creativity, initiative, and a willingness to develop new programs and approaches. Enjoy collaborating with colleagues while also working independently to advance projects. Value innovation and continuous improvement in faculty development. Possess strong interpersonal, organizational, and leadership skills. Be excited by the opportunity to influence mentoring culture and practices across the university. Conditions of Employment This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Current faculty appointment at the University of Colorado Denver. Position will last for one academic year. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at - $5,000 stipend. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is/is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Oct 19, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to Aubrey Thorburn, AUBREY.THORBURN@UCDENVER.EDU. Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41199&lang=en": {"title": "Dean of the Business School", "description": "Posted Date: Sep 23, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCASA/EVCASA Academic&Stdnt Af Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Dean Working Title: Dean of the Business School FTE: Full-time Salary Range: $260,000 - $320,000 Position # 00350380 \u2013 Requisition #41199 About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at Summit Search Solutions- Dean of the Business School - University of Colorado Denver (Denver, CO) * The Dean of the Business School, reporting to the Provost and Executive Vice Chancellor for Academic Affairs, is responsible for serving as the chief academic officer of the school with full responsibility for its academic programs and curricula, the school\u2019s budget, outreach and engagement with the business community, and development activities. In collaboration with the faculty, the Dean will provide intellectual leadership and a strong commitment to the School\u2019s undergraduate and graduate programs. The Dean is expected to increase the school\u2019s resource base by leading fundraising activities for the school, in partnership with an advancement officer. The Dean will also: strengthen engagement of and collaborations with industry and business partners; increase the amount and visibility of scholarship (research/creative work) activity of the faculty; work to promote transformation, innovation and entrepreneurial activities that will prepare the school well for the future; lead the development of strategies to increase enrollments, improve retention and enhance the student experience including internships and other experiential learning activities; foster a climate that demonstrates a commitment to diversity and inclusion; develop a strong alumni network in conjunction with an enhanced focus on job placement; and demonstrate a strong commitment to the university\u2019s urban location while exploring opportunities to engage across Colorado and around the globe. Dean of Business School What you will do: Reporting to the Provost and Executive Vice Chancellor for Academic Affairs, the Dean serves as the chief academic, administrative, and financial officer of the Business School. The Dean provides visionary, collaborative, and entrepreneurial leadership that advances the School's mission and aligns with the university's strategic plan. Working closely with faculty, staff, students, alumni, industry partners, and university leadership, the Dean will strengthen academic excellence, expand the School's impact, foster innovation and entrepreneurship, support research production, and enhance student success and workforce outcomes. Strategic Leadership and Vision Provide bold, collaborative leadership to advance the Business School and position it for long-term success. \u2022 Develop and implement a strategic vision for the Business School that aligns with the university's refreshed strategic plan and reflects the opportunities of a leading urban research university. \u2022 Foster a culture of innovation, adaptability, and continuous improvement in response to emerging trends in business, technology, workforce development, and higher education. \u2022 Partner with faculty, staff, students, alumni, and community stakeholders to identify priorities and achieve measurable outcomes. \u2022 Collaborate with the Provost, Deans, and campus leaders to advance institution-wide goals and initiatives. \u2022 Serve as the chief advocate and ambassador for the Business School locally, statewide, nationally, and globally. Academic Excellence, Research, Innovation, and Entrepreneurship Advance excellence in teaching, scholarship, innovation, and entrepreneurial thinking across all programs. \u2022 Provide intellectual leadership for undergraduate, graduate, executive, and professional education programs. \u2022 Support faculty excellence in teaching, research, creative work, and community-engaged scholarship. \u2022 Increase the visibility, impact, and external funding of faculty scholarship and research. \u2022 Promote interdisciplinary collaboration and partnerships that address complex business and societal challenges. \u2022 Strengthen innovation, entrepreneurship, and experiential learning throughout the curriculum and co-curricular experience. \u2022 Ensure successful maintenance and continuous improvement of AACSB accreditation and academic quality standards. \u2022 Position the School as a leader in emerging areas such as artificial intelligence, data analytics, digital transformation, sustainability, and entrepreneurial innovation. Student Success and Career Outcomes Champion a student-centered culture that promotes access, success, belonging, and career readiness. \u2022 Lead strategies that increase enrollment, persistence, retention, graduation, and post-graduation success. \u2022 Enhance the student experience through high-impact practices, experiential learning, internships, applied projects, and global learning opportunities. \u2022 Strengthen pathways that support student achievement and social mobility. \u2022 Expand partnerships that create employment opportunities, career preparation, and professional mentorship. \u2022 Foster an inclusive learning environment where all students can thrive and achieve their educational goals. \u2022 Utilize data-informed decisionsto support enrollment management, student success, and program effectiveness. Partnerships, Advancement, and External Engagement Cultivate relationships that advance the School's reputation, impact, and resource base. \u2022 Build and strengthen strategic partnerships with business, industry, government, nonprofit, and community organizations. \u2022 Expand collaborations that support internships, workforce development, sponsored research, innovation, and entrepreneurship. \u2022 Lead fundraising efforts in partnership with University Advancement to secure philanthropic support and strategic investments. \u2022 Engage alumni as ambassadors, mentors, advisors, employers, and donors. \u2022 Enhance the visibility and reputation of the Business School through thought leadership and engagement with external stakeholders. \u2022 Leverage the university's urban location to create meaningful regional, statewide, national, and global partnerships. Organizational, Financial, and People Leadership Lead with transparency, collaboration, accountability, and a commitment to shared governance. \u2022 Oversee the School's budget, personnel, facilities, and resources to ensure long-term fiscal sustainability. \u2022 Recruit, retain, develop, and support outstanding faculty and staff. \u2022 Support department chairs and program directors in achieving academic and strategic goals. \u2022 Foster a culture of collaboration, accountability, trust, shared governance, and mutual respect. \u2022 Promote excellence through clear expectations, assessment, and continuous improvement. \u2022 Advance a welcoming and inclusive environment that values diverse perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds. \u2022 Meet established goals and performance expectations while ensuring responsible stewardship of university resources. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. \u2022 Earned terminal degree in a discipline relevant to the Business School's academic programs. \u2022 Record of transformative leadership demonstrating the ability to develop and execute strategic priorities, lead organizational change, and achieve measurable results. \u2022 Evidence of success building partnerships with industry, government, nonprofit, and community organizations. \u2022 Demonstrated ability to secure resources through fundraising, external partnerships, sponsored programs, or other revenue-generating activities. \u2022 Proven ability to lead collaboratively and effectively in complex organizations. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) \u2022 Successful senior leadership experience at a research university, business school, or comparable complex organization. \u2022 Demonstrated record of advancing innovation, entrepreneurship, and interdisciplinary collaboration. \u2022 Experience leading initiatives that improve student success, enrollment growth, retention, and career outcomes. \u2022 Record of advancing inclusive excellence and fostering environments where diverse communities thrive. \u2022 Understanding of the evolving landscape of business education, including technology-enabled learning, AI, workforce partnerships, and emerging business disciplines. \u2022 Experience with strategic planning, accreditation, and organizational transformation. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities \u2022 A strong record of thought leadership and influence in business; credibility with business and government leaders as an innovator in business practice and education; and strong mentorship; \u2022 Exceptional visionary and strategic thinking and leadership skills; \u2022 A record of successful engagement with the business community; \u2022 Excellence in leading, evaluating, recruiting and analyzing; \u2022 Demonstrated management and administrative ability; \u2022 Effectiveness as a fundraiser, networker and strategic alliance-builder; \u2022 A commitment to diversity and inclusion; \u2022 Successful experience and/or strong potential for success building and/or enhancing strong programs of corporate sponsorships, funded research, and other mission-aligned revenue generation; \u2022 Success in establishing mutually beneficial relationships with external constituents such as, but not limited to, alumni, government, and accrediting bodies; \u2022 Excellent oral and written communication skills; \u2022 The ability to build and work with teams up and across the organization; \u2022 Demonstrable accomplishments in working with business-related constituencies that will bridge to a university setting; \u2022 A strong record demonstrating a broad working knowledge of innovation and accomplishment, entrepreneurship and technology application in business at the local, state, national and international levels; \u2022 Experience with CRM systems and data driven decision making that will translate to enrollment and marketing; \u2022 Ability to lead the development of strategies to increase enrollments, improve retention and enhance the student experience including internships and experiential learning activities. Conditions of Employment \u2022 Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. \u2022 This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. \u2022 This position is for a three-year appointment. A review will be conducted during the third year to determine reappointment. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements \u2022 The ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $260,000 - $320,000. For candidates considering a move, relocation assistance may be available. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by October 10, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: Summit Search Solutions- Dean of the Business School - University of Colorado Denver (Denver, CO) and attach: \u2022 A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications \u2022 A current CV/resume \u2022 List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Lyndi Hewitt, lhewitt@summitsearchsolutions.com Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41193&lang=en": {"title": "Dean, School of Public Affairs", "description": "Posted Date: Sep 23, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCASA/EVCASA Academic&Stdnt Af Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Dean Working Title: Dean, School of Public Affairs FTE: Full Time 1.0 FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: $235,000 - $275,000 Position #00611800\u2013 Requisition #41193 Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at: https://www.imsearch.com/open-searches/university-colorado-denver-school-public-affairs/dean Dean, School of Public Affairs Strategic Leadership and Vision Provide bold, collaborative leadership to advance the School of Public Affairs and position it for long-term success. \u2022 Develop and implement a strategic vision for the School of Public Affairs that aligns with the university's refreshed strategic plan and reflects the opportunities of a leading urban research university. \u2022 Foster a culture of innovation, adaptability, and continuous improvement in response to emerging issues in public policy, public administration, social equity, governance, nonprofit leadership, criminal justice, public finance, and civic engagement. \u2022 Partner with faculty, staff, students, alumni, and community stakeholders to identify priorities and achieve measurable outcomes. \u2022 Collaborate with the Provost, Deans, and campus leaders to advance institution-wide goals and initiatives. \u2022 Serve as the chief advocate and ambassador for the School of Public Affairs locally, statewide, nationally, and globally. \u2022 Position the School as a thought leader in addressing complex public challenges facing cities, states, nations, and communities. Academic Excellence, Research, and Public Impact Advance excellence in teaching, scholarship, policy engagement, and public service. \u2022 Provide intellectual leadership for undergraduate, graduate, and professional education programs. \u2022 Support faculty excellence in teaching, research, creative work, policy engagement, and community-engaged scholarship. \u2022 Increase the visibility, impact, and external funding of faculty scholarship and research. \u2022 Promote interdisciplinary collaboration and partnerships that address pressing public challenges and inform public decision-making. \u2022 Support applied research, policy analysis, and evidence-based solutions that contribute to the public good. \u2022 Ensure successful maintenance and continuous improvement of NASPAA accreditation and academic quality standards. \u2022 Strengthen the School's national reputation and ranking as a leading school of public affairs. \u2022 Advance scholarship and educational programs in areas such as public policy, public administration, nonprofit management, criminal justice, public budgeting and finance, sustainability, governance, technology and society, public health policy, and social equity. \u2022 Foster partnerships among faculty, research centers, policymakers, and practitioners to translate knowledge into action and public impact. Student Success and Leadership Development Champion a student-centered culture that promotes access, success, belonging, and preparation for public leadership. \u2022 Lead strategies that increase enrollment, persistence, retention, graduation, and post-graduation success. \u2022 Prepare students for impactful careers across government, nonprofit, philanthropic, international, and public-serving organizations. \u2022 Enhance the student experience through experiential learning, internships, capstone projects, community-engaged learning, and public service opportunities. \u2022 Strengthen pathways that support student achievement, leadership development, and social mobility. \u2022 Expand partnerships that create employment opportunities, policy fellowships, public service experiences, and professional mentorship. \u2022 Foster an inclusive learning environment where all students can thrive and achieve their educational goals. \u2022 Utilize data-informed decisions to support enrollment management, student success, and program effectiveness. \u2022 Promote civic engagement, ethical leadership, and a lifelong commitment to public service. Partnerships, Advancement, and External Engagement Cultivate relationships that advance the School's reputation, impact, and resource base. \u2022 Build and strengthen strategic partnerships with local, state, federal, and international government agencies; nonprofit organizations; philanthropic foundations; community organizations; and private-sector partners. \u2022 Expand collaborations that support research, policy innovation, experiential learning, workforce development, and community impact. \u2022 Serve as a visible and trusted leader in policy, civic, and community conversations that advance the public good. \u2022 Lead fundraising efforts in partnership with University Advancement to secure philanthropic support and strategic investments. \u2022 Engage alumni as ambassadors, mentors, advisors, practitioners, and donors. \u2022 Enhance the visibility and reputation of the School through thought leadership, public engagement, and professional association involvement. \u2022 Leverage the university's urban location and proximity to the seat of state government to create meaningful regional, statewide, national, and global partnerships. \u2022 Support executive education, professional development, and community-facing programs that serve public sector and nonprofit leaders. Organizational, Financial, and People Leadership Lead with transparency, collaboration, accountability, and a commitment to shared governance. \u2022 Oversee the School's budget, personnel, facilities, and resources to ensure long-term fiscal sustainability. \u2022 Recruit, retain, develop, and support outstanding faculty and staff. \u2022 Support center directors and program leaders in achieving academic, research, and strategic goals. \u2022 Foster a culture of collaboration, accountability, trust, shared governance, and mutual respect. \u2022 Promote excellence through clear expectations, assessment, and continuous improvement. \u2022 Advance a welcoming and inclusive environment that values diverse perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds. \u2022 Support faculty and staff development while fostering a culture of engagement, innovation, and high performance. \u2022 Meet established goals and performance expectations while ensuring responsible stewardship of university resources. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. \u2022 A terminal degree in a relevant discipline offered by the School of Public Affairs, from an accredited institution. \u2022 Record of transformative leadership demonstrating the ability to develop and execute strategic priorities, lead organizational change, and achieve measurable results. \u2022 Evidence of success building partnerships with government, nonprofit, and community organizations. \u2022 Demonstrated ability to successfully secure resources through fundraising, external partnerships, sponsored programs, or other revenue-generating activities. \u2022 Proven ability to lead collaboratively and effectively in complex organizations. \u2022 Substantial financial management experience, including the equitable allocation of resources across multiple programs and initiatives, and supporting innovation around new degrees, certificates, or other revenue generators. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) \u2022 Successful senior leadership experience at a research university, school of public affairs, or comparable complex organization. \u2022 Demonstrated record of advancing innovation and interdisciplinary collaboration. \u2022 Experience leading initiatives that improve student success, enrollment growth, retention, and career outcomes. \u2022 An innovative, intellectually engaged leader who makes difficult decisions with reflection, fairness, and transparency and is willing to challenge the status quo to guide the college to further prominence locally, nationally, and internationally. \u2022 A clear, transparent, empathetic, and empowering communication style; an openness to listening and integrating the input of others; an ability to advocate for the college's priorities; an ability to convey the mission, vision, and impact of the college and university to both internal and external audiences; and the capacity to serve as a thought leader within Colorado and beyond. \u2022 A champion for inclusive excellence, access and campus engagement with exemplary skills in communicating, collaborating with, and supporting a diverse community, removing barriers to inclusion, promoting student voice, and valuing student agency. \u2022 Ability to foster a deep sense of community both internally at the college and externally with partners; desire to listen and learn and to serve as a visible and positive presence at the school and on campus; and ability to foster a culture and community where kindness, humility, and respect are high priorities. \u2022 A relationship-based leadership style that values teamwork and collaboration; a firm belief in shared governance and a high level of collegiality in working with faculty, staff, and students; experience bringing people together to solve challenges and seize opportunities; ability to delegate; respect and appreciation for all of the disciplines of the college; and experience facilitating strong partnerships among academic programs and other divisions of the university. \u2022 A leadership style that demonstrates accountability, integrity, compassion, empathy, kindness, humility, curiosity, enthusiasm, humor, flexibility, forward-thinking, good judgment, and discernment. \u2022 A deep appreciation for research and scholarly endeavors, a record of recruiting and developing both people and programs of the highest quality. \u2022 Successful experience in or a demonstrated capacity for fundraising; an eagerness to build relationships with donors, alumni, and community partnerships to help advance the mission of SPA. \u2022 Familiarity with the issues and opportunities across a range of academic areas and a natural curiosity about a broad range of intellectual endeavors, including those represented throughout the college\u2019s programs. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities \u2022 Credibility with community and government leaders as a thought leader and innovator in industry practice and education Exceptional visionary and strategic thinking and leadership skills. \u2022 Excellence in leading, evaluating, recruiting and analyzing. \u2022 Demonstrated management and administrative ability. \u2022 Effectiveness as a fundraiser, networker and strategic alliance-builder. \u2022 Strong, demonstrated commitment and accomplishment in inclusive excellence, access and campus engagement. \u2022 Successful experience and/or strong potential for success building and/or enhancing strong programs of corporate sponsorships, funded research, and other mission-aligned revenue generation. \u2022 Success in establishing mutually beneficial relationships with internal and external constituents such as, but not limited to, alumni, government, and accrediting bodies. \u2022 Excellent oral and written communication skills. \u2022 The ability to build and work with teams up and across the organization. \u2022 The ability to resolve conflict in a positive manner. \u2022 Demonstrable accomplishments in working with a variety of teams, groups, and leaders that will bridge to a university setting. \u2022 Experience with data driven decision making that translates to enrollment and marketing. \u2022 Ability to lead the development of strategies to increase enrollments, improve retention and enhance the student experience including internships and experiential learning activities. Conditions of Employment \u2022 Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. \u2022 This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. \u2022 This position is for a three-year appointment. A review will be conducted during the third year to determine reappointment. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements \u2022 The ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $235,000 - $275,000 The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline \u2022 Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, and interviews begin. Preference will be given to complete applications received by October 5th, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: https://www.imsearch.com/open-searches/university-colorado-denver-school-public-affairs/dean Questions should be directed to Janette Martinez, jmartinez@imsearch.com Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41101&lang=en": {"title": "Assistant Professor", "description": "Posted Date: Sep 15, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CEDC-Computer SC & Engineering Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Assistant Professor Working Title: Assistant Professor FTE: Full-time Salary Range: $90,000 - $125,000 Position #00636050\u2013 Requisition #41101 About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Computer Science and Engineering Department (CSE) currently has sixteen full-time faculty members. The department offers a ABET accredited Bachelor of Science degree in Computer Science, a Bachelor of Arts degree in Computer Science, a Bachelor of Science degree in Cybersecurity, a Master of Science degree in Computer Science, and two multidisciplinary PhD degrees in Computer Science and Information Systems and Engineering and Applied Science, and several certificates. The CSE department provides quality computer science education and research opportunities to our students and quality professional service to the professional community and the general public in the Denver metropolitan area. The current strengths of the faculty are in the areas of algorithms, artificial intelligence, computer networks, graphics, parallel and distributed systems, mobile systems, machine learning, Cybersecurity and secure computing, data science and AI, and theory. Our faculty are engaged in multidisciplinary research and encourage collaborative research among disciplines. In addition to general computing labs, the department houses several specialized research labs in Next Generation Networking & Security, Cyber-Physical Systems (CPS), Active Cyber Infrastructure and Defense (ACID), Machine Learning (ML), networks (DECENT), Big Data Management & Mining Laboratory (BDLab), Animation, Neuroscience & AI, and parallel and distributed systems (PDS). The College of Engineering, Design and Computing values innovation, creativity and an interdisciplinary approach to engineering and research. We focus on providing our students with a comprehensive engineering education at the undergraduate, graduate and professional level. Faculty conduct research that spans our five disciplines of civil, electrical and mechanical engineering, bioengineering, and computer science and engineering. The college collaborates with industry from around the state; our laboratories and research opportunities give students the hands-on experience they need to excel in the professional world. Assistant Professor What you will do: The Department of Computer Science and Engineering in the College of Engineering, Design and Computing at the University of Colorado Denver invites applications for Assistant Professor. Reporting to the Chair of the Computer Science and Engineering Department, these positions will be expected to develop and teach lecture and laboratory courses at all levels; establish an active externally funded research program; conduct high quality research involving students at all levels, leading to sponsored research and refereed publications; advise students; and contribute to Department, College, and University governance and to the profession. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. \u2022 Ph.D. in Computer Science or closely related field. \u2022 Demonstrated expertise and track record of research and teaching accomplishments commensurate with the candidate\u2019s rank in computer science, as evidenced by their record. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) \u2022 While candidates in all areas of computer science will be considered, the areas of AI, Quantum Computing (including Quantum Machine Learning), Health Informatics and Technologies, Intelligent Systems, Cybersecurity, Edge Computing, Computer Vision and Cyber-Physical Systems, and/or a related field will be given priority. Conditions of Employment \u2022 These positions may follow a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preference. Working from the office is required for teaching, student interactions, committee work, and other responsibilities. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements \u2022 These positions may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. \u2022 These positions may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position may be eligible now and in the future for certain visa sponsorship limited to Change of Status (COS) within the United States or if the candidate meets the criteria for the portability provision. While the hiring unit may be willing to pursue certain visa sponsorship, an offer of employment will be contingent on the candidate having a visa status that allows employment with the University as of the start date for the position or the University\u2019s petition being approved and on the candidate being able to obtain the appropriate visa status. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at: $90,000 - $125,000. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline \u2022 Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, and interviews begin. Preference will be given to complete applications received by November 27, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: \u2022 Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). \u2022 One (1) PDF containing the following documents combined (may not exceed 2.5 megabytes): o A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. o Statement of teaching philosophy, experience, and interests (3-page limit). o Statement of research philosophy, experience, and interests (3-page limit). o List of three professional references including name, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting references). Questions should be directed to Kelly Konrad, kelly.p.konrad@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41049&lang=en": {"title": "Academic Services and CPE Program Coordinator", "description": "Posted Date: Sep 9, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SEHD DEAN Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Academic Services Senior Professional Working Title: Academic Services and CPE Program Coordinator FTE: Full-time Salary Range: $54,256 - $59,968 Position #00649345\u2013 Requisition #41049 About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * Jobs in this career family provide direct professional support for the teaching and/or educational service mission of the university. Functions include academic advising/counseling, student personnel administration, recruitment and admissions, registration, financial aid, faculty affairs, library services, curriculum administration, and others involving direct support of the educational mission of an academic unit. The School of Education and Human Development (SEHD) and its Academic Services and Continuing & Professional Education Offices are committed to recruiting and retaining a diverse student body. Nature of Work The Academic Services and CPE Program Coordinator is a shared position between the Academic Services department and the Continuing & Professional Education (CPE) office in the School of Education and Human Development. In Academic Services this position manages admissions, course planning, registration and enrollment, student services, progress tracking, and graduation certification for graduate programs. CPE is an entrepreneurial unit that offers a wide range of self-funded courses and programs for working teachers and other education professionals, as well as for adults preparing for careers in education, mental health or supporting educational enterprises. This position will work with districts and partner organizations to provide student advising and program support, and will manage the implementation of both degree and non-degree programs. Additionally, the Coordinator provides administrative support to faculty, students, and staff. Academic Services and CPE Program Coordinator What you will do: Recruitment and Admissions \u2022 Provides proactive, personalized, and integrated engagement to prospective students, primarily through phone and digital outreach, in a fast-paced environment, with a focus on connecting potential students to appropriate academic and student support resources. \u2022 Recruit, follow-up, and facilitate admission for students, from initial inquiry through enrollment, including students in partnership-based cohort programs. \u2022 Help students understand their estimated cost of attendance and financial aid and scholarship opportunities. \u2022 Coordinate, plan and participate in information sessions, recruitment activities, interview days, orientations, etc. \u2022 Provide oversight and advisement of applicants on admission requirements and support prospective students through the online application system. \u2022 Provide wrap-around services which include support related to financial aid, student services, and academic resources available on campus. \u2022 Facilitate the processing of applications by managing communication, materials and eligibility criteria; provides timely feedback regarding the status of applications. \u2022 Verifies transcript information, such as credits, cumulative GPA, and awarded degrees. \u2022 Tracks new student acceptance and update the student listservs. Program Coordination \u2022 Maintains a detailed multi-year course schedule to ensure students can complete their requirements. \u2022 Coordinates and communicates important deadlines. \u2022 Helps students and faculty navigate multiple academic calendars, policies and platforms. \u2022 Distributes registration information to students each term appropriate for their cohort/concentration/program of study. \u2022 Maintains confidential academic records, uploads data into student information systems, and uses advising and reporting tools to ensure accuracy. \u2022 Tracks student progress for retention. \u2022 Oversees the processes related to leaves of absence, program discontinuation, transfers, withdrawals, and academic probation for students. \u2022 Perform graduation audits when students apply to graduate and certify graduation. \u2022 Track and determine student completion of certificate and degree programs, and assist with efforts to recruit continuing and professional education non-degree students into degree programs. \u2022 Processes student forms and routes as necessary to campus administrative offices. \u2022 Supports students as they navigate the administrative aspects of the enrollment process, including those connected to admissions, financial aid, registration, and bursar functions. \u2022 Supports in-person and virtual activities; assists with catering, vendor arrangements, event and program logistics. \u2022 Assists with all university-wide commencement preparations and day-of activities. \u2022 Ensures student handbooks are updated annually and posted to the SEHD website and distributed to faculty and students. \u2022 Coordinate program activities, to include communication with program faculty, program oversight team, partner organization representatives/design team, student services, and CPE to ensure timely and efficient registration, evaluation, grading, and billing for the CPE programs. \u2022 Manage graduate faculty appointment process for CPE lecturers. \u2022 Work with instructors and program leaders to ensure that course and instructor documentation is current and accurate; that required processes, such as course evaluations and grades are completed; and that courses are scheduled according to required university timelines. Administration \u2022 Maintains files on current students including program of study, progress to degree, and other documentation related to student progress. \u2022 Maintains contact information for prospects, current students, and alumni. \u2022 Collaborates and liaises with faculty. \u2022 Organize team meetings, shared calendars, activities, and retreats. \u2022 Reviews website material related to programs to identify areas in need of revision or update. \u2022 Responsible for other duties as assigned. This description is a summary only and describes the general level of work being performed; it is not intended to be all-inclusive. The duties of this position may change from time to time based on business needs. We reserve the right to add or delete duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the supervisor and/or hiring authority. Primary work hours are 8:00AM \u2013 5:00PM Monday-Friday, and some evening/weekend activities may be required. The primary work location is the CU Denver campus, but some partial remote work options are available. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. \u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree from an accredited institution of higher education. \u2022 One (1) year of experience working in higher education in either recruitment, admissions, advising, financial aid, or student support services. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor\u2019s degree on a year-for-year basis. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) \u2022 Master\u2019s degree from an accredited college or university in education in student affairs, or related field is highly desired. \u2022 Two years of extensive, diverse and progressively responsible experience, including direct responsibility for program coordination and management. \u2022 Proficient in Microsoft Office, Zoom, Slate, student information systems, and other platforms. Competencies \u2022 Demonstrated initiative and ability to work as part of a team. \u2022 Exceptional customer service skills \u2022 Able to communicate well and build rapport quickly with students, faculty, and staff. \u2022 Ability to work independently and with interdepartmental teams on various initiatives. \u2022 Excellent organization and time management skills, including the ability to set and meet goals and deadlines, manage appointments, create schedules, coordinate and facilitate meetings, and make decisions. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $54,256 - $59,968. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by September 24th, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: \u2022 A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications \u2022 A current CV/resume \u2022 List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to SEHD HR at sehdhr@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41047&lang=en": {"title": "Crisis Counseling Manager", "description": "Posted Date: Sep 9, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCSSLS-HWAS Stdnt&CommCounslng Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Health Care Manager Working Title: Crisis Counseling Manager FTE: Full-time Salary Range: $84,206 - $93,070 Position #00691789 \u2013 Requisition #41047 About the University of Colorado - Denver The University of Colorado Denver is the state\u2019s premier public urban research university and equity-serving institution. Globally connected and locally invested, CU Denver partners with future-focused learners and communities to design accessible, relevant, transformative educational experiences for every stage of life and career. Across seven schools and colleges in the heart of downtown Denver, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges through break through innovations and impactful research, and creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. For more information, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Crisis Counseling Manager is a licensed mental health professional within the CU Denver Student and Community Counseling Center and reports to the Assistant Director at the Counseling Center. This position provides leadership for the Counseling Center's crisis services program and is responsible for ensuring timely, coordinated, and effective responses to students experiencing acute mental health concerns and elevated levels of risk. The Crisis Counseling Manager oversees the assessment, triage, case coordination, and follow-up of high-risk students while maintaining continuity of care across university and community systems. This role collaborates closely with campus partners including Disability Resources and Services, Student Conduct and Community Standards, the Office of Case Management, faculty, International Student Services, the Ombuds Office, Auraria Health Center, and other stakeholders to support student wellbeing and safety. The Crisis Counseling Manager develops and maintains crisis response protocols, risk management procedures, referral pathways, and systems for tracking and coordinating care for students identified as high risk. The position facilitates transitions to higher levels of care when student needs exceed the Counseling Center's scope of practice and supports successful reintegration to campus following hospitalization, medical leave, or other significant mental health events. The Crisis Counseling Manager provides consultation to students, families, faculty, staff, administrators, and community providers regarding complex mental health concerns and crisis response. In addition to program leadership responsibilities, the Crisis Counseling Manager provides culturally responsive clinical services, including crisis intervention, brief individual counseling, group counseling, case management, intake assessment, consultation, outreach, and prevention programming. The position also develops and delivers training and educational programs for campus stakeholders regarding student mental health, crisis response, and wellbeing promotion. The Crisis Counseling Manager supervises crisis counseling staff, contributes to the training and development of clinical trainees, and participates in departmental meetings, university committees, and collaborative initiatives that support student success and wellbeing. Based on a total of 100% of time, this position will be responsible for approximately: 40% Coordination of Crisis Services 30% Counseling Services (includes on-call) 10% Administrative (e.g., staff meeting, team meeting, trainee review, high-risk) 15% supervision and practicum student training 5% outreach and prevention services Crisis Counseling Manager What you will do: \u2022 Lead and coordinate the Counseling Center's crisis services program, including policy and procedure development, service design, workflow management, staffing plans, clinician coverage, and continuous quality improvement initiatives. \u2022 Provide clinical and administrative supervision, performance management, consultation, and professional development for crisis counseling staff. \u2022 Oversee training activities related to crisis counseling for clinical staff, trainees, and practicum students. \u2022 Provide drop-in crisis assessment and intervention services; coordinate care for students experiencing acute distress through consultation, case management, collaboration with campus partners, and referral to community resources when appropriate. \u2022 Develop and maintain systems for triage, referral management, case tracking, documentation, and follow-up of students identified as high risk. \u2022 Consult with students, families, faculty, staff, administrators, and community providers regarding complex mental health concerns, crisis response, hospitalization follow-up, and return-to-campus planning. \u2022 Provide culturally responsive brief counseling, crisis intervention, group counseling, case management, and outreach services to a diverse student population. \u2022 Monitor and evaluate crisis services utilization, outcomes, and operational effectiveness; use data to inform program improvements and resource planning. \u2022 Represent the Counseling Center on multidisciplinary teams addressing students of concern, behavioral risk, and university crisis response efforts. \u2022 Participate in recruitment, hiring, onboarding, and training of crisis services staff. \u2022 Develop and deliver trainings, workshops, and consultations for campus stakeholders on mental health, crisis response, and student wellbeing; participate in departmental meetings, committees, and outreach initiatives. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) \u2022 Master\u2019s degree in counseling-related field from an accredited institution. \u2022 Licensure as mental health professional in Colorado (LPC, LMFT, LCSW). \u2022 At least three (3) years of related professional level experience Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) \u2022 Experience with crisis management, including assessment, intervention, stabilization, and disposition planning. \u2022 Experience coordinating care for individuals requiring involuntary mental health evaluation, hospitalization, or higher levels of care, including related assessment, consultation, coordination, and documentation. \u2022 History of work in acute settings, such as crisis phone lines, hospital settings, behavioral health/primary care, inpatient treatment facilities, drop-in crisis centers, crisis stabilization units, etc. \u2022 Experience providing clinical supervision, consultation, or support to mental health professionals and trainees. \u2022 Experience coordinating, developing, or managing clinical programs or services. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities \u2022 Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. \u2022 Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships across the institution. \u2022 Demonstrated commitment to equitable, inclusive, and culturally responsive clinical practice. \u2022 Ability to provide culturally responsive crisis intervention and brief therapy to a diverse student population. \u2022 Ability to assess, manage, and respond effectively to students experiencing acute mental health crises. \u2022 Ability to conduct suicide, homicide, and behavioral threat risk assessments. \u2022 Ability to provide rapid assessment, triage, stabilization, and referral services in a fast-paced clinical environment. \u2022 Ability to collaborate effectively within a multidisciplinary treatment team. \u2022 Ability to consult with campus and community partners regarding students of concern. \u2022 Ability to coordinate care across campus and community systems. \u2022 Ability to provide clinical and operational leadership for a crisis services program, including team coordination, workflow management, staff support, program development, and continuous quality improvement. Conditions of Employment \u2022 Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. \u2022 This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements \u2022 This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $84,206 - $93,070. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by priority deadline of September 27th, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: \u2022 A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications \u2022 A current CV/resume \u2022 List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Dr. Matthew Heermann, matthew.heermann@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41040&lang=en": {"title": "Lecturer", "description": "Closing Date: 12/08/2026 Posted Date: Sep 9, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CLAS-Political Science Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer FTE : Part-time Salary Range: The starting salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established as $1,704 per credit hour (undergraduate level), or $1,849 per credit hour (graduate level). Position #00007258\u2013 Requisition #41040 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top ranked bachelors, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * This posting will establish and maintain a pool of part-time lecturers with experience teaching Political Science courses in designated fields of the discipline, which may include specializations in areas such as Area Studies, American Political Thought, Research Methodology, Constitutional Law, Environmental Politics, Labor, Social Economy, Local Government Leadership, Community Organizing/Development, and courses within their area of expertise, for the Department of Political Science in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at the University of Colorado Denver. The Center for New Directions in Politics & Policy is within the Department of Political Science and manages an applied Master's Degree and several undergraduate and graduate certificates, delivered primarily through weekend intensive in-person graduate courses. New Directions will also hire lecturers from this pool of applicants. By submitting your application, you will become part of an applicant pool. Candidates hired from this pool will fill temporary, non-tenure track positions and will teach no more than two courses per semester. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50%) and will be made semester-by-semester, depending on the needs of the department and subject to budgetary approval. Therefore, this posting does not necessarily reflect a current open position. The Department of Political Science will contact you if there is an opening that suits your qualifications. Working Faculty Title What you will do: Teach one or two courses in the Political Science Department. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master\u2019s Degree in political Science or related field. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Discipline related certifications PhD or ABD in Political Science. Experience teaching in a higher education environment in related field to teaching assignment. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Expertise in one or more of the related teaching assignment(s). Ability to communicate in a positive and effective manner, across various modalities. Ability to effectively listen and share relevant information. Ability to establish and respond to, as well as, balance multiple work priorities, follow through, and meet established deadlines. Intentionally contribute to a respectful, equitable, positive, and professional workplace. Commitment to enhancing diversity, equity and inclusion. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Understanding of the needs of a diverse student population. Strong commitment to student education and success. Experience in online or hybrid delivery. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The starting salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established as $1,704 per credit hour (undergraduate level), or $1,849 per credit hour (graduate level). The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [Sept. 9, 2026]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the six\u2011month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Please detail your availability in your letter, including the specific days (Monday-Friday, weekends) and times (daytime or evening) you are able to teach. Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to Kayla Spencer, kayla.spencer@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=37723&lang=en": {"title": "Substance Use Disorder Treatment Counselor (Entry \u2013 Senior Level)", "description": "Posted Date: Sep 9, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SOM-PSYCH-ARTS SP/G Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus School of Medicine | Department of Psychiatry | Addiction Research & Treatment Services (ARTS) | Adult Outpatient Program Job Title: Substance Use Disorder Treatment Counselor (Entry \u2013 Senior Level) Position: #00730526 \u2013 Requisition: #37723 Job Summary: The Substance Use Disorder (SUD) Treatment Counselor provides drug and alcohol assessment, psychosocial, and pharmacological treatment to adults who are living with SUD. This clinical position is responsible for performing counseling duties and will be supervised by a senior counselor, a Clinical Team Lead, and/or the Clinic Manager. This position will primarily work with patients who are participating in Medication Assisted Treatment (MAT), referred from criminal justice programs, recovery courts, probation departments, and/or other referral sources (i.e. department of social services). This position is required to share on-call and Saturday coverage duties. Evening hours may be necessary as well. Some positions are morning shifts (6:00am-2:30pm) and others may be day/afternoon shifts (10:30am-7:00pm). Key Responsibilities: Provide assessments of clients for admission to treatment. Perform SUD evaluations. Complete patient intakes (new, returning, internal transfer, external transfer, etc.). Perform group, individual and family counseling. Use evidence-based practices for treating offenders and criminal-justice involved populations. Maintain accurate and timely documentation in patient charts. Develop and carry out individualized treatment plans and case management duties as needed to meet the needs of external sources as well as linking client's treatment progress to referral sources. Complete monthly billing report and statistics. Assess and collect fees from clients. Staff on-call shift rotations. Coverage of clinic front desk as needed. Work closely with problem solving courts, the Veterans Administration, Department of Social Services/Human Services, and/or other referral sources. Performing other work as assigned or required. Work Location: Onsite \u2013 this role is expected to work onsite at Adult Outpatient Clinics or the ARTS Medication Mobile Unit across the greater Metro Denver area. Why Join Us: Adult Outpatient Clinics for CU\u2019s ARTS team are leading the fight against substance use disorder (SUD) in the state. We have several clinics across the greater Metro Denver area including in Arvada, central Denver, and Aurora. Additionally, we have a new Medication Mobile Unit which delivers medication assisted treatments to the patients of our city. We are hiring across all locations. Joining this team not only sets you up for a long-term career within the university but also makes a lasting impact in our community. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation, and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 10/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Entry Level: Bachelor's degree in psychology, social work, counseling, human services, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. A combination of education and/or related technical or professional experience may be substituted for the bachelor\u2019s degree on a year for year basis. Possess a valid registration in good standing with the Colorado Department of Regulatory Agencies (DORA) as a Certified Addictions Specialist (CAS), Licensed Professional Counselor Candidate (LPC-C), Social Worker Candidate (SW-C), Licensed Addiction Counselor Candidate (LAC-C), or Marriage and Family Therapist Candidate (MFT-C). Intermediate Level: Bachelor's degree in psychology, social work, counseling, human services, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. A combination of education and/or related technical or professional experience may be substituted for the bachelor\u2019s degree on a year for year basis. One (1) year of professional level experience in Mental Health, Behavioral Health or closely related field, case management, research of Mental Health, Behavioral Health, or closely related field. Possess a valid registration in good standing with the Colorado Department of Regulatory Agencies (DORA) as a Certified Addictions Specialist (CAS), Licensed Professional Counselor Candidate (LPC-C), Social Worker Candidate (SW-C), Licensed Addiction Counselor Candidate (LAC-C), or Marriage and Family Therapist Candidate (MFT-C). Senior Level: Bachelor's degree in psychology, social work, counseling, human services, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. A combination of education and/or related technical or professional experience may be substituted for the bachelor\u2019s degree on a year for year basis. Two (2) years of professional level experience in Mental Health, Behavioral Health or closely related field, case management, research of Mental Health, Behavioral Health, or closely related field. Possess a valid registration in good standing with the Colorado Department of Regulatory Agencies (DORA) as a Licensed Clinical Social Worker (LCSW), Licensed Social Worker (LSW), Licensed Professional Counselor (LPC), Licensed Marriage and Family Therapist (LMFT) or Licensed Addiction Counselor (LAC). Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in psychology, social work, counseling, human services, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Experience working in a counselor role with clients who are involved with probation, human services, social services, criminal justice programs, and/or other referral sources. Experience conducting, leading, or co-leading group counseling sessions. Experience working in a counselor role with opioid-dependent, adult clients. Experience conducting individual and/or family counseling. Experience creating individualized treatment plans and other clinical documentation (for example, DAP notes). Experience with therapeutic confrontation and structures. Experience observing, monitoring, and intervening in drug/alcohol treatment. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Excellent written communication skills, which includes the ability to check for typographical, grammatical, and spelling errors. Ability to effectively manage difficult behaviors. Ability to engage patients in treatment for substance use disorder treatment. Ability to comply with established rules, policies and procedures and meet deadlines. Ability to be open-minded and nonjudgmental. Ability to develop healthy relationships with clients. Ability to establish boundaries with clients. Ability to exercise discretion (e.g. patient confidentiality). Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Conditions of Employment: Must agree to undertake and successfully pass a fingerprint check. Must agree to undertake and successfully pass a criminal background check, professional references check, and motor vehicle records check. Must possess and maintain current and valid registration in good standing with the Colorado Department of Regulatory Agencies (DORA) to provide behavioral health treatment and care to patients throughout employment in this position. Must possess a valid driver\u2019s license to operate a motor vehicle in Colorado or obtain one within 30 days from date of hire. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. Questions should be directed to: Heidi McKinnon, heidi.mckinnon@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until position is filled. For best consideration, apply by November 30, 2026. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established as: Entry Level: $56,555 \u2013 $71,939 Intermediate Level: $61,546 \u2013 $78,286 Senior Level: $66,536 \u2013 $84,634 The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing non-discrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu \u200b. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students, and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41035&lang=en": {"title": "Instructor - ICB", "description": "Closing Date: 12/31/2026 Posted Date: Sep 9, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CLAS-Communication Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Instructor Working Title: Instructor - ICB FTE: Full-time, 0.9 (90%) FTE | On Site in Bejing, China Salary Range : $54,000 - $56,692 Position #00637374\u2013 Requisition #41035 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top ranked bachelors, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Located in the Haidian District of Beijing, International College Beijing (ICB) is an international partnership between China Agricultural University (CAU) and the University of Colorado Denver that offers complete undergraduate programs in Economics and Communication. All courses are administered and taught by CU Denver faculty in English, and the degree earned is awarded by CU Denver. The ICB program offers a thriving and collegial environment that strives to embody the best promises of international education. For more information about the CU Denver/ICB program, please see the International College Beijing web site: https://www.ucdenver.edu/offices/international-affairs/partners/international-college-beijing. What this position offers: initial airline ticket to Beijing is covered by the university and a $2,500 moving allowance is provided, payable once you start. After the initial ticket, an additional allowance is provided to purchase tickets to and from Beijing. Employees receive generous health benefits through Blue Cross Blue Shield with access to top private, English-speaking clinics in Beijing and minimal out-of-pocket costs. U.S. citizens may further qualify for a 100% return of all paid state and federal income taxes. Housing options include free guesthouse apartments (inclusive of all utilities) with private rooms, private showers, shared laundry and kitchen, as well as a gym; or heavily subsidized off-campus housing (within 200ft of campus) that offers spacious 3-bedroom, 2-bath apartments, with a sunroom and city views at higher levels of accommodation. All housing has free maintenance and upkeep. China Agricultural University, whose campus ICB is located on, is nationally famous for its outstanding food offerings \u2013 this includes multiple canteens and food vendors across campus that offer highly subsidized, delicious and nutritious food, including a Halal restaurant. At ICB, semesters are 12 to 14 weeks long; semester start dates are based on the lunar calendar with fall semesters beginning early to mid-September, and spring semesters beginning mid-February to early March. Summar and Winter semester teaching may be available for additional pay. Communication courses are offered Mon-Thurs, with no classes on Fridays, which offers opportunities to explore Beijing and its surroundings. As an ancient and modern city, Beijing offers all the amenities of a major U.S. or international city. It has excellent public transportation (including subway, highspeed rail, low-cost taxis, and two major airports) that make getting around town and travel convenient. ICB also provides faculty with professional development funds towards research and/or pedagogy, and offers free Chinese language courses. In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification document form upon hire. The University does not have direct authority to hire Chinese citizens working in China. Faculty hired to teach at ICB must be able to meet the requirements to obtain the Z Visa to work in China ( http://english.gov.cn/services/workinchina/ ). Our understanding of these requirements includes: prior to the position start date, international (non-Chinese) candidates must hold their Master\u2019s degree or above and have worked full-time for at least two years in a relevant area after receiving their Bachelor\u2019s degree, or begin their appointment at ICB within 12 months of obtaining their Ph.D. Under these Chinese rules, the maximum age of candidates seeking a work Visa is 59. These requirements are subject to change by the Chinese government without notice. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The University of Colorado Denver Department of Communication invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track teaching position at the International College of Beijing (ICB). The job will commence in Beijing in Spring 2027. Depending on the performance of the individual hired and other circumstances, multi-year renewals are possible. We seek to hire a colleague who can teach a wide array of Communication courses across Health Communication, Digital Media, and humanistic approaches to AI, supporting one or more of the Department\u2019s pathways and certificates, especially in health communication, strategic communication, and/or AI and human communication. This may include courses such as Interpersonal Communication, Communication Research & Writing, Communication & Citizenship, Health Communication, and Digital Health Narratives, among others. We are particularly interested in a colleague who is well-versed in incorporating the use of AI tools and/or critically examines AI\u2019s broader societal impacts. We similarly seek a colleague who is experienced in integrating workplace readiness elements into their course design to prepare students for the workforce. The teaching load is 8 courses per academic year (4 in fall and 4 in spring) and will also assume 10% of their duties in service roles assigned in consultation with the ICB Director, Department Chair, and Associate Program Chair. These service roles may include advising students on the communication major, minor, and certificates; serving as faculty advisor or director of student clubs; contributing to or overseeing annual student festivals and ceremonies; contributing to newsletters and outcomes assessment; and other tasks. Instructor - ICB What you will do: Teach 8 courses per academic year (4 in fall and 4 in spring) Service duties assigned in consultation with the Department Chair, ICB Director, and Associate Program Chair Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master\u2019s degree in Communication or a closely allied field (English-medium) Two years independent teaching experience as the instructor of record (English-medium) Evidence of highly effective teaching Evidence of multifaceted and excellent service to an academic department Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Ph.D. in Communication (or a closely allied discipline) Demonstrated experience in communication in U.S.-China contexts Demonstrated experience in incorporating AI tools in student assignments and assessments Demonstrated experience integrating workplace readiness and/or career preparation elements into student assignments and assessments Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Proficient skills in instructional technology, digital and social media environments, as well as AI/media production tools (for example, Canvas, ChatGPT, DeepSeek, Adobe, PowerPoint, Canva, and others) Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally, in a variety of institutional contexts. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with students and employees at all levels throughout the institution. Ability to live and work in Beijing as a CU Denver employee Conditions of Employment Required to work in China for this position. Faculty hired to teach at ICB must be able to meet the requirements to obtain the Z Visa to work in China (http://english.gov.cn/services/workinchina/) To be paid via CU Denver payroll, you must have a social security number and a U.S. bank account for direct deposit CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $54,000 - $56,692. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, and interviews begin. Preference will be given to complete applications received by September 20, 2026. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Three professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). A single PDF file providing evidence for (a) at least two years independent teaching experience as the instructor of record (English-medium), (b) highly effective teaching, and (c) multifaceted and excellent service to an academic department. Questions should be directed to Dr. Mia Fischer, Associate Professor, Department of Communication, CU Denver, mia.fischer@ucdenver.ed u. Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41031&lang=en": {"title": "Veteran Transition and Support Senior Coordinator", "description": "Posted Date: Sep 8, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCSSLS-AVCRESS VeteranStudSrvc Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Student Services Senior Professional Working Title: Veteran Transition and Support Senior Coordinator FTE: Full-time 1.0 (100%) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: $55,322 - $61,146 Position #00709287 \u2013 Requisition #41031 About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * Under the direction of the Director of the Office of Veteran & Military Student Services (VMSS), this position will include developing a comprehensive faculty and staff training, developing peer support programs, developing internal and external communication materials, developing, and maintaining participant tracking, developing programming and workshops in coordination with other University services (ex. Career Center, Experiential Learning) to provide job readiness and transition skills. This position will create new programming and support and oversee existing programming and support for veterans and military-connected students and will work with campus partners in creating and implementing these programs. This position will create and maintain program information materials, such as brochures, flyers, and newsletters. This position will perform outreach to existing and potential students to provide information and resources. This position will perform outreach to build and maintain strategic community partnerships. Veteran Transition & Support Senior Coordinator: What you will do: \u2022 Coordinate all VMSS program activities, events, and programs. \u2022 Serve as a resource for all military-connected students seeking education and career transition services. \u2022 Coordinate internship and career portions of the program with appropriate internal programs. \u2022 Coordinate the mentorship aspect of the program, including, but not limited to, maintaining the roster of students and professional mentors, matching them according to major (student) and career/field (mentor), introducing/connecting the student and mentor as well as monitoring the mentorship process. \u2022 Under the direction of the Director, this position will serve as a point person on Boots to Suits related issues and serve as a community liaison to local businesses/corporations, veteran organizations, and community resources. \u2022 This position will assist and be present in all Boots to Suits courses. \u2022 Coordinate services with other University Departments, specifically the CU Denver Experiential Learning and Career Centers, and others as needed. \u2022 Monitor Boots to Suits student program participants as they matriculate through the program. \u2022 Oversee the creation and continuation of all Boots to Suits promotional materials, social media information and program website. \u2022 Maintain and foster new relationships internal and external relationships with various veteran serving organizations to further develop resources for CU Denver students. \u2022 Develop and maintain a roster of CU Denver Veteran Alumni and contact them for potential future mentorship opportunities. \u2022 Perform outreach in both the CU Denver student veteran population as well as the local business community to generate more student and business interest and participation. \u2022 Develop and administer staff and facility training programs. \u2022 Oversee peer-to-peer mentor development and programing. \u2022 Serve as advisor/liaison for student veteran affiliated campus organizations. \u2022 All other duties or unforeseen responsibilities regarding the program as needed. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. \u2022 A bachelor\u2019s degree in education, communication, social science, business, public administration, business administration, higher education, counseling, liberal arts, finance, accounting, human services, student affairs, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. \u2022 Two (2) years of professional level experience working in higher education. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor\u2019s degree on a year for year basis. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) \u2022 Veteran of the United States Armed Forces. \u2022 Master\u2019s degree in progress or completed. \u2022 One year or more experience working with Veterans in a higher education setting. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities \u2022 Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. \u2022 Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. \u2022 Demonstrate a commitment to providing outstanding customer service skills. \u2022 Demonstrate an understanding of access and engagement with a commitment to developing equitable practices. Conditions of Employment \u2022 Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. \u2022 This position follows a hybrid work structure where in-person is for three to four days and remote for one to two days based on the needs of the office. There will be occasional periods when in person work will be required five days a week based on the needs of the office. \u2022 Working from the office is required when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements \u2022 This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. \u2022 This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. \u2022 Moves equipment weighing up to 50 pounds. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu. Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $55,322 - $61,146. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by September 23rd, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: \u2022 A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications \u2022 A current CV/resume \u2022 List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Leona Lopez, leona.lopez@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41026&lang=en": {"title": "Development Assistant", "description": "Posted Date: Sep 8, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: ADM-CHAN Advancement Denver Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Admin Assistant II Working Title: Development Assistant FTE: Full-time Salary Range: $50,381 - $55,684 Position #00001851 \u2013 Requisition #41026 Join the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Office of Advancement connects those who are passionate about education and research to the people and programs at CU Denver who can excel with their support. We serve as a trusted campus and community resource that inspires alumni pride and private support to advance CU Denver's mission, and we work to ensure a bright and promising future for CU Denver through robust engagement, transformative philanthropy, and a deep sense of pride in the university. The Development Assistant will perform administrative duties and tasks, reflecting substantial variety and complexity, in the Office of Advancement. *This is a term limited position that is currently funded through June 30th 2029. The position will be reviewed by January 2029 to assess financial sustainability. If your term of employment will be concluded based on a lack of funding, you will be provided 30 days notice of the termination of the term of employment in writing by the University. Development Assistant What you will do: \u2022 Provides general office support including but not limited to catering orders, organization of office and donor events, purchasing donor flowers/gifts, printing support, receipts, reservations, and facilitating guest parking. \u2022 Performs research and updates, fund and EID look-up support in Salesforce (CU Ascend) for Advancement staff. \u2022 Serves as a data and records management resource as it relates to Advancement \u2013 understanding the data platforms, information stored and appropriate tools to access requested information. \u2022 Serves as primary point of contact and day to day operations for gift handling, accepting donations, creating accurate records and ensuring timely delivery to the Gift Processing unit at the CU Foundation. \u2022 Provides backup front desk coverage and presence to greet, direct, and address questions and concerns of visitors in person, as well as via phone and email. \u2022 Manages general triage for the Advancement and DA Support email accounts, sorting and distributing mail, scheduling conference rooms, and facilitating meeting setup. \u2022 Acts as liaison between the CU Foundation, CU System, and CU Denver campus partners regarding questions, research information, reports, and operations. \u2022 Supports team with event bios and briefings for personal meetings, prospect lists, and analyses as needed. \u2022 Supports certain events as assigned including but not limited to mailing, packaging, event assembly, prep, and take down. \u2022 Maintains cleanliness and orderliness of communal office space including lobby and kitchen; keeps inventory on office supplies, external communication documents, and swag. \u2022 Other duties as assigned Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. \u2022 Two (2) years of relevant experience in an occupation related to the work assigned to this position Substitution: A combination of related education and/or relevant experience in an occupation related to the work assigned equal to two (2) years Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) \u2022 Experience with data management and/or data research. \u2022 Experience with Microsoft Excel and CRM database. \u2022 Professional experience working in non-profit, events, and/or development/fundraising. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities \u2022 Outstanding customer service skills. \u2022 Proficiency and familiarity with Advance, Salesforce, or similar databases. \u2022 Proficiency in pulling, extracting, and organizing intricate data reports. \u2022 Ability to communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing. \u2022 Ability to utilize internet navigation and research tools (e.g., online, printed, etc.) \u2022 Proficiency in pulling, extracting, and organizing intricate data reports. \u2022 Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. \u2022 Ability to conceptualize and utilize data. \u2022 Demonstrate an exceptional understanding of access and engagement with a commitment to developing equitable practices. \u2022 Ability to manage multiple tasks simultaneously, adapt to changing priorities, manage time and meet deadlines. \u2022 Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and internet navigation tools with proven knowledge of word processing, spreadsheet software, email, and internet access software. Conditions of Employment \u2022 Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required for Advancement events. \u2022 This position requires an in-office presence (3 days a week) but does provide flexibility with a hybrid accommodation for remote work at the discretion of the unit. \u2022 Requires valid driver\u2019s license. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $50,381 - $55,684. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by September 23rd, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: \u2022 A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications \u2022 A current CV/resume \u2022 List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Nickolas Chabot-Olson, Nickolas.Chabot-Olson@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=39037&lang=en": {"title": "Lecturer Pool Posting, School of Education and Human Development", "description": "Posted Date: Sep 3, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SEHD DEAN Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Pool Posting, School of Education and Human Development Working Title: Lecturer Pool Posting, School of Education and Human Development FTE: part-time Salary Range: $5,125 for a fully-enrolled 3-credit course. Position #00626465 Requisition #39037 About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top ranked bachelors, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The School of Education & Human Development at the University of Colorado Denver is a statewide and national leader for educational quality, access and equity across the education lifespan, from birth through higher education. Members of the school community have been informing policy and practice while addressing the most important challenges faced by individuals, schools, and communities for more than 50 years. We prepare inclusive educational, community, family, and mental health practitioners, scholars, and leaders dedicated to championing change that leads to well-being, opportunity, and life-long learning in the diverse urban, rural, and global communities that we serve. Our Inclusive Excellence Plan reflects our efforts to ensure that those we serve have access to an excellent education through inclusive practice and scholarship in a climate that is responsive to their needs. The school\u2019s degree programs engage students in a strategic and interrelated combination of course work and internships in schools, agencies, and community-based organizations. The school offers three doctoral level programs, an educational specialist degree, 13 master's degrees in multiple program areas, and two undergraduate degrees, along with many licenses, endorsements and certificates. The undergraduate and graduate programs prepare and inspire education and mental health leaders to have a profound impact on fostering opportunity achievement, and success across rural, urban, and diverse communities. Programs are designed to be highly impactful for working professionals and distance learners with evening, online and hybrid class options. Community-engaged and global partnerships are the heartbeat of SEHD. Innovative initiatives co-constructed with school districts, community colleges, and service organizations draw upon personnel strengths in education, human well-being, and equity-centered and community-focused research. These partnerships foster and celebrate diverse community voices, relevant student learning opportunities that build careers, positive outcomes for partner institutions, and outstanding research publications cited around the world. In 2024, SEHD was recognized as the number one graduate online education program in Colorado and among the top graduate education programs in the nation according to U.S. News and World Report. The School of Education & Human Development's strategic plan outlines its commitment to academic excellence, inclusive practices, and community engagement. It emphasizes fostering innovation in teaching, research, and service to meet the evolving needs of students and society. To read the full statement, click here: https://education.ucdenver.edu/about-us/strategic-plan Lecturer The purpose of this posting is to expand our pool of Lecturers available to teach courses for the School of Education & Human Development. Lecturers selected from this pool will become vital members of the School\u2019s innovative education programs. For information on the specific programs and courses offered, please visit https://education.ucdenver.edu. The School of Education & Human Development will establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers for future appointments to temporary, part-time, non-tenure-track positions. Lecturers are generally limited to two courses per term. This will be a semester-by-semester appointment, with the possibility of renewal. As this is a pool posting, multiple hires will be made, and the posting will reopen periodically throughout the year to support semester-based hiring. It is typically open during the following timeframes: mid-February through April, June through July, and September through October. You are welcome to reapply to the new posting at the beginning of each year. Teaching assignments may fluctuate and are contingent upon the schedule of courses offered each term, the required number of student enrollments in your tentatively scheduled course(s), and budget availability. Thus, we cannot guarantee that you will teach particular courses or that you will actually teach in a given term. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. \u2022 Significant successful teaching or work experience in education, community, or business contexts, especially in urban and diverse settings. \u2022 At a minimum, an earned master\u2019s degree in relevant content area (some courses may require a minimum of an earned doctoral degree). See minimum qualifications for each academic level below. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Undergraduate Lecturer Minimum Qualifications \u2022 M.A. or M.S. in Education, Human Development, Family Relations, or a closely related discipline, or \u2022 B.A. or B.S. in Education, Human Development, Family Relations, or a closely related discipline, AND a M.A. or M.S. in any field in addition to at least 18 graduate level credit hours in Education or a closely related discipline, or \u2022 If the Master\u2019s Degree is in an unrelated field, the candidate must have a minimum of 5 years of successful experience in the field related to the course documented on the CV. Candidates need to supply some evidence (e.g., subject matter expertise or leadership expertise) of experience. Graduate Lecturer Minimum Qualifications MA Degree Programs \u2022 PhD, EdD, PsyD in Education, Counseling, Human Development, Family Relations, or closely related disciple field area. \u2022 If the terminal degree is in an unrelated field, the candidate must demonstrate experience in the field related to the course documented on the CV Candidates need to supply some evidence of experience (e.g., subject matter expertise or leadership expertise). \u2022 If the candidate does not have a terminal degree, the candidate must have a M.A. or M.S. AND a minimum of 5 years of successful experience in the field related to the course documented on the CV. Candidates need to supply some evidence (e.g., teaching experience, school principal, board certified counselor, etc.) of experience PhD, EdD, PsyD Degree Programs \u2022 PhD, EdD, PsyD in Education, Counseling, Human Development, Family Relations, or closely related disciple field area. \u2022 If the doctorate degree is in an unrelated field, the candidate must demonstrate at least 18 graduate level credit hours in related discipline and/or 5 years\u2019 experience in the field related to the course documented on the CV. Candidates need to supply some evidence (e.g., subject matter expertise or leadership expertise) of experience. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) \u2022 Ed.D. or Ph.D. in Education or a closely related field. \u2022 Experience teaching at the graduate level. \u2022 Experience teaching online or with blended/hybrid models (e.g. Blackboard or eCollege and LiveText) Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities \u2022 Experience with culturally, linguistically, and economically diverse communities, knowledge of urban educational community issues, and an interest in collaborating with a variety of constituencies in an urban environment. \u2022 Proficient with basic technology (e.g. MS Office) Conditions of Employment This position involves working closely with students where the person may become aware of campus safety issues that may need to be reported as part of CU\u2019s commitment to compliance with the Clery Act. The person in this role will receive the related training and be required to submit data once per year to the campus Clery Act team. For more information about our commitment to campus safety as it relates to this law, please visit https://www.ucdenver.edu/emergencymanagement/clery-act CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,125 for a fully-enrolled 3-credit course. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. As this is a pool posting, multiple hires will be made, and the posting will reopen periodically throughout the year to support semester-based hiring. It is typically open during the following timeframes: mid-February through April, June through July, and September through October. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: \u2022 A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. \u2022 Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). \u2022 Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). \u2022 Additional materials can be added here if applicable. Questions should be directed to SEHD HR, sehdhr@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40928&lang=en": {"title": "Associate Registrar for Operations", "description": "Posted Date: Aug 26, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCSSLS-AVCSEOC-Rg Rcrd/Regstr Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Academic Services Associate Director Working Title: Associate Registrar for Operations FTE: Full Time 1.0 (100%) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: $91,766 - $95,000 Position #00679137 \u2013 Requisition #40928 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado, Denver | Anschutz Medical Campus CU Denver and the CU Anschutz Medical Campus serve as vital pillars of the University of Colorado system. Located in the heart of the city, CU Denver helps make education work for all by offering unique opportunities at a premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs, across seven schools and colleges. Just a few miles away in Aurora, the CU Anschutz Medical Campus is a nationally recognized academic medical campus, home to six health professional schools, more than 60 centers and institutes, and two nationally ranked hospitals\u2014UCHealth University of Colorado Hospital and Children\u2019s Hospital Colorado\u2014which together see more than 2.6 million patient visits annually. While on separate campuses, the two universities collaborate in key areas to provide comprehensive support for students, faculty, and staff. The results are powerful: Together, CU Denver and CU Anschutz Medical Campus have earned an R1 classification for conducting cutting-edge and life-changing research that creates impact in our communities. Additionally, for more than a decade, they have received a national Military Friendly\u00ae School designation. For more information visit, ucdenver.edu and cuanschutz.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Associate Registrar for Operations position leads and supervises a team of six professionals in the Registrar\u2019s Office who support the academic mission of the university through managing, protecting, and authenticating student records. The team managed by the Associate Registrar for systems is charged with supporting the Registrar operations through systems access and development, document creation and management, curriculum maintenance, catalog production, and course scheduling, and reports to the University Registrar. Associate Registrar for Operations: What you will do: Provide leadership in the Registrars office for Registrar operations Lead the Registrar operations that are conducted through PeopleSoft Campus Solutions, student system development, testing, troubleshooting, and error resolution Support the provision of security access to CU student data systems and applications Manage theproduction services functions to support Registrar office operations Ensure effective us of OnBase imaging, forms, and workflow Oversee the registrar processes for uAchieve degree audit and transfer, Transferology and TES Lead the catalog and curriculum management through the utilization ofLeepfrog CAT and CIM modules, Manage the processes related to the Parchment transcript system software Oversee the processes related to the Paradigm ordering system application Lead the team and processes that utilize the EMS class scheduling software for class and National Student Clearinghouse and National Student Loan Data System enrollment reporting, and related services that include, but are not limited to: Research, policy development and compliance, problem solving, project management, business process design, and infrastructure decision-making. Employee management, including hiring, onboarding, training, development, and performance management. Other Duties as assigned Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Bachelor's degree in a related field. Four (4) years of progressively responsible experience in management level positions, including supervisory experience. Experience with systems and applications such as Campus Solutions, uAchieve, Leepfrog, OnBase, Parchment, Paradigm, and EMS. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor\u2019s degree on a year for year basis. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Master\u2019s degree from an accredited college or university in computer science, computer programming, information technology, information systems, student affairs, student personnel services, higher education, or related field of study Experience at the Assistant Registrar level or above in a higher education Registrar\u2019s Office. Experience in software development, configuration, and/or regression testing Experience with National Student Clearinghouse and National Student Loan Data System enrollment reporting and reconciliation, Experience establishing, reviewing, and communicating policy, and Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally, including successfully communicating technical details to non-technical colleagues. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding customer service skills. Demonstrated commitment and leadership ability to advance diversity and inclusion. Strong organizational skills and the ability to handle multiple initiatives simultaneously. Demonstrated ability to generate and implement direction for the assigned area and ensure alignment with the department, divisional unit, and university strategic goals. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements The ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. Moves equipment weighing up to 50 pounds. The University of Colorado - Denver is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $91,766 - $95,000. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation.Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Sep 9, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications A current CV/resume List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Meredith Husk, Meredith.Husk@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=39036&lang=en": {"title": "Lecturer - CPE, Continuing and Professional Education (Pool Posting)", "description": "Posted Date: Aug 24, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SEHD CPE Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer - CPE, Continuing and Professional Education (Pool Posting) Working Title: Lecturer - CPE, Continuing and Professional Education (Pool Posting) FTE: Part-time Salary Range: $5,125 for a fully-enrolled 3-credit course. Position #00007000 Requisition #39036 About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top ranked bachelors, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The School of Education & Human Development at the University of Colorado Denver is a statewide and national leader for educational quality, access and equity across the education lifespan, from birth through higher education. Members of the school community have been informing policy and practice while addressing the most important challenges faced by individuals, schools, and communities for more than 50 years. We prepare inclusive educational, community, family, and mental health practitioners, scholars, and leaders dedicated to championing change that leads to well-being, opportunity, and life-long learning in the diverse urban, rural, and global communities that we serve. Our Inclusive Excellence Plan reflects our efforts to ensure that those we serve have access to an excellent education through inclusive practice and scholarship in a climate that is responsive to their needs. The school\u2019s degree programs engage students in a strategic and interrelated combination of course work and internships in schools, agencies, and community-based organizations. The school offers three doctoral level programs, an educational specialist degree, 13 master's degrees in multiple program areas, and two undergraduate degrees, along with many licenses, endorsements and certificates. The undergraduate and graduate programs prepare and inspire education and mental health leaders to have a profound impact on fostering opportunity achievement, and success across rural, urban, and diverse communities. Programs are designed to be highly impactful for working professionals and distance learners with evening, online and hybrid class options. Community-engaged and global partnerships are the heartbeat of SEHD. Innovative initiatives co-constructed with school districts, community colleges, and service organizations draw upon personnel strengths in education, human well-being, and equity-centered and community-focused research. These partnerships foster and celebrate diverse community voices, relevant student learning opportunities that build careers, positive outcomes for partner institutions, and outstanding research publications cited around the world. In 2024, SEHD was recognized as the number one graduate online education program in Colorado and among the top graduate education programs in the nation according to U.S. News and World Report. The School of Education & Human Development's strategic plan outlines its commitment to academic excellence, inclusive practices, and community engagement. It emphasizes fostering innovation in teaching, research, and service to meet the evolving needs of students and society. To read the full statement, click here: https://education.ucdenver.edu/about-us/strategic-plan Lecturer - CPE, Continuing and Professional Education (Pool Posting) What you will do: Our Office of Continuing and Professional Education (CPE) provides a wide array of courses, an alternative teacher licensure program, certificates, endorsements, workshops and leadership training tailored to meet your professional development needs. The purpose of this posting is to expand our pool of Lecturers available to teach courses for CPE. Lecturers selected from this pool will become vital members of the School\u2019s innovative education programs. For information on the specific programs and courses offered through CPE, please visit https://education.ucdenver.edu/continuing-education. The School of Education & Human Development will establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers for future appointments to temporary, part-time, non-tenure-track positions in Continuing and Professional Education (CPE). Lecturers are generally limited to two courses per term. This will be a semester-by-semester appointment, with the possibility of renewal. Teaching assignments may fluctuate and are contingent upon the schedule of courses offered each term, the required number of student enrollments in your tentatively scheduled course(s), and budget availability. Thus, we cannot guarantee that you will teach particular courses or that you will actually teach in a given term. This position involves working closely with students where the person may become aware of campus safety issues that may need to be reported as part of CU\u2019s commitment to compliance with the Clery Act. The person in this role will receive the related training and be required to submit data once per year to the campus Clery Act team. For more information about our commitment to campus safety as it relates to this law, please visit https://www.ucdenver.edu/emergencymanagement/clery-act Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. \u2022 Significant successful teaching or work experience in education, community, or business contexts, especially in urban and diverse settings. \u2022 At a minimum, an earned master\u2019s degree in relevant content area (some courses may require a minimum of an earned doctoral degree). See minimum qualifications for each academic level below. Undergraduate Lecturer Minimum Qualifications \u2022 M.A. or M.S. in Education, Human Development, Family Relations, or a closely related discipline, or \u2022 B.A. or B.S. in Education, Human Development, Family Relations, or a closely related discipline, AND a M.A. or M.S. in any field in addition to at least 18 graduate level credit hours in Education or a closely related discipline, or If the Master\u2019s Degree is in an unrelated field, the candidate must have a minimum of 5 years of successful experience in the field related to the course documented on the CV. Candidates need to supply some evidence (e.g., subject matter expertise or leadership expertise) of experience. Graduate Lecturer Minimum Qualifications MA Degree Programs \u2022 PhD, EdD, PsyD in Education, Counseling, Human Development, Family Relations, or closely related disciple field area. If the terminal degree is in an unrelated field, the candidate must demonstrate experience in the field related to the course documented on the CV Candidates need to supply some evidence of experience (e.g., subject matter expertise or leadership expertise). If the candidate does not have a terminal degree, the candidate must have a M.A. or M.S. AND a minimum of 5 years of successful experience in the field related to the course documented on the CV. Candidates need to supply some evidence (e.g., teaching experience, school principal, board certified counselor, etc.) of experience PhD, EdD, PsyD Degree Programs \u2022 PhD, EdD, PsyD in Education, Counseling, Human Development, Family Relations, or closely related disciple field area. If the doctorate degree is in an unrelated field, the candidate must demonstrate at least 18 graduate level credit hours in related discipline and/or 5 years\u2019 experience in the field related to the course documented on the CV. Candidates need to supply some evidence (e.g., subject matter expertise or leadership expertise) of experience. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) \u2022 Ed.D. or Ph.D. in Education or a closely related field. \u2022 Experience teaching at the graduate level. \u2022 Experience teaching online or with blended/hybrid models (e.g. Blackboard or eCollege and LiveText. \u2022 Experience with culturally, linguistically, and economically diverse communities, knowledge of urban educational community issues, and an interest in collaborating with a variety of constituencies in an urban environment. \u2022 Proficient with basic technology (e.g. MS Office) CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,125 for a fully-enrolled 3-credit course. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. As of January 1, 2021, Lecturer positions will accrue sick leave at a rate of 0.034 hours per hour worked with a maximum accrual of 48 hours per fiscal year (July 1 \u2013 June 30). This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. As this is a pool posting, multiple hires will be made, and the posting will reopen periodically throughout the year to support semester-based hiring. It is typically open during the following timeframes: mid-February through April, June through July, and September through October. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: \u2022 A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. \u2022 Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). \u2022 Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to SEHD HR, sehdhr@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=39022&lang=en": {"title": "CU Succeed, Lecturer (Gold)", "description": "Closing Date: 12/31/2026 Posted Date: Aug 21, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CLAS-CU Succeed Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Adjunct Lecturer Working Title: CU Succeed Lecturer (Gold) FTE: Part Time Salary Range : non-compensated (see below for details) Position #00722892 \u2013 Requisition #20282 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top ranked bachelors, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The CU Succeed program seeks currently employed High School teachers as part-time Lecturers. This program enables high school juniors and seniors to take CU Denver courses in their high schools for dual credit during the school day. All applicants into this position are seeking approval as CU Denver Adjunct Faculty members to teach CU Denver courses in the high school where they are already employed. This adjunct lecturer role is a non\u2011compensated appointment within the CU Succeed program. Individuals approved for this position serve on a voluntary basis and do not receive salary, stipend, or benefits from the University of Colorado Denver. The role is designed to formally recognize and authorize qualified high\u2011school educators to deliver CU Denver course content in their home schools, in alignment with academic standards and departmental expectations. Participation as an unpaid adjunct reflects a collaborative partnership between CU Denver and Colorado high schools to expand dual\u2011credit learning opportunities and does not create an employment relationship or guarantee future compensated teaching assignments with the university. CU Succeed Lecturer (Gold) What you will do: Instructors will teach courses in Colorado High Schools. These instructors are approved by academic departments to offer course content for designated courses. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Masters Degree or 18 credit hours at the graduate level in the discipline you are seeking approval. Currently employed in a Colorado High School. Conditions of Employment This position requires an onsite presence, on the teacher's home high school campus, at the discretion of the home school\u2019s schedule. This adjunct lecturer appointment is a voluntary, non\u2011compensated role and does not constitute a paid employment relationship with the University of Colorado Denver. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements The ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. The position requires the ability to effectively collaborate across functions with both CU Denver faculty and staff and with personnel at the partnering high school, including sustained communication, coordination, and shared academic planning. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Compensation and Benefits This adjunct lecturer appointment is a voluntary, non\u2011compensated role and does not constitute a paid employment relationship with the University of Colorado Denver. All compensation and benefits should be handled by the instructor\u2019s home institution. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to six (6) months from the posting date, or [DATE]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the six\u2011month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Current Curriculum Vita, including Education (degrees, dates, institutions attended, etc.), Teaching Experience, Publications and References (names, titles and phone numbers) Undergraduate and graduate transcripts Department specific required education qualifications and additional requirements found here: https://clas.ucdenver.edu/cusucceed/new-lecturer-application Questions should be directed to Leslie Cummings, leslie.cummings@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=35883&lang=en": {"title": "Lecturer", "description": "Closing Date: 11/11/2026 Posted Date: Aug 13, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CLAS-Chemistry Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/ Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer FTE: part-time Salary Range: $1 , 615 p e r credit hour (lower division), $1645 per credit hour (upper division), or $1808 per credit hour (graduate level) Position #00 007315 ID: 35883 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado - Denver The University of Colorado Denver is the state\u2019s premier public urban research university and equity-serving institution. Globally connected and locally invested, CU Denver partners with future-focused learners and communities to design accessible, relevant, transformative educational experiences for every stage of life and career. Across seven schools and colleges in the heart of downtown Denver, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges through break through innovations and impactful research, and creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. For more information, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * Lecturer What you will do: The teaching load for this lecturer position is a maximum of two Chemistry or Biochemistry courses per semester . The lecturer will teach the assigned course (s) , hold office hours , and submit grades at the end of each semester accordingly. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. M S in Chemistry or Biochemistry or a closely related field is required D emonstrated record of excellence in teaching. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to communicate in a positive and effective manner, across various modalities. Ability to effectively listen and share relevant information. Ability to establish and respond to, as well as, balance multiple work priorities, follow through, and meet established deadlines. Intentionally contribute to a respectful, equitable, positive, and professional workplace. Commitment to enhancing diversity, equity and inclusion. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Understanding of the needs of a diverse student population. Strong commitment to student education and success. Experience in online or hybrid delivery . Physical Requirements the ability to stand and walk for extended periods, bend and reach to assist students, lift and carry moderate weight (like books or supplies), Good vision and hearing, Clear speech, manual dexterity for writing and using technology. Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established at $ 1, 615 \u2013 1808, per credit hour accordingly . The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix . Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified , and interviews begin. P reference will be given to complete applications received by May 31, 2025 at 11:59:00 PM . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position . Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate) , and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed t o Laura Cuellar , LAURA.CUELLAR@UCDENVER.EDU. Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu \u200b ."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40606&lang=en": {"title": "Lecturer", "description": "Posted Date: Jul 22, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CLAS - Interdisciplinary Studi Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer FTE: Part-time Salary Range: The starting salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established as $1,704 per credit hour (undergraduate level), or $1,849 per credit hour (graduate level). Position #00630439 \u2013 Requisition #40606 About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * This posting will establish and maintain a pool of part-time lecturers with experience teaching Interdisciplinary Studies Related courses in designated fields of the discipline, which may include specializations in areas such as Health Humanities, Humanities, Religious Studies, Social Justice, Sustainability, Women and Gender Studies, or another interdisciplinary studies related field for the Interdisciplinary Studies Program in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at the University of Colorado Denver. By submitting your application, you will become part of an applicant pool. Candidates hired from this pool will fill temporary, non-tenure track positions and will teach no more than two courses per semester. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50%) and will be made semester-by-semester, depending on the needs of the department and subject to budgetary approval. Therefore, this posting does not necessarily reflect a current open position. The Department of Political Science will contact you if there is an opening that suits your qualifications. Lecturer What you will do: \u2022 Teach up to two courses per semester on an as needed basis. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. \u2022 Master\u2019s degree or PhD in Interdisciplinary Studies or related field Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) \u2022 Previous teaching experience \u2022 PhD or ABD in Interdisciplinary Studies or related field Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities \u2022 Ability to communicate in a positive and effective manner, across various modalities. \u2022 Ability to effectively listen and share relevant information. \u2022 Ability to establish and respond to, as well as, balance multiple work priorities, follow through, and meet established deadlines. \u2022 Intentionally contribute to a respectful, equitable, positive, and professional workplace. \u2022 Commitment to enhancing diversity, equity and inclusion. \u2022 Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. \u2022 Understanding of the needs of a diverse student population. \u2022 Strong commitment to student education and success. \u2022 Experience in online or hybrid delivery. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The starting salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established as $1,704 per credit hour (undergraduate level), or $1,849 per credit hour (graduate level). The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on number of credit hours and whether it is graduate or undergraduate. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline This posting will establish and maintain a pool of part-time lecturers with experience teaching Interdisciplinary Studies Related courses. By submitting your application, you will become part of an applicant pool. This posting does not necessarily reflect a current open position. The department will contact you if there is an opening that suits your qualifications. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: \u2022 A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. \u2022 Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). \u2022 Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40601&lang=en": {"title": "Lecturer", "description": "Posted Date: Jul 22, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SPA - OTHER Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer FTE: Part-Time Salary Range: $5,124.01 per 3-credit hour course for Fall 2026. Beginning January 2027, SPA will apply annual merit pool increases consistent with campus guidelines. This position is part of an ongoing pooled posting; rates may differ for Senior Lecturers who are retired or Emeritus SPA faculty. To inquire about the current rate for any appointment type, please contact SPA.HR@ucdenver.edu. Position #00825852\u2013 Requisition #40601 About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The University of Colorado Denver Campus seeks individuals with demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. We value the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty and staff of diverse backgrounds. This posting will establish and maintain a pool of candidates to fill temporary, non-tenure track Lecturer positions for the School of Public Affairs. Candidates hired from this pool may teach undergraduate courses in the Bachelor of Public Administration (BAPA) or Bachelor of Criminal Justice (BACJ) programs, or graduate level courses in the school's Master of Public Administration program (MPA), the Master of Public Policy (MPP) program, or Master of Criminal Justice (MCJ) program. If selected, this would be a part-time, semester-by-semester appointment, with the possibility of renewal. This pool will remain active until May 31, 2027, at which point all applicants will be cleared from the pool. Applicants are encouraged to apply to future recruitment pools after that date. US News & World Report places CU Denver's School of Public Affairs as a whole at number 25 nationally, tied with Duke University, Georgetown University and several other prominent institutions. Four of SPA\u2019s academic focus areas\u2014now offered as graduate certificates\u2014are ranked among the top 25 programs nationally. - 10th in environmental policy and management - 13th in nonprofit management - 22nd in public management & leadership - 25th in public policy management Degrees offered include the Ph.D. in Public Affairs, the Master of Public Administration, the Master of Public Policy, the Master of Criminal Justice, the Bachelor of Arts in Criminal Justice, and the Bachelor of Arts in Public Administration. Please visit https:// publicaffairs.ucdenver.edu/ for further details. Lecturer What you will do: Lecturers in the School of Public Affairs (SPA) contribute to the teaching mission across the School\u2019s undergraduate and graduate programs in public administration, public policy, and criminal justice. Teaching assignments may include in-person, hybrid, or online formats depending on program need and instructor expertise. Lecturers may teach no more than two courses per semester or term across all CU campuses. If you are teaching in any unit outside SPA, please make sure to note that in your application. As a lecturer, you will: \u2022 Teach one or two courses per term that align with SPA\u2019s curriculum and learning outcomes. \u2022 Develop and deliver high-quality, inclusive instruction that reflects SPA\u2019s mission to Lead. Solve. Change. \u2022 Foster an engaging, equitable learning environment for a diverse student population of working professionals, traditional students, and community partners. \u2022 Design course content and assessments consistent with SPA\u2019s learning outcomes and assessment philosophy emphasizing applied, evidence-based learning and equity-minded reflection. \u2022 Communicate regularly with students and provide timely, constructive feedback consistent with SPA\u2019s teaching guidelines. \u2022 Collaborate with program faculty and the program manager in the syllabus collection and review process, ensuring syllabi reflect current objectives and university policies. \u2022 Participate in instructor communication and onboarding processes and maintain compliance with required training and campus policies. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Candidates must have completed a terminal degree. For most courses, this requires an MPA, MCJ, or Ph.D. in public administration, public policy, criminal justice, or a related field. Candidates must also show strong accomplishment in teaching. \u2022 For undergraduate courses: the instructor should possess a relevant graduate degree at least one level above the course taught; if the instructor\u2019s graduate degree is in a non-relevant field, the instructor must have completed at least 18 hours in a graduate program in a relevant field \u2022 For master\u2019s level courses: the instructor should possess a terminal degree relevant to the discipline and a record of research, scholarship, or achievement appropriate to the program \u2022 For doctoral courses: the instructor should possess a terminal degree relevant to the discipline and a record of scholarship and preparation to teach at the doctoral level \u2022 For dual credit courses (e.g., CU Succeed): the instructor should possess the same qualifications as required for undergraduate courses Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) \u2022 Teaching experience in higher education, particularly with adult learners or hybrid/online delivery. \u2022 Demonstrated professional experience in public service, nonprofit management, policy analysis, or the criminal justice system. \u2022 Experience using Canvas or comparable learning management systems and applying inclusive, high-impact teaching practices. \u2022 Evidence of commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging in teaching or professional work. \u2022 Ability to connect academic theory with real-world application in public affairs practice. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities \u2022 Knowledge of public administration, public policy, or criminal justice frameworks and their contemporary applications. \u2022 Strong organizational and communication skills, with the ability to manage multiple course demands. \u2022 Cultural competency and awareness of the role of equity and justice in public service education. \u2022 Facility with applied learning techniques such as case studies, simulations, community-based projects, and data-driven assignments. \u2022 Ability to engage students through accessible course design and learner-centered pedagogy. \u2022 Proficiency with online systems as used in course coordination. Conditions of Employment \u2022 Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. \u2022 This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements \u2022 Ability to sustain periods of focused work and communication in online or in-person instructional settings. \u2022 Capacity to adapt to varying class modalities (in-person, hybrid, online). \u2022 Regular use of computer and learning technology systems. \u2022 Commitment to maintaining a respectful, collaborative, and inclusive environment consistent with SPA and CU Denver values. \u2022 Occasional evening or weekend work may be required depending on course schedules. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,124.01 per 3-credit hour course for Fall 2026. Beginning January 2027, SPA will apply annual merit pool increases consistent with campus guidelines. This position is part of an ongoing pooled posting; rates may differ for Senior Lecturers who are retired or Emeritus SPA faculty. To inquire about the current rate for any appointment type, please contact SPA.HR@ucdenver.edu.The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline This is a pooled posting. Applications are reviewed by each Program Director quarterly. If a vacant teaching need is identified, applicants that fit the qualifications and experience for a particular course may be contacted. Please direct questions to SPA.HR@ucdenver.edu. Thank you! Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: 1. A letter of application which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications 2. A current Resume/CV 3. Proof of degree (unofficial transcript or diploma is acceptable) 4. The names, addresses, daytime telephone numbers and e-mail addresses for 3-5 professional references, either attached to your resume/CV or uploaded as a separate document 5. Lecturers may teach no more than two courses per semester or term across all CU campuses. If you are teaching in any unit outside SPA, please make sure to note that in your application. Please be advised that the University does check references as part of the employment process. Please do not submit any of your application material (via email) to the job posting contact. Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40482&lang=en": {"title": "CU Succeed Lecturer (Silver)", "description": "Closing Date: 12/18/2026 Posted Date: Jul 21, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CLAS-CU Succeed Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: CU Succeed Lecturer (Silver) FTE: Part Time | In-Person Salary Range : $4,002 per 3 credit course Position #00723102 \u2013 Requisition #40482 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top ranked bachelors, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The CU Succeed program enables high school juniors and seniors to take CU Denver courses in their high schools for dual credit during the school day. All applicants into this position are seeking approval as CU Denver Adjunct Faculty members to teach CU Denver courses that are requested by Denver area High Schools. The posting will establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers for the CU Succeed Silver program. Candidates hired from this pool will fill temporary, non-tenure track positions and will teach no more than two courses per semester. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50%) and will be made semester-by-semester, depending on the needs of Denver area High Schools. Therefore, this posting does not necessarily reflect a current open position. This temporary Lecturer recruitment pool is anticipated to remain continuously active. CU Succeed Lecturer (Silver) What you will do: Instructors will teach courses in High Schools. These instructors are approved by academic departments to offer course content for designated courses. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Masters Degree the discipline you are seeking approval, or a Masters Degree with at least or 18 credit hours at the graduate level in the discipline. Ability to travel to locations requiring a lecturer CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Compensation and Benefits The salary range for this position has been established at $4,002 per 3 credit course, per semester. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to six (6) months from the posting date July 21st, 2026. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the six\u2011month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Current resume or Curriculum Vita, including Education (degrees, dates, institutions attended, etc.), Teaching Experience, Publications and References (names, titles and phone numbers). Undergraduate and graduate transcripts. Department specific required education qualifications and additional requirements found here: https://clas.ucdenver.edu/cusucceed/new-lecturer-applicationDepartment specific required. Questions should be directed to Leslie Cummings, leslie.cummings@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40420&lang=en": {"title": "Lecturer of Recording Arts (Undergraduate)", "description": "Posted Date: Jul 7, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CAM-Music & Entertainment Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer of Recording Arts (Undergraduate) FTE: .225 per 3 credit course Salary Range: $5,371.19 per 3 credit course Position # 00726509 \u2013 Requisition #40420 About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * At the College of Arts & Media (CAM), we empower a diverse community of makers, scholars, and innovators to thrive in the rapidly evolving creative industries. Through a dynamic blend of critical inquiry, creative exploration, and real-world engagement, CAM prepares students for lives filled with opportunity, meaning, and purpose. Rooted in community and driven by a spirit of intellectual and artistic freedom, CAM embraces risk-takers, visionaries, and cultural disruptors by providing access to cutting-edge technology, global perspectives, and a nurturing environment where bold ideas flourish. CAM offers top-ranked degrees and programs in Film & Television, Media Forensics, Music & Entertainment, and Visual Arts. The Music & Entertainment Industry Studies (MEIS) Department features some of the best contemporary-focused music industry programs in the country. With about 500 students, MEIS has one of the biggest music business, recording arts, singer/songwriter, and contemporary performance programs in the Western U.S. Our downtown Denver location is perfect for enabling our students to be very involved with the thriving Denver music scene while they are in the program. As one of the only music departments in the country with a contemporary focus, Music & Entertainment Industry Studies (MEIS) at CU Denver provides students with the guidance, knowledge, and expertise needed to transform passion for music into a lifelong profession. This is an ongoing posting for a lecturer pool. There is not a specific recruitment timeframe or hiring timeline. There may or may not be a current need for lecturers in this area. As needs arise, applications in the pool will be reviewed and candidates contacted for interview. The posting will remain open for a maximum of 6 months. Lecturer appointments are at-will and teaching assignments are determined on a semester by semester basis. Teaching assignments may fluctuate and are contingent upon the schedule of courses offered each term. Lecturer of Recording Arts (Undergraduate) What you will do: 100% Teaching You will teach one or two classes per semester (3-6 credit hours) As a Lecturer in Recording Arts (Undergraduate), your primary focus will be on inspiring and training the next generation of contemporary musicians. This can include instruction in the following: \u2022 Basics of Audio Production \u2022 Advanced Audio Production \u2022 Mixing Techniques \u2022 Mastering Techniques \u2022 Critical Listening \u2022 Pro-Tools Lab \u2022 Digital Audio Workstation Techniques and application \u2022 Live sound Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. BA/BS/BM in Music or a related field Or substitution of tested experience as exemplified by one or more of the following: \u2022 Engineering, mixing, or mastering a recording(s) with a reputable label \u2022 Extensive experience as a reputable studio or live sound engineer \u2022 Evidence of mixing/engineering sound for a national/international tour/festival \u2022 Evidence of recording published/performed by a major artist/publishing/media outlet (i.e. film or TV show) or company \u2022 Two years successful experience teaching at a major university or college in same or similar program Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) \u2022 Master\u2019s Degree in Music or a related field \u2022 Experience teaching Music at the college level Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities \u2022 Ability to communicate in a positive and effective manner, across various modalities. \u2022 Ability to balance multiple projects and tasks while maintaining attention to detail. \u2022 Ability to create equitable and positive experiences for all. \u2022 Outwardly contribute to a respectful, positive, and professional workspace. \u2022 Demonstrate influential ability to embrace and advance equity and equitable inclusion. \u2022 Ability to establish work priorities, follow through, and meet established deadlines. \u2022 Strong judgment and critical thinking skills. \u2022 Ability to authentically listen and communicate relevant information, anticipate problems, and offer suggestions for resolution. \u2022 Demonstrate dedication to mentoring students to best realize their potential as artists in society. \u2022 Demonstrated excellence and experience in organizational teamwork, communication, and interpersonal skills CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,371.19 per 3 credit course. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. This position is not eligible for benefits. Application Deadline This is an ongoing posting for a lecturer pool. There is not a specific recruitment timeframe or hiring timeline. There may or may not be a current need for lecturers in this area. As needs arise, applications in the pool will be reviewed and candidates contacted for interview. The posting will remain open for a maximum of 6 months. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: 1. Letter of application specifically addressing the position requirements and outlining qualifications 2. Current CV or r\u00e9sum\u00e9 Questions should be directed to Evan Shelton, evan.shelton@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40266&lang=en": {"title": "Lecturer in Landscape Architecture", "description": "Closing Date: 12/31/2026 Posted Date: Jun 18, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CAP-Landscape Arch Dept Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in Landscape Architecture FTE: .225 per 3-credit course or .45 per 6-credit course Part-time Salary Range: The salary for this position as been established at $5,860 for a 3-credit hour course or $8,680 for a 6-credit hour course Position #00642344 \u2013 Requisition #40266 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * This posting establishes a pool of candidates who can teach one studio or technical seminar per semester in Landscape Architecture on an as needed basis. This posting does not necessarily reflect a current, open position. Single course appointments will be made semester-by-semester, as teaching needs arise. This temporary Lecturer pool is anticipated to remain continuously active through August 2026, at which point, all applications will be cleared from the pool. Applicants will be welcome to apply to future pools after that date. Lecturer What you will do: The Department of Landscape Architecture in the College of Architecture and Planning at the University of Colorado Denver is seeking a pool of Lecturers from which future appointments will be made. Lecturers selected from this pool will teach in the College\u2019s graduate program. Classes taught may range from three to six credit hours and may include lectures, seminars, and studios in all teaching modes (in-person, hybrid, online, remote). Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. A master\u2019s degree in Landscape Architecture or a related field, or a terminal degree and expertise in the course content is required. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Preference may be given to applicants with prior teaching experience, a record of professional practice in landscape architecture, and a professional degree in a related field. Applicants for courses addressing specific subjects are also given consideration based on the course needs; in this case, they must have an advanced degree or proven expertise in the topic. Applicants should have substantive knowledge of the landscape architecture field and/or the subject matter which they will be teaching.Individuals with multidisciplinary education and expertise are strongly encouraged to apply. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to communicate effectively, across various modalities. Strong interpersonal and communication skills that support building positive, respectful relationships with students and colleagues. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty and staff in a collegial academic environment. Ability to develop a clear syllabus outlining learning outcomes, policies, and assessments for the class. Ability to adapt teaching strategies to different course formats (in-person, online, hybrid) and student needs. Ability to foster an inclusive classroom environment that encourages respectful dialogue across diverse perspectives. Ability to incorporate inclusive and equitable teaching practices that support student success. A commitment to inclusive excellence, including supporting students from diverse backgrounds and perspectives. Conditions of Employment The position may involve in-person or hybrid work depending on the specific course(s) being taught. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary for this position has been established at: $5,860 for a 3-credit hour course. $8,680 for a 6-credit hour course. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. This part-time appointment is not eligible for group health, life insurance, or retirement benefits. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to six (6) months - Dec 31, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the six\u2011month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to CAP Human Resources, CAP.HR@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40203&lang=en": {"title": "Lecturer Urban and Regional Planning", "description": "Closing Date: 12/01/2026 Posted Date: Jun 12, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CAP-Urban & Regional Planning Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in Urban and Regional Planning FTE: Part-time .225 per 3-credit course or .45 per 6-credit course | Hybrid Salary Range : The salary for this position as been established at $5,860 for a 3-credit hour course or $8,680 for a 6-credit hour course Position #00611154 \u2013 Requisition #40203 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * This posting establishes a pool of candidates to fill temporary, non-tenure-track lecturer positions in Urban & Regional Planning. This posting does not necessarily reflect a current, open position. Single-course appointments will be made semester by semester, as teaching needs arise. This temporary Lecturer pool is anticipated to remain continuously active through August 2026, at which point, all applications will be cleared from the pool. Applicants will be welcome to apply to future pools after that date. Lecturer What you will do: The Department of Urban and Regional Planning in the College of Architecture and Planning at the University of Colorado Denver is seeking a pool of Lecturers from which future appointments will be made. Lecturers selected from this pool will teach in the College\u2019s graduate program. Classes may range from three to six credit hours and may include lectures, seminars, and studios in all teaching modes (in-person, hybrid, online, remote). Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. A master\u2019s degree in Planning or a related field. Applicants should have a substantive background in urban planning or related fields, including experience with professional activities, research, interdisciplinary collaborations, community engagement, and relevant software. Preferred Qualifications to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Preference may be given to applicants with prior teaching experience, a record of professional practice in planning, and a professional degree in a planning-related field. Individuals with multi-disciplinary education and expertise are strongly encouraged to apply. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to communicate effectively, across various modalities. Strong interpersonal and communication skills that support building positive, respectful relationships with students and colleagues. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty and staff in a collegial academic environment. Ability to develop a clear syllabus outlining learning outcomes, policies, and assessments for the class. Ability to adapt teaching strategies to different course formats (in-person, online, hybrid) and student needs. Ability to foster an inclusive classroom environment that encourages respectful dialogue across diverse perspectives. Ability to incorporate inclusive and equitable teaching practices that support student success. A commitment to inclusive excellence, including supporting students from diverse backgrounds and perspectives. Conditions of Employment The position may involve in-person or hybrid work depending on the specific course(s) being taught. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary for this position has been established at: $5,860 for a 3-credit hour course. $8,680 for a 6-credit hour course. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. This part-time appointment is not eligible for group health, life insurance, or retirement benefits. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to six (6) months from the posting date [Dec 1, 2026, 11:59:00 PM]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the six\u2011month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to CAP Human Resources, cap.hr@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40204&lang=en": {"title": "Lecturer in Architecture", "description": "Closing Date: 12/01/2026 Posted Date: Jun 11, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CAP-Architecture Department Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in Architecture FTE: Part-time . 225 per 3-credit course or .45 per 6-credit course Salary Range: The salary for this position as been established at $5,860 for a 3-credit hour course or $8,680 for a 6-credit hour course Position #00696918 \u2013 Requisition #40204 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * This posting establishes a pool of candidates to fill temporary, non-tenure-track lecturer positions in Architecture. This posting does not necessarily reflect a current, open position. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50%) and will be made semester-by-semester, as teaching needs arise. This temporary Lecturer pool is anticipated to remain continuously active through August 2026, at which point, all applications will be cleared from the pool. Applicants will be welcome to apply to future pools after that date. Lecturer What you will do : The Department of Architecture in the College of Architecture and Planning at the University of Colorado Denver is seeking a pool of Lecturers from which future appointments will be made. Lecturers selected from this pool will teach six-credit-hour design studios in the Department of Architecture\u2019s undergraduate and/or graduate programs. These may include lectures/studios in all teaching modes (in-person, hybrid, online, remote). Lecturers that are hired to teach design studios are expected to have expertise and experience in architectural design. This includes knowledge of different design paradigms, design skills, and approaches to project design. A successful applicant must be able to develop and manage student projects through constructive criticism, the use of technologies ranging from technical drafting to advanced digital design tools and visualization software. If applying to a non-studio course the applicant must possess and be able to demonstrate expertise in the area of focus. If an applicant has an area of expertise other than or in addition to a design studio and would like to be considered to teach a three-credit-hour course, the applicant should highlight this interest in a cover letter. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. A bachelor\u2019s degree in Architecture or a related field is required. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Preference will be given to applicants with a professional degree in architecture or a terminal degree in a related field. Additional preference will be given to applicants with prior teaching experience, and/or professional registration, and/or a record of professional practice in architecture. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to communicate effectively, across various modalities. Strong interpersonal and communication skills that support building positive, respectful relationships with students and colleagues. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty and staff in a collegial academic environment. Ability to develop a clear syllabus outlining learning outcomes, policies, and assessments for the class. Ability to adapt teaching strategies to different course formats (in-person, online, hybrid) and student needs. Ability to foster an inclusive classroom environment that encourages respectful dialogue across diverse perspectives. Ability to incorporate inclusive and equitable teaching practices that support student success. A commitment to inclusive excellence, including supporting students from diverse backgrounds and perspectives. Conditions of Employment The position may involve in-person or hybrid work depending on the specific course(s) being taught. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary for this position has been established at: $5,860 for a 3-credit hour course. $8,680 for a 6-credit hour course. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. This part-time appointment is not eligible for group health, life insurance, or retirement benefits. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to six (6) months from the posting date [Dec 1, 2026, 11:59:00 PM]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the six\u2011month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to CAP Human Resources, cap.hr@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=38968&lang=en": {"title": "Lecturer of Acting", "description": "Posted Date: May 12, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CAM-Film & Television Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer of Acting FTE: .225 per 3 credit course Salary Range: $5,371.19 per 3 credit course Position #00605107 \u2013 Requisition #38968 About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * At the College of Arts & Media (CAM), we empower a diverse community of makers, scholars, and innovators to thrive in the rapidly evolving creative industries. Through a dynamic blend of critical inquiry, creative exploration, and real-world engagement, CAM prepares students for lives filled with opportunity, meaning, and purpose. Rooted in community and driven by a spirit of intellectual and artistic freedom, CAM embraces risk-takers, visionaries, and cultural disruptors by providing access to cutting-edge technology, global perspectives, and a nurturing environment where bold ideas flourish. CAM offers top-ranked degrees and programs in Film & Television, Media Forensics, Music & Entertainment, and Visual Arts. The Film & Television department within the College of Arts & Media invites dynamic educators and creative professionals to apply to join our collaborative faculty team as a part-time Lecturer specializing in Acting. This is an opportunity to inspire and empower tomorrow\u2019s filmmakers in the heart of Denver, working alongside innovative peers in a thriving urban arts scene. Why join CU Denver CAM? \u2022 Be part of a forward-looking, supportive faculty committed to excellence and innovation. \u2022 Enjoy a culture that values your unique artistic and academic contributions. \u2022 Teach within a nationally recognized program. \u2022 Shape a vibrant program positioned at the crossroads of professional opportunity and creative experimentation, in a city alive with storytelling and artistic energy. The Film & Television program offers a Bachelor of Fine Arts (BFA) in Film and Television. This BFA emphasis provides intensive, practical training that requires successful completion of numerous film/TV projects, ranging from fiction to documentary. The emphasis is designed for students to progress through the semesters as a cohort. Undergraduates will work on their own projects and assist with numerous group projects. Students graduate with both a theoretical and historical perspective, as well as hands-on experience in film and television production. This program prepares students to begin their careers at entry-level positions in the film or television industry, start their personal creative journey, or continue their studies in a graduate program. We believe in the power of transformative education, hands-on learning, and creative exploration. Our BFA program cultivates storytellers with a strong technical foundation and artistic vision, preparing graduates for immediate impact in the film, television, and media industries. \u2022 Accolades: For the fourth consecutive year, CU Denver's Film & Television program has been named to MovieMaker Magazine's Top 30 Best Film Schools list. We are recognized for our hands-on, cohort-based curriculum, affordability, and strong industry connections. \u2022 Career Pathways & Networking: Graduates are successful across multiple areas, including opportunities in Hollywood, independent film, commercial film, and post-production studios. \u2022 Hands-on from Day One: The curriculum is sequence-based, allowing students to build on skillsets developed throughout their college career. \u2022 Students building a High-Volume Portfolio: The curriculum is known for its rigor, as students often complete 20+ films/exercises on their portfolios by graduation. This indicates a highly engaged and active student body. \u2022 Access to Professional Gear: The program's \"film cage\" provides students with access to industry-standard, professional-grade cameras, sound, lighting, and grip equipment. \u2022 Only BFA Production Program in the Region: CU Denver is the only school in the region offering a BFA in production. \u2022 Collaborative Cohort Culture: The program is built on a cohort-style curriculum in which students build strong bonds by working on each other's film sets, emphasizing collegiality and team-based teaching and learning. \u2022 Integrated Acting Emphasis: The new Acting for the Screen BFA emphasis is fully integrated with the filmmaking students. This intentional structure means acting in student films is a part of their training, fostering essential on-set collaboration between filmmakers and actors. We seek individuals with a passion for teaching and the ability to mentor and inspire students in a dynamic learning environment. If you\u2019re ready to inspire the next generation of media makers and enrich an inclusive academic community, we want to hear from you! This is an ongoing posting for a lecturer pool. There is not a specific recruitment timeframe or hiring timeline. There may or may not be a current need for lecturers in this area. As needs arise, applications in the pool will be reviewed and candidates contacted for interview. The posting will remain open for a maximum of six (6) months. Lecturer appointments are at-will and teaching assignments are determined on a semester by semester basis. Teaching assignments may fluctuate and are contingent upon the schedule of courses offered each term. Lecturer of Acting What you will do: 100% Teaching As a Lecturer, your primary focus will be on inspiring and training the next cohort of filmmakers with practical, hands-on experience. You\u2019ll guide students through real-world projects, helping them develop essential technical and artistic skills. You\u2019ll teach acting and performance related courses, mentor aspiring professionals, and contribute to shaping a program known for its collegiality, creative innovation, and commitment to student growth. Teaching 100% \u2022 Teaching Load: You will teach one or two classes per semester (3-6 credit hours) \u2022 Instruction: Your focus will include acting and performance for film and television related courses (acting, directing, movement, and/or voice). Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. \u2022 Degree/Experience: MFA or BA in Acting \u2022 Expertise: 3 years of experience in acting or directing for the screen at the professional level. \u2022 Teaching: 2 years of experience teaching acting for the screen (high school level, college level, or community based productions). Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) \u2022 Degree/Experience: MFA \u2022 Expertise: More than 3 years of experience acting or directing for the screen at the professional level. Demonstrated mastery of professional vocal or physical pedagogies. \u2022 Teaching: Experience teaching acting for the screen at the college level. \u2022 Certifications: Voice (Linklater, Fitzmaurice, etc.) and/or Movement (Alexander, Laban, Chekhov, Lecoq, Sensory Training, etc.) Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge \u2022 Extensive knowledge and experience in acting for film and television. Skills \u2022 Observable Activities: o Ability to bridge traditional conservatory training with film-specific applications. o Ability to mentor and inspire students in a dynamic learning environment. o Ability to contribute to a collaborative faculty culture. o The capacity to help shape the future of a growing program. Abilities \u2022 Recurring Patterns: o Striving (The 'Why'): A passion for teaching and a desire to mentor and inspire students. o Thinking (The 'How'): The ability to weigh alternatives and apply creative and technical expertise to a teaching role. o Relating (The 'Who'): The capacity to work effectively with colleagues and students in a collaborative environment. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,371.19 per 3 credit course. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. This position is not eligible for benefits. Application Deadline This is an ongoing posting for a lecturer pool. There is not a specific recruitment timeframe or hiring timeline. There may or may not be a current need for lecturers in this area. As needs arise, applications in the pool will be reviewed and candidates contacted for interview. The posting will remain open for a maximum of six (6) months. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: \u2022 A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. \u2022 Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Questions should be directed to David Liban, david.liban@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=39923&lang=en": {"title": "Lecturer of Screenwriting", "description": "Posted Date: May 12, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CAM-Film & Television Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer of Screenwriting FTE: .225 per 3 credit course Salary Range: $5,371.19 per 3 credit course Position #00612169 \u2013 Requisition #39923 About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * At the College of Arts & Media (CAM), we empower a diverse community of makers, scholars, and innovators to thrive in the rapidly evolving creative industries. Through a dynamic blend of critical inquiry, creative exploration, and real-world engagement, CAM prepares students for lives filled with opportunity, meaning, and purpose. Rooted in community and driven by a spirit of intellectual and artistic freedom, CAM embraces risk-takers, visionaries, and cultural disruptors by providing access to cutting-edge technology, global perspectives, and a nurturing environment where bold ideas flourish. CAM offers top-ranked degrees and programs in Film & Television, Media Forensics, Music & Entertainment, and Visual Arts. The Film & Television department within the College of Arts & Media invites dynamic educators and creative professionals to apply to join our collaborative faculty team as a part-time Lecturer specializing in Screenwriting. This is an opportunity to inspire and empower tomorrow\u2019s filmmakers in the heart of Denver, working alongside innovative peers in a thriving urban arts scene. Why join CU Denver CAM? \u2022 Be part of a forward-looking, supportive faculty committed to excellence and innovation. \u2022 Enjoy a culture that values your unique artistic and academic contributions. \u2022 Teach within a nationally recognized program. \u2022 Shape a vibrant program positioned at the crossroads of professional opportunity and creative experimentation, in a city alive with storytelling and artistic energy. The Film & Television program offers a Bachelor of Fine Arts (BFA) in Film and Television. This BFA emphasis provides intensive, practical training that requires successful completion of numerous film/TV projects, ranging from fiction to documentary. The emphasis is designed for students to progress through the semesters as a cohort. Undergraduates will work on their own projects and assist with numerous group projects. Students graduate with both a theoretical and historical perspective, as well as hands-on experience in film and television production. This program prepares students to begin their careers at entry-level positions in the film or television industry, start their personal creative journey, or continue their studies in a graduate program. We believe in the power of transformative education, hands-on learning, and creative exploration. Our BFA program cultivates storytellers with a strong technical foundation and artistic vision, preparing graduates for immediate impact in the film, television, and media industries. \u2022 Accolades: For the fourth consecutive year, CU Denver's Film & Television program has been named to MovieMaker Magazine's Top 30 Best Film Schools list. We are recognized for our hands-on, cohort-based curriculum, affordability, and strong industry connections. \u2022 Career Pathways & Networking: Graduates are successful across multiple areas, including opportunities in Hollywood, independent film, commercial film, and post-production studios. \u2022 Hands-on from Day One: The curriculum is sequence-based, allowing students to build on skillsets developed throughout their college career. \u2022 Students building a High-Volume Portfolio: The curriculum is known for its rigor, as students often complete 20+ films/exercises on their portfolios by graduation. This indicates a highly engaged and active student body. \u2022 Access to Professional Gear: The program's \"film cage\" provides students with access to industry-standard, professional-grade cameras, sound, lighting, and grip equipment. \u2022 Only BFA Production Program in the Region: CU Denver is the only school in the region offering a BFA in production. \u2022 Collaborative Cohort Culture: The program is built on a cohort-style curriculum in which students build strong bonds by working on each other's film sets, emphasizing collegiality and team-based teaching and learning. \u2022 Integrated Acting Emphasis: The new Acting for the Screen BFA emphasis is fully integrated with the filmmaking students. This intentional structure means acting in student films is a part of their training, fostering essential on-set collaboration between filmmakers and actors. We seek individuals with a passion for teaching and the ability to mentor and inspire students in a dynamic learning environment. If you\u2019re ready to inspire the next generation of media makers and enrich an inclusive academic community, we want to hear from you! This is an ongoing posting for a lecturer pool. There is not a specific recruitment timeframe or hiring timeline. There may or may not be a current need for lecturers in this area. As needs arise, applications in the pool will be reviewed and candidates contacted for interview. The posting will remain open for a maximum of six (6) months. Lecturer appointments are at-will and teaching assignments are determined on a semester by semester basis. Teaching assignments may fluctuate and are contingent upon the schedule of courses offered each term. Lecturer of Screenwriting What you will do: 100% Teaching As a Lecturer, your primary focus will be on inspiring and training the next cohort of filmmakers with practical, hands-on experience. You\u2019ll guide students through real-world projects, helping them develop essential technical and artistic skills. You\u2019ll teach screenwriting courses, mentor aspiring professionals, and contribute to shaping a program known for its collegiality, creative innovation, and commitment to student growth. Teaching 100% \u2022 Teaching Load: You will teach one or two classes per semester (3-6 credit hours) \u2022 Instruction: Your focus will include screenwriting for fiction, non-fiction, and/or episodic television courses. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. \u2022 Degree/Experience: MFA or BA \u2022 Expertise: 3 years of experience in screenwriting at the professional level. \u2022 Teaching: 2 years of experience teaching screenwriting. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) \u2022 Degree/Experience: MFA \u2022 Expertise: More than 3 years of experience in screenwriting at the professional level. \u2022 Teaching: Experience teaching screenwriting at the college level. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge \u2022 Extensive knowledge and experience in screenwriting for fiction, non-fiction, and/or episodic television. Skills \u2022 Observable Activities: o Ability to mentor and inspire students in a dynamic learning environment. o Ability to contribute to a collaborative faculty culture. o The capacity to help shape the future of a growing program. Abilities \u2022 Recurring Patterns: o Striving (The 'Why'): A passion for teaching and a desire to mentor and inspire students. o Thinking (The 'How'): The ability to weigh alternatives and apply creative and technical expertise to a teaching role. o Relating (The 'Who'): The capacity to work effectively with colleagues and students in a collaborative environment. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,371.19 per 3 credit course. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. This position is not eligible for benefits. Application Deadline This is an ongoing posting for a lecturer pool. There is not a specific recruitment timeframe or hiring timeline. There may or may not be a current need for lecturers in this area. As needs arise, applications in the pool will be reviewed and candidates contacted for interview. The posting will remain open for a maximum of six (6) months. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: \u2022 A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. \u2022 Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Questions should be directed to David Liban, david.liban@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=39736&lang=en": {"title": "Lecturer", "description": "Posted Date: Apr 24, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CEDC-Electrical Engineering Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer FTE: Part-time Salary Range: $5825.00 per 3-credit course. $2903.60 per 1-credit lab. Position #00619467 \u2013 Requisition #39736 About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top ranked bachelors, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The University of Colorado Denver seeks individuals with demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. We value the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty and staff of diverse backgrounds. This posting establishes a pool of candidates to fill temporary, non-tenure track lecturer positions to teach one or more undergraduate level courses as needed in the Department of Electrical Engineering on a part-time semester-by-semester basis for AY26/27. Courses will vary from term to term. This position is paid on a per-course basis. Assignments are dependent upon student enrollments and are paid on a per course basis. There are no travel and relocation expenses available. Lecturer What you will do: \u2022 Teach one to three classes as assigned per term. \u2022 Prepare for each class session and deliver balanced, rigorous lessons via Canvas and Zoom in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes. \u2022 Hold weekly office hours as appropriate per course allocation. \u2022 Assess student progress according to curricular objectives and adhere to program policies. \u2022 Record attendance and grades online and be accessible for communication with students. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. \u2022 A Master of Science degree in electrical engineering or in a related field is required for teaching undergraduate level courses. \u2022 A PhD degree in electrical engineering or related fields is required for teaching graduate level courses. \u2022 A Bachelor of Science degree in Engineering or a related field is required to teach undergraduate labs. Substitution: \u2022 A combination of a bachelor's degree and 5 years of directly related experience may be substituted for the master's degree. \u2022 A combination of a master's degree and 5 years of related experience may be substituted for the PhD. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) \u2022 Candidates with teaching experience in the higher education environment are preferred. \u2022 Candidates with research or industrial experience in a related discipline are preferred. \u2022 Candidates residing within proximity to campus are preferred. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities \u2022 Ability to integrate academic knowledge and current field practices into the classroom. \u2022 Ability to clearly explain complex concepts. \u2022 Ability to maintain an engaging, productive classroom with a diverse range of students. \u2022 Ability to effectively use technology in the classroom. Conditions of Employment \u2022 Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. \u2022 Most courses require presence on campus at least twice a week. \u2022 The position may involve in-person or hybrid work depending on the specific course(s) being taught. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements \u2022 This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. \u2022 This position may be performed in a hybrid environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. \u2022 The ability to lecture for full class periods, utilize white boards or similar communication methods, and ability to oversee hands-on activities. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5825.00 per 3-credit course. $2903.60 per 1-credit lab. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline \u2022 Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to six (6) months from the posting date. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the six\u2011month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: \u2022 A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications \u2022 A current CV/resume \u2022 List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Mark Golkowski, mark.golkowski@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=39735&lang=en": {"title": "Lecturer", "description": "Posted Date: Apr 24, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CEDC-Dean of Engineering Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer FTE: Part-time Salary Range: $5825.00 - $6500 per 3-credit course Position #00782785 \u2013 Requisition #39735 About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The University of Colorado Denver, College of Engineering, Design and Computing, seeks individuals with demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. We value the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty and staff of diverse backgrounds. This posting establishes a pool of candidates to fill temporary, non-tenure track lecturer positions to teach one or more undergraduate level courses as needed in the following departments: \u2022 College of Engineering, Design and Computing Dean\u2019s Office. \u2022 Department of Biomedical Engineering. \u2022 Department of Civil Engineering and Construction. \u2022 Department of Mechanical Engineering. Positions are part-time semester-by-semester basis for AY26/27. Courses will vary from term to term and may include required courses, technical electives or labs. Assignments are dependent upon student enrollments and are paid on a per course basis. There are no travel and relocation expenses available. Lecturer What you will do: \u2022 Teach one to three classes as assigned per term. \u2022 Prepare for each class session and deliver balanced, rigorous lessons via Canvas and Zoom in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes. \u2022 Hold weekly office hours as appropriate per course allocation. \u2022 Assess student progress according to curricular objectives and adhere to program policies. \u2022 Record attendance and grades online and be accessible for communication with students. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. \u2022 A Master of Science in Engineering or a related field is required for teaching undergraduate level courses. A combination of a Bachelor\u2019s degree. \u2022 A PhD in Engineering or a related field is required for teaching graduate level courses. \u2022 A Bachelor of Science degree in Engineering or a related field is required to teach undergraduate labs. Substitution: \u2022 A combination of a bachelor's degree and 5 years of directly related experience may be substituted for the master's degree. \u2022 A combination of a master's degree and 5 years of related experience may be substituted for the PhD. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) \u2022 Candidates with teaching experience in the higher education environment are preferred. \u2022 Candidates with research or industrial experience in a related discipline are preferred. \u2022 A professional engineering license is preferred. \u2022 Candidates residing within proximity to campus are preferred. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities \u2022 Ability to integrate academic knowledge and current field practices into the classroom. \u2022 Ability to clearly explain complex concepts. \u2022 Ability to maintain an engaging, productive classroom with a diverse range of students. \u2022 Ability to effectively use technology in the classroom. Conditions of Employment \u2022 Occasional work during the evening may be required. \u2022 Most courses require presence on campus at least twice a week. \u2022 The position may involve in-person or hybrid work depending on the specific course(s) being taught. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements \u2022 This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. \u2022 This position may be performed in a hybrid environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. \u2022 The ability to lecture for full class periods, utilize white boards or similar communication methods, and ability to oversee hands-on activities. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5825.00 - $6500.00 per semester per 3-credit course. $2903.60 per semester per 1-credit lab. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline \u2022 Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to six (6) months from the posting date. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the six\u2011month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: \u2022 A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. \u2022 Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). \u2022 List of Three professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to Amy.Fauver@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=39732&lang=en": {"title": "Lecturer", "description": "Posted Date: Apr 24, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CEDC-Computer SC & Engineering Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer FTE: Part-time Salary Range: $6500 - $7500 per 3 credit course; $3250 per 1 credit lab. Position #00605249 \u2013 Requisition #39732 About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top ranked bachelors, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The University of Colorado Denver seeks individuals with demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. We value the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty and staff of diverse backgrounds. This posting establishes a pool of candidates to fill non-tenure track lecturer positions to teach one or more undergraduate or graduate level course(s) as needed in the Computer Science and Engineering Department on a part-time semester-by-semester basis for AY26/27. Courses will vary from term to term. This position is paid on a per-course basis. Assignments are dependent upon student enrollments. The department is interested in experienced software engineering professionals to teach undergraduate security courses, undergraduate level discrete structures and graduate level software engineering courses. There are no travel and relocation expenses available. Lecturer What you will do: \u2022 Teach one to three classes as assigned per term. \u2022 Prepare for each class session and deliver balanced, rigorous lessons via Canvas and Zoom in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes. \u2022 Hold weekly office hours as appropriate per course allocation. \u2022 Assess student progress according to curricular objectives and adhere to program policies. \u2022 Record attendance and grades online and be accessible for communication with students. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. \u2022 A Master of Science degree in computer science or a related field is required for teaching undergraduate level courses. A combination of a bachelor's degree and 5 years of directly related experience may be substituted for the master's degree. \u2022 A PhD degree in computer science or related fields is required for teaching graduate level courses. A combination of a master's degree and 5 years of related experience may be substituted for the PhD. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) \u2022 Candidates with teaching experience in the higher education environment are preferred. \u2022 Candidates with research or industrial experience in a related discipline are preferred. \u2022 Candidates residing within proximity to campus are preferred. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities \u2022 Ability to integrate academic knowledge and current field practices into the classroom. \u2022 Ability to clearly explain complex concepts. \u2022 Ability to maintain an engaging, productive classroom with a diverse range of students. \u2022 Ability to effectively use technology in the classroom. Conditions of Employment \u2022 This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. \u2022 Occasional work during the evening may be required. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements \u2022 This position may be performed in a hybrid environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. \u2022 The ability to lecture for full class periods, utilize white boards or similar communication methods, and ability to oversee hands-on activities. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu. Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $6500 - $7500 per 3 credit course; $3250 per 1 credit lab. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline This is an open continuous position for AY26/27. Once you apply you will be placed on our candidate inventory list and will continuously be considered for positions as vacancies become available. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: \u2022 A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications \u2022 A current CV/resume \u2022 List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Kelly Konrad at Kelly.p.konrad@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=39309&lang=en": {"title": "Associate Director, CFDA", "description": "Posted Date: Mar 16, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: AVCASA-FAUE FacAffrs/UG Enrich Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Associate Director Working Title: Associate Director CFDA FTE: Part-time (0.5 FTE) Salary: $10,000 stipend plus course buy-outs Position #00781410 \u2013 Requisition #39309 About the University of Colorado - Denver The University of Colorado Denver is the state\u2019s premier public urban research university and equity-serving institution. Globally connected and locally invested, CU Denver partners with future-focused learners and communities to design accessible, relevant, transformative educational experiences for every stage of life and career. Across seven schools and colleges in the heart of downtown Denver, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges through break through innovations and impactful research, and creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. For more information, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Center for Faculty Development & Advancement (CFDA) is seeking a visionary Associate Director (AD) who is passionate about empowering faculty and shaping the future of academic life at CU Denver. This is an exciting opportunity for a campus leader who thrives on building community, designing innovative development experiences, and helping colleagues unleash their full potential. In this role, you will directly influence the faculty experience\u2014strengthening pathways for growth, fostering belonging, and creating the kind of campus environment where faculty excel, connect, and thrive. Working closely with the Director, the AD will co-create impactful initiatives for faculty across the Denver campus. Key areas of focus include developing tailored mentorship programs, building professional learning\u2014especially for IRC faculty\u2014and supporting the Center\u2019s core programming. This position may also lead interactive workshops (virtual and in person), host topic-based faculty communities, assist faculty with career and dossier development, and engage in a wide range of activities that foster growth, belonging, and excellence. In partnership with the Director, the AD will lead, design, and deliver programs that support faculty of all ranks and disciplines. Associate Director, CFDA What you will do: \u2022 Collaborating with the Director to plan strategic programming, services, and initiatives, with particular attention to IRC faculty\u2019s career advancement and professional development needs. \u2022 Designing and facilitating mentorship programs (individual, peer, group) for faculty at all ranks as well as developing programs to support mentors for inclusive and effective mentoring practices. \u2022 Supporting faculty as they prepare for rank advancement. \u2022 Engaging across campus to elevate CFDA\u2019s visibility and strengthen partnerships. \u2022 Leading innovative efforts to strengthen community, belonging, and engagement among faculty. \u2022 Work with the Director to manage the CFDA grant programs. \u2022 Identifying opportunities for improved practices and implementing solutions that strengthen departmental and campus-wide faculty development. \u2022 Assessing faculty needs using research-informed data collection methods. \u2022 Working with faculty groups and academic leaders to design tailored professional development programs for faculty. \u2022 Consulting with faculty on professional, scholarly, and career development goals. \u2022 Performing additional duties as assigned. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. \u2022 Current rostered University of Colorado Denver faculty member. \u2022 Terminal degree in any discipline from an accredited institution. \u2022 At least three (3) years of rostered faculty experience at CU Denver. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) \u2022 Experience designing and delivering professional learning opportunities. \u2022 Expertise in evidence-based and innovative approaches to faculty development. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities \u2022 Ability to build strong, collaborative relationships across all campus levels. \u2022 Strong knowledge of CU Denver faculty policies and practices. \u2022 Excellent collaboration, communication, and facilitation skills. \u2022 Strategic, innovative thinker responsive to faculty needs. \u2022 Demonstrated commitment to campus engagement, equity, and inclusion. \u2022 Knowledge of best practices in faculty mentoring and development. \u2022 Strong understanding of promotion and/or tenure processes. \u2022 Leadership experience and the ability to launch new initiatives and solve problems creatively and efficiently. \u2022 Demonstrated mentoring skills and enthusiasm for supporting others\u2019 growth. \u2022 Ability to write, present, lead discussions, and provide one-on-one consultations effectively. \u2022 Ability to incorporate faculty well-being and community-building principles into programs. \u2022 Strong organization skills, with the ability to prioritize and manage multiple projects independently and collaboratively. Conditions of Employment \u2022 This 9-month role is approximately a 0.5 FTE appointment. Faculty will continue their duties within their program area at 0.5 FTE. The appointment will begin in August 2026 running through May 2027. The expected term is three (3) years, each year renewal will be based on successful performance of the job duties in the pervious year. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements \u2022 The ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The position will include a $10,000 stipend and expected to approximate a .5 FTE. For faculty with a teaching load of 5 courses or less per year, there are 2 course buyouts per academic year, for faculty with a teaching load of more than 5 courses per year, there are 3 course buyouts per academic year. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline \u2022 Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by April 6, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: \u2022 A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. \u2022 Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). \u2022 Three professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to Bryn Harris, Director of the CFDA, bryn.harris@ucdenver.edu Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=38598&lang=en": {"title": "Lecturer", "description": "Posted Date: Jan 14, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CLAS-Mathematics Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title : Lecturer FTE: Part Time Salary Range: The hiring rate (or budgeted rate) for this position has been established at $1,667 per credit hour (undergraduate level) or $1,808 per credit hour (graduate level). Position # 00763623 \u2013 Requisition # 38598 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top ranked bachelors, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Department of Mathematical and Statistical Sciences is housed on the Auraria campus in the heart of Denver's commercial, cultural, and recreational district. Its location in downtown Denver attracts a diverse population, comprising both traditional and non-traditional students. This diversity is enriched by our commitment to a philosophy of inclusion, embedded in all aspects of campus life from its community members, curriculum, research and community service, allowing for the creation of a learning environment that welcomes, embraces, sustains and celebrates the unique and shared experiences of faculty, staff, and students. This posting is a pool for continuous faculty hires. The Department of Mathematical & Statistical Sciences has an opening for a temporary, non-tenure track, part-time lecturer to teach mathematics and statistics courses. The appointment is for one semester, with the possibility of renewal for future semesters. Lecturer What you will do: Design and Deliver courses. Deliver lectures, seminars, and tutorials. Design and deliver assessments, such as exams, assignments, and reports. Collaborating with other lecturers, faculty and course coordinators to improve teaching methods and expand knowledge base. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master\u2019s degree A Master\u2019s degree in mathematical sciences from an accredited university; OR A master\u2019s degree in any area and 18 credit hours of graduate-level course work in mathematical sciences. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) A record of successful teaching at the secondary or college level. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to communicate Effectively, both in Writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with other department employees. Demonstrated commitment and leadership ability to teach a diverse student body. Ability to develop a clear syllabus outlining learning outcomes, policies, and assessments for the class. Commitment to applying rules in a consistent manner Ability to present in a classroom in an engaging way. Ability to work effectively with students on a 1-to-1 basis. Ability to provide clear feedback on student written work. Flexibility and empathy in adapting to student circumstances. Conditions of Employment Most courses offered by the department are delivered in person, and the successful candidate will be required to teach on campus. While there may be occasional opportunities to teach hybrid or online courses, these are dependent on departmental course availability and scheduling needs. Remote or hybrid teaching is not guaranteed and will be determined by the assigned course mode. Candidates should be prepared for a primarily in-person teaching role. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements The ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The hiring rate (or budgeted rate) for this position has been established at $1,667 per credit hour (undergraduate level) or $1,808 per credit hour (graduate level).The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Review of applications will begin in early 2026 and this position will remain open until filled for the 2026 - 2027 semester / academic year. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Three professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Statement of teaching philosophy Unofficial transcript(s) Questions should be directed to Stephen Hartke, Stephen.Hartke@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41358&lang=en": {"title": "Senior Production Support Professional", "description": "Closing Date: 10/22/2026 Posted Date: Oct 15, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: University InformationServices Schedule: Full-time Join Our Team and Make a Difference in Higher Education! At the System Administration office at the University of Colorado, we are dedicated to building a workplace where everyone feels valued, supported, and empowered to thrive. Our office is committed to fostering a culture where employees find community, a sense of belonging, and the opportunity to contribute meaningfully to our mission and purpose. By joining our team, you\u2019ll have a direct impact on shaping the future of higher education. In addition to the Office of the Board of Regents, the University of Colorado\u2019s system administration includes 19 units that provide essential services to CU\u2019s campuses in Aurora, Boulder, Colorado Springs, and Denver, as well as the Office of the President. While not a part of any one campus, we are proud to serve in the centralized office for the University system. Together, we ensure CU continues to deliver outstanding education, groundbreaking research, and valuable service to our communities. We believe in creating an environment where the unique experiences and perspectives of everyone are embraced, enriching the work we do and the strategic outcomes we pursue. If you\u2019re passionate about making a difference, contributing to a dynamic team, and supporting a mission that matters, we encourage you to apply and be part of our journey. Learn more about CU System Administration . Position Summary: University Information Systems (UIS) provides technical services and enterprise applications to the University of Colorado campuses and the Office of the President. UIS is committed to excellence in customer service and technical expertise. Through the development of enterprise applications, UIS supports the University as a whole with systems used by students, faculty, human resources employees, finance employees, and others. The Sr Production Support Professional assists in the management and oversight of all batch processing for the University of Colorado systems and applications. This position serves as a technical professional with the ability to understand IT processes, troubleshoot, test, create technical documentation, and assist university stakeholders with any inquiries that the team may receive. This position will provide support to Production Support Professionals through issue resolution. This position is heavily involved in scripting and automation to meet sophisticated customer requirements more efficiently. The Sr Production Support Professional will need to have a solid basis of IT knowledge and the ability to work on an on-call schedule. This position is Essential Services. Positions falling into Essential Services are required to work their normal hours even when the office is closed during a normal or holiday week. This position reports to the Assistant Director of Production Services and is exempt from the State of Colorado Classified Staff system. Where You Will Work: Applicants must be Colorado residents or able to relocate to Colorado within a month of starting employment with University of Colorado System Administration. This role is eligible to work remotely within Colorado. Please note, leadership may adjust in-office work requirements with a minimum of three months' notice before any change can be implemented. Equal Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Duties and Responsibilities: Duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Serve as a technical professional to support production batch processing: resolve daily issues, build new processes, file transfers, monitoring processing, data security, and maintaining all aspects of a production environment. Remove manual tasks by building automated processes using scripting to solve complex customer requirements. Ensure high-availability and stability of production environments. Troubleshoot sophisticated, tier-2 technical production issues. Resolve higher level issues and provide expert support to Production Support Professionals. Escalate issues as needed to Principal Production Support Professional. Work independently and directly as a team member with other Production support and other IT departments. Work closely with development teams to support their work efforts. Develop thorough documentation for systems, processes, and procedures. Follow change control processes. Enhance existing and create new processes and procedures by replacing manual tasks with automation Participate in an on-call rotation and shift work as necessary. Provide excellent customer service to internal and external customers while developing positive customer relationships. Creation and testing of automated batch processes. Migrations for all Enterprise Systems. What We Offer: Salary: The anticipated hiring range has been established at $68,150. CU System Administration takes into consideration a combination of the selected candidate\u2019s education, training and experience as it relates to the position, as well as the position\u2019s scope and complexity, internal pay equity and external market value when determining a salary level for potential new employees. Benefits: With our unparalleled range of benefits, including top-notch healthcare, comprehensive wellness programs, enriching professional development, and a dynamic work-life balance, we ensure your holistic growth and happiness. No-cost or low-cost medical & dental plan options, some inclusive of IVF assistance. Disability, Life, Vision Insurance options. Multiple retirement planning options including a mandatory 401(a) plan where CU contributes 10% of your gross pay, a 401k or 403b plan and a 457 deferred compensation plan. Pre-tax savings plans, such as Health care and Dependent care flexible spending accounts. Embrace a healthy work-life balance with ample sick and vacation leave, along with at least 12 paid holidays. This includes a dedicated week off for winter break. 6 weeks of parental leave to adjust to the joys of parenthood. A tuition benefit program for you and/or your dependents. Free RTD EcoPass and free onsite parking at our 1800 Grant Street Office. Many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Additional taxable fringe benefits may be available. For more information on benefits programs, please review our Comprehensive Benefits Guide . Access our Total Compensation Calculator to see what your total rewards could be at CU. (This position is a University Staff position) Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Please include all relevant experience in your resume to be accurately assessed against these qualifications. You must meet all minimum requirements at the time of application to be considered for this role. Bachelor\u2019s degree from an accredited institution of higher education, or equivalent professional experience (professional experience may be substituted for the educational requirement on a year-for-year basis) Three (3) years\u2019 equivalent experience in a service desk, call center, data processing center or other customer service environment Preferred Qualifications: Five (5) years\u2019 equivalent experience in production services, including: Batch experience UNIX or Linux administration Documentation for systems and processes/procedures Understanding of change control processes Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To be successful in this position a candidate will need the following: Knowledge of data processing and batch production processes Ability to design, develop, and troubleshoot complex scripts to meet specific customer requirements and automate repetitive tasks efficiently. Proficient in Linux-based servers, ensuring high availability and security. Proficient in writing complex cURL commands to interact with APIs, web services, and perform data transfers securely and efficiently. Ability to configure email scripts for efficient and reliable job scheduling and automation working with prompt sets, call objects, rule definitions, and spreadsheet parsing. Knowledge of IT policies and standard methodologies Demonstrated self-starting initiative with the ability to work with minimal guidance Ability to work independently and directly as a team member with other Production support and other IT departments. Ability to work a flexible schedule \u2013 including off hours, weekend, and holiday on-call hours Ability to prioritize work tasks and projects while meeting deadlines Ability to deliver a high level of commitment to customer service Able to articulate clearly via email and phone conversations Attention to detail Basic computer skills such as Microsoft Office Suite (Outlook, Microsoft Teams, etc.) Excellent troubleshooting and problem-solving skills How to Apply: For full consideration, please attach the following as separate documents to your application: A cover letter identifying the job specific minimum qualifications you possess and interest in the position. A resume including all relevant experience to be accurately assessed against the qualifications listed in the posting. Please ensure you check the \u201cJob Specific Attachments\u201d box next to each document on the \u201cRequired Documents\u201d page of the application for the appropriate documents to be attached. Per the Colorado Job Application Fairness Act, you are not required to provide your date of birth, dates of school attendance, or dates of graduation on your resume or cover letter. If an application requires additional materials, such as a transcript or certification, you may redact identifying information relating to your date or birth, dates of school attendance, or dates of graduation. When to Apply: For full consideration completed applications must be submitted by October 22, 2026 . Reference checking is a standard step in our hiring process. You may be asked to provide contact information, including email addresses and phone numbers, for up to five references as part of the search process for this position. *Please note: All application materials must be submitted through CU Careers; emailed materials will not be considered. * Sponsorship Statement: We are unable to sponsor applicants for work visas for this position. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The Immigration Reform and Control Act requires that a verification of employment eligibility be documented for all new employees by the end of the third day of work. The University of Colorado is committed to diversity and equality in education and employment. ADA Statement: We are committed to an inclusive and barrier-free search process. We provide accommodations for applicants requesting accommodation through the search process such as alternative formats of this posting. Individuals with disabilities in need of accommodations throughout the search process should contact the ADA Coordinator at: systemhr@cu.edu ."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41355&lang=en": {"title": "Customer Experience Specialist", "description": "Posted Date: Oct 15, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: Procurement Service Center Schedule: Full-time Join Our Team and Make a Difference in Higher Education! At the System Administration office at the University of Colorado, we are dedicated to building a workplace where everyone feels valued, supported, and empowered to thrive. Our office is committed to fostering a culture where employees find community, a sense of belonging, and the opportunity to contribute meaningfully to our mission and purpose. By joining our team, you\u2019ll have a direct impact on shaping the future of higher education. In addition to the Office of the Board of Regents, the University of Colorado\u2019s system administration includes 19 units that provide essential services to CU\u2019s campuses in Aurora, Boulder, Colorado Springs, and Denver, as well as the Office of the President. While not a part of any one campus, we are proud to serve in the centralized office for the University system. Together, we ensure CU continues to deliver outstanding education, groundbreaking research, and valuable service to our communities. We believe in creating an environment where the unique experiences and perspectives of everyone are embraced, enriching the work we do and the strategic outcomes we pursue. If you\u2019re passionate about making a difference, contributing to a dynamic team, and supporting a mission that matters, we encourage you to apply and be part of our journey. Learn more about CU System Administration . Position Summary: Do you enjoy building relationships with diverse audiences, continuously learning, and being the go-to person for your customers? If so, this position is perfect for you. This role is a part of the Procurement Service Center (PSC), which is responsible for the purchasing, payables, contracts, commercial card, strategic sourcing, sustainability, small business program, and travel for the University of Colorado\u2019s (CU) four campuses and the Office of the President. As a Customer Experience Specialist, you will provide training and support to customers needing assistance with Procurement Service Center (PSC) functions. You will be an expert in guiding customers on the use of PSC tools such as PeopleSoft, Concur, CU Marketplace, and others as they arise. Additionally, you will promote employee compliance by interpreting University policies related to procurement, commercial cards, travel, purchasing, and accounts payable. You will also constantly seek ways to improve the customer experience by offering insights into resource and training development to help customers succeed in managing PSC processes. This role is crucial to the PSC\u2019s mission of delivering excellent customer service. This position reports to the Customer Success Program Manager and is exempt from the State of Colorado Classified Staff System. Where You Will Work: Applicants must be Colorado residents or able to relocate to Colorado within a month of starting employment with University of Colorado System Administration. This role is eligible for a hybrid schedule, working some days from home and some days in the office at 1800 Grant St, Denver, CO. Please note, leadership may adjust in-office work requirements with a minimum of three months' notice before any change can be implemented. Equal Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Duties and Responsibilities: Duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Support and Service: Provides individualized training and support to employees and affiliates across all four campuses and the Office of the President on the use of various complex tools, including the Concur Travel & Expense system and CU\u2019s Marketplace e-procurement system through email, phone, video meetings, virtual office hours, and webinar training. Responds to a high volume of email and phone interactions, simultaneously throughout the day during the PSC\u2019s core operational hours of 8 a.m.-12 p.m. and 1 p.m.-5 p.m. MST. Remains up to date on PSC and University policies and provides guidance to partners and customers on their applicability Assists external suppliers by researching the status of payments, identifying resolutions for payment delay, and assisting in the supplier request and registration process Instructs internal and external customers on Procurement Service Center website resources, including navigating to policies, procedures, forms, learning resources, tax and other information Investigates issues, identifying when action is required by other resources, and escalating to appropriate stakeholders as necessary Utilize procurement tools (Concur, CU Marketplace, PeopleSoft Finance, etc.) as needed to complete basic system tasks and provide easy resolutions for campus customers Takes quick action on escalating potential issues with systems or policy when short-term customer contact trends suggest the need Interacts regularly with PSC personnel to learn and stay current on business processes, policies, and tool configuration Identifies gaps in content and creates content to support knowledge and AI chatbot functionality. Work on special projects as assigned. Knowledge Collection and Process Improvement: Self-starter that continually looks for opportunities to increase knowledge in internal PSC functions to better support customers. Develops relationships and builds trust with customers as the front line into the PSC Provides professional, accurate and timely resolution to customer inquiries Tracks and manages contacts, tasks, research, and communications using CRM and other specialized tools/software Creates content for the PSC Knowledge Base in the form of Knowledge Articles that can be utilized to accurately resolve future inquiries as it relates to PSC processes and policies. Work on special projects as assigned. What We Offer: Salary: The anticipated hiring range has been established at $56,500-$60,000. CU System Administration takes into consideration a combination of the selected candidate\u2019s education, training and experience as it relates to the position, as well as the position\u2019s scope and complexity, internal pay equity and external market value when determining a salary level for potential new employees. Benefits: With our unparalleled range of benefits, including top-notch healthcare, comprehensive wellness programs, enriching professional development, and a dynamic work-life balance, we ensure your holistic growth and happiness. No-cost or low-cost medical & dental plan options, some inclusive of IVF assistance. Disability, Life, Vision Insurance options. Multiple retirement planning options including a mandatory 401(a) plan where CU contributes 10% of your gross pay, a 401k or 403b plan and a 457 deferred compensation plan. Pre-tax savings plans, such as Health care and Dependent care flexible spending accounts. Embrace a healthy work-life balance with ample sick and vacation leave, along with at least 12 paid holidays. This includes a dedicated week off for winter break. 6 weeks of parental leave to adjust to the joys of parenthood. A tuition benefit program for you and/or your dependents. Free RTD EcoPass and free onsite parking at our 1800 Grant Street Office. Many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Additional taxable fringe benefits may be available. For more information on benefits programs, please review our Comprehensive Benefits Guide . Access our Total Compensation Calculator to see what your total rewards could be at CU. (This position is a University Staff position) Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Please include all relevant experience in your resume to be accurately assessed against these qualifications. You must meet all minimum requirements at the time of application to be considered for this role. Bachelor\u2019s degree from an accredited institution of higher education, or equivalent professional experience (professional experience may be substituted for the educational requirement on a year-for-year basis) One (1) year of professional work experience in a customer service role (e.g., inbound help desk/call center; or other customer engagement environment) Preferred Qualifications: Two (2) years of professional work experience in a customer service role supporting a business, procurement, finance, and/or educational function Experience with one or more of the following: General procurement practices Procure to pay business processes eProcurement and financial systems Salesforce Service Cloud Peoplesoft Chatbots Managing customer inquiries through Live Chat functionality Professional experience working in a higher education institution Experience using Artificial Intelligence (AI)-driven solutions in support of customers and business operations Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To be successful in this position a candidate will need the following: Impeccable customer service skills Oral, written, listening, and interpersonal skills (including the ability to facilitate interaction, communication, and teamwork between others), along with excellent comprehension skills A teaching mindset and skillset, including the ability to utilize multiple methods with one individual in order to ensure learning is received and retained Collaboration skills, including the ability to work (in-person and remotely) with others from different areas and backgrounds to reach a common goal Computer skills, including proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, along with the ability to research and implement new software/tools to advance office goals and business processes Organizational skills, with the ability to work under pressure, manage multiple concurrent/competing projects, and adapt to changing priorities while maintaining personal effectiveness and strong customer service Critical thinking skills, including the ability to identify problems, questions, and assumptions; establish significance; and develop new ideas and initiatives that improve the performance of the organization Customer service skills, including the ability to actively listen, address customer needs, defuse tense situations, and maintain an open, flexible, and friendly demeanor Ability to work independently in a highly dynamic, flexible, and fast-paced environment Ability to learn technical, policy, and procedural information quickly and to retain it well Ability to utilize AI solutions to assist or perform business operations Knowledge of AI ethics and data privacy considerations in the workplace Knowledge of natural language prompting (NLP) Ability to produce content, ideate, edit, and perform analysis How to Apply: For full consideration, please attach the following as separate documents to your application: A cover letter identifying the job specific minimum qualifications you possess and interest in the position. A resume including all relevant experience to be accurately assessed against the qualifications listed in the posting. Please ensure you check the \u201cJob Specific Attachments\u201d box next to each document on the \u201cRequired Documents\u201d page of the application for the appropriate documents to be attached. Per the Colorado Job Application Fairness Act, you are not required to provide your date of birth, dates of school attendance, or dates of graduation on your resume or cover letter. If an application requires additional materials, such as a transcript or certification, you may redact identifying information relating to your date or birth, dates of school attendance, or dates of graduation. When to Apply: For full consideration completed applications must be submitted by Tuesday, October 20th . Reference checking is a standard step in our hiring process. You may be asked to provide contact information, including email addresses and phone numbers, for up to five references as part of the search process for this position. *Please note: All application materials must be submitted through CU Careers; emailed materials will not be considered. * Sponsorship Statement: We are unable to sponsor applicants for work visas for this position. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The Immigration Reform and Control Act requires that a verification of employment eligibility be documented for all new employees by the end of the third day of work. The University of Colorado is committed to diversity and equality in education and employment. ADA Statement: We are committed to an inclusive and barrier-free search process. We provide accommodations for applicants requesting accommodation through the search process such as alternative formats of this posting. Individuals with disabilities in need of accommodations throughout the search process should contact the ADA Coordinator at: systemhr@cu.edu ."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41419&lang=en": {"title": "Lecturer", "description": "Closing Date: 01/12/2027 Posted Date: Oct 14, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CLAS-Ethnic Studies Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer FTE : part-time Salary Range: The hiring rate for this position has been established at $1,704 per credit hour for undergraduate courses per semester or $1,849 per credit hour per graduate courses per semester. Position #00653636\u2013 Requisition #41419 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * Lecturer What you will do: This posting will establish and maintain a pool of part-time lecturers with experience teaching general Ethnic Studies courses, such as the Introduction to Ethnic Studies, Indigenous Studies and courses within their area of expertise, for the Department of Ethnic Studies in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at the University of Colorado Denver. Lecturers may be asked to teach on campus or fully online. By submitting your application, you will become part of an applicant pool. Candidates hired from this pool will fill temporary, non-tenure track positions and will teach no more than two courses per semester. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50%) and will be made semester-by-semester, depending on the needs of the department and subject to budgetary approval. Therefore, this posting does not necessarily reflect a current open position. We will contact you if an opening suits your qualifications. The Downtown campus is located in the heart of the city's commercial, cultural and recreational district. Its location in downtown Denver attracts a diverse population, comprising both traditional and non-traditional students. This diversity is enriched by our commitment to a philosophy of inclusion, embedded in all aspects of campus life from its community members, curriculum, research and community service, allowing for the creation of a learning environment that welcomes, embraces, sustains and celebrates the unique and shared experiences of faculty, staff, and students. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master's degree in Ethnic Studies or related field Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor\u2019s degree on a year for year basis. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Experience teaching Ethnic Studies courses. Experience teaching online using the Canvas LMS. Conditions of Employment This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Compensation and Benefits The hiring rate for this position has been established at $1,704 per credit hour for undergraduate courses per semester or $1,849 per credit hour per graduate courses per semester. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [October 14, 2026]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three\u2011month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to Edelina Burciaga, Edelina.Burciaga@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41345&lang=en": {"title": "Assistant Professor \u2013 Criminal Justice", "description": "Closing Date: 12/31/2026 Posted Date: Oct 14, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: SPA - OTHER Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Assistant Professor Working Title: Assistant Professor \u2013 Criminal Justice FTE: Full-Time Salary Range: $76,000 - $87,000 Position #00008187\u2013 Requisition #41345 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit cudenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The University of Colorado Denver seeks individuals with demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. We value the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty and staff of diverse backgrounds. The nationally-ranked, NASPAA accredited School of Public Affairs (SPA) at the University of Colorado Denver seeks a full-time 9-month/academic year Assistant Professor for the CJ programs within SPA, starting fall of 2027. The standard teaching load is four courses over the academic year in person and online (2 in each semester). There may be additional summer teaching opportunities available as a separate contract as well. The candidate must be able to teach in our BACJ and MCJ cores, as well as some elective courses within the CJ programs. A strong research trajectory is required. The successful candidate will be expected to develop and sustain an active program of high-quality research, including actively pursuing external funding. Experience with externally funded research, including participation in or leadership of grant proposals, is highly desirable. We are seeking a very collegial scholar, who feels comfortable doing CJ research/teaching within a broader applied social science/public affairs school setting. Experience working with scholars from other related fields is a plus. Assistant Professor \u2013 Criminal Justice What you will do: Teaching: Teach courses online and in-person as needed by SPA Teach courses at both the Undergraduate and Graduate (master\u2019s) level as needed by SPA May teach cross-listed courses with Public Administration, and Public Policy programs as needed by SPA Areas of expertise and teaching areas that we are looking for could include, but are not limited to: Criminological Theory, Interpersonal or Community Violence, Courts, Victimology, Statistics and Research Methods, Data Visualization, GIS, Mixed Method Design, and Practice-Informed Analysis. Service & Leadership Contribute to the ongoing growth of the Criminal Justice program through committee service, student mentorship (formal academic advising provided by professional advisors in the School), serving as a second reader on capstone projects, and positively contributing to SPA programs Research To help us achieve our campus goal to become internationally known for our research and creative work, the successful candidate will be expected to develop and sustain a strong program of high-quality research and contribute to the overall research agenda of the School of Public Affairs. Expectations include producing peer-reviewed scholarship and actively pursuing external funding. Interest and experience in collaborative and interdisciplinary research are desirable. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. PhD in Criminal Justice, Criminology, Public Administration, Public Policy, Political Science, Public Affairs, Sociology, or a closely related field. Applicants must have teaching experience and effectiveness in Criminal Justice, Criminology, Public Affairs/Public Policy, and/or Sociology programs. A strong research trajectory. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Demonstrated ability/experience teaching online classes Success and/or experience with grant funded research Experience designing and teaching courses with a university learning management system (preferably Canvas) Ability and experience teaching at the graduate and undergraduate level. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Willingness to contribute to the holistic growth of the Criminal Justice Program Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Outstanding student service skills and a student-centered attitude Demonstrated commitment and leadership ability to advance diversity and inclusion. Conditions of Employment This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. The search committee may conduct a limited number of preliminary interviews during the ASC Annual Meeting. These interviews may be scheduled through and conducted in the ASC Employment Exchange designated interview area. Participation in conference-based interviews is optional and will not adversely affect consideration for this position. Applicants who are not attending the conference will have alternative interview opportunities available. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is eligible now and in the future for visa sponsorship. While the hiring unit is willing to pursue visa sponsorship, an offer of employment will be contingent on the candidate having a visa status that allows employment with the University as of the start date for the position or the University\u2019s petition being approved and on the candidate being able to obtain the appropriate visa status. Compensation and Benefits The starting salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established as HIRING RANGE: $76,000 - $87,000 per academic year depending on experience and other qualifications. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Monday, November 9, 2026 a 11:59:00 PM. . Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant teaching experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and specifying any experience or abilities that you meet in our preferred qualifications list. The letter should speak to your ability and/or experience teaching students across different modalities (in-person, online, hybrid, etc). Curriculum vitae / Resume List of three to five professional references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Any FCQs or student evaluations for the last 2 years, if available. Questions should be directed to: Chris Smith at chris.smith@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41374&lang=en": {"title": "Creative Technology Specialist", "description": "Closing Date: 11/13/2026 Posted Date: Oct 14, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: LIB LIBRARY Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Academic Services Intermediate Professional Working Title: Creative Technology Specialist FTE: Full time 1.0 (100%) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: $58031 - $64140 Position #00716247 \u2013 Requisition #41374 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We\u2019re the state\u2019s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top ranked bachelors, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners\u2014at any stage of their life and career\u2014for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state\u2019s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Creative Technology Specialist will support the work of the Innovation Garage and Digital Media Studio, two of the Auraria Library\u2019s dynamic service points. This position works directly with students, faculty, and staff of the Auraria Campus across a variety of areas including graphic design, large format printing, 3D printing, and related makerspace tools, photo and video cameras, and audio equipment. This position provides consulting services in professional resources and tools related to these areas. As one of the primary service providers for the Innovation Garage and Digital Media Studio, the Creative Technology Specialist oversees daily operations, ensuring the consistent application of policies and procedures, supporting the work of Access and User Services colleagues, staff, and student employees. Creative Technology Specialist What you will do: I nnovation Garage Duties Provides expert consulting services in large format printing, vinyl cutting, 3D printing, image digitization, maker tools and other creative technologies. Monitoring email inquiries, booking calendars, assisting users, and maintaining equipment. Maintains a safe and comfortable environment for creative technology service users, thus creating a positive user experience. Provides users with tools and services to bring their ideas to life. Works across the Library to promote understanding and use of Creative Technology Services. Provides formal and informal technology training to library staff and campus faculty, staff, and students. Performs inventory, monitoring, and ordering supplies as needed. Stays current with creative and maker trends through continuing education, research, and environmental scans. Evaluates creative hardware and software and makes upgrade recommendations as part of continual service improvement. Documents and refines workflows and other standard operating procedures. Employs problem-solving and critical thinking skills to arrive at creative solutions to complex issues. Ensures Innovation Garage website content is up to date. Collects, analyzes, and applies data to inform decision-making. Provide recommendations for equipment purchases and repairs. Contributes to a positive working environment. Digital Media Studio Duties Maintains extensive knowledge of and ability to operate DMS photography, video, and audio equipment and related software. Monitoring email inquiries, booking calendar, assisting users, and maintaining equipment. Fulfills appointments by setting up equipment properly and on time, assisting users, maintaining equipment, and creating a positive user experience. Ensures Digital Media Studio website content is up to date. Assists in training other staff on DMS operations and equipment use as needed. Provides informed recommendations for equipment purchases and repairs. Incorporates critical research into DMS practices and services. Additional duties Member of Library committees and task forces as needed. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Bachelor's degree in related discipline, such as digital design or film production. 1+ years of professional experience in digital media, educational/creative technology, or related fields. Customer service experience. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical or professional experience may be substituted for the bachelor\u2019s degree on a year-for-year basis. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Experience supervising a service point supporting student success in a higher education setting. Experience creating and maintaining workflow documentation. Experience in a library or higher education environment. Supervisory experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Advanced proficiency with Adobe Creative Cloud or related products. Advanced knowledge of and experience working with image and video projects. Advanced knowledge of a variety of makerspace services and equipment. Inventory monitoring experience. Ability to solve technology problems quickly and creatively. Effective learning and presentation skills. Ability to work independently and in team settings. Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. Experience with Microsoft Office products including Excel, Word, and Outlook. Conditions of Employment Work Hours: Monday-Friday; 8:00am \u2013 5:00pm. Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position is primarily in person to support users, equipment, and daily operations, with limited hybrid work available based on the needs of the library. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $58,031 - $64,140. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Nov 13, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications. A current CV/resume. List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to Peyton Hertz, at PEYTON.HERTZ@UCDENVER.EDU . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."}}, "rows": {"https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41375&lang=en": {"school_id": 168, "posting_url": "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41375&lang=en", "job_title_in_post": "Executive Assistant", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor; Full_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "10/26/2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41348&lang=en": {"school_id": 168, "posting_url": "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41348&lang=en", "job_title_in_post": "Treasury Manager", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "10/17/2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=38857&lang=en": {"school_id": 168, "posting_url": "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=38857&lang=en", "job_title_in_post": "Pipe Mechanical Trades - II Facilities Maintenance Technician Lead (Housing)", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "10/24/2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41337&lang=en": {"school_id": 168, "posting_url": "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41337&lang=en", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Budget Director", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor; Full_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "11/01/2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41323&lang=en": {"school_id": 168, "posting_url": "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41323&lang=en", "job_title_in_post": "Associate Vice Chancellor for Student Affairs", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Division of Strategic Enrollment and Student Success", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "12/01/2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41344&lang=en": {"school_id": 168, "posting_url": "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41344&lang=en", "job_title_in_post": "Faculty Fellow for Lecturer Success", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "Center for Faculty Development & Advancement", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "10/28/2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41335&lang=en": {"school_id": 168, "posting_url": "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41335&lang=en", "job_title_in_post": "Professor, Director of Construction", "position_type": "Full_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "College of Engineering, Design and Computing", "area_key_words": "Construction; Associate Professor-track appointment", "deadline_of_application": "12/31/2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41299&lang=en": {"school_id": 168, "posting_url": "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41299&lang=en", "job_title_in_post": "Director of Development SEHD", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "School of Education & Human Development", "area_key_words": "Development SEHD; Prospect; Strategy", "deadline_of_application": "11/15/2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41297&lang=en": {"school_id": 168, "posting_url": "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41297&lang=en", "job_title_in_post": "Director of Development - CAM", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "College of Arts & Media", "area_key_words": "Development; Prospect; Strategy", "deadline_of_application": "11/15/2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41295&lang=en": {"school_id": 168, "posting_url": "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41295&lang=en", "job_title_in_post": "Lecturer - Illustration", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "College of Arts & Media", "area_key_words": "Illustration", "deadline_of_application": "11/01/2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41231&lang=en": {"school_id": 168, "posting_url": "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41231&lang=en", "job_title_in_post": "Midcareer Faculty Success Fellow", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor; Full_Professor", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "Center for Faculty Development and Advancement", "area_key_words": "Midcareer", "deadline_of_application